[{"sha":"a5ec6dd0fec66ad321c1cc0f5e2f990c9026e03f","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGE1ZWM2ZGQwZmVjNjZhZDMyMWMxY2MwZjVlMmY5OTBjOTAyNmUwM2Y","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-15T23:10:43Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-15T23:10:43Z"},"message":"feat(code): prompt before updating an out-of-date dcode install (#3995)\n\nThe `deepagents-code` install script now prompts before updating an\nout-of-date install in interactive shells (and skips work when already\nup to date); set `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_YES=1` to auto-accept.\n\n---\n\nThe `deepagents-code` installer (`scripts/install.sh`) ran `uv tool\ninstall -U` unconditionally, silently pulling the latest version on\nevery run. It now probes PyPI for the latest release so it can be\ndeliberate about updates: it exits early when already up to date, and\nfor an existing default-path install it prompts before upgrading in an\ninteractive shell. Piped/non-interactive runs with no usable TTY still\nupgrade automatically (preserving prior behavior), and\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_YES=1` accepts the update without prompting. Pinned\nversions (`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_VERSION`) and pre-release strategies\n(`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_PRERELEASE`) express explicit intent and install\ndirectly without a prompt.\n\nA `can_prompt` helper verifies `/dev/tty` is actually openable, since\n`IS_INTERACTIVE` only access-checks it and can be wrong under\ncron/systemd/CI.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"a03d7f2ea6d34c97e77bfb77520421ee1af89f48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a03d7f2ea6d34c97e77bfb77520421ee1af89f48"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/a5ec6dd0fec66ad321c1cc0f5e2f990c9026e03f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMIZzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6FgQAH9Po+wXLZ5nERXkZMnZNKLG\ncM58+9uJag9+6AAhuVKyiVEPha5wpPqwakJdy9FC/I7d44vAygofy4gsSLNi7LB8\nl6yNg5UsNynehKjbyhQ09710V9EBHhCnwpOGOWkWQGUUt9V+hQweEER3/I6zXQ3m\n2G7vnDvN8e5+kzdUPc1yb5CsUF2NDA0QODA5pHV59fv5qmSRfQS5T1L+HhNTh22K\nUHD0Pl0afAuPEqwBrFvaE65IIjDywJsHYTzW/SNYIhZP+EX79JTAc5mCVVvDncbu\n1dvq2QeiRNB8dwHroJgGt6nUOBU3pLs7+pOkbzaDMzxvNI32mSYQJkUuLZA3AqpV\nMhDSecLMpxVx/ZgTl07pjdhFFk+iFYRSpyLpUl3Sk+MBJr1/z/LndK+7a+948jqt\nI9Qcdf0+OpJeFI7OfmsXpNRBR+5dQvdBGbfmdrwkXt4ET5An+EeRYgD25BbsLgyQ\nKNqMjh9Mvx7UcGjTmTYO05CRYEi5TcaroEuWXHQ38PrmEJts3R5YswJLJf1Rgwxu\nIXPuqgOmTYwPF5FqdhQo1HzWAtoh0a226ueVp844rPmKxPkClg2ig/8oAjz4XVhS\npc9JuFeBVbqKq7mFPpmCueh0Mjev6YkwBUJ+5y+wKlZJm3OmzrJr6ItGAaM1N43j\nXHf33wbT7JiAoalsw+Qj\n=AekO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a03d7f2ea6d34c97e77bfb77520421ee1af89f48\nparent 7ff6e2224d7ba8462c073333da937c35831f9b34\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781565043 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781565043 -0400\n\nfeat(code): prompt before updating an out-of-date dcode install (#3995)\n\nThe `deepagents-code` install script now prompts before updating an\nout-of-date install in interactive shells (and skips work when already\nup to date); set `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_YES=1` to auto-accept.\n\n---\n\nThe `deepagents-code` installer (`scripts/install.sh`) ran `uv tool\ninstall -U` unconditionally, silently pulling the latest version on\nevery run. It now probes PyPI for the latest release so it can be\ndeliberate about updates: it exits early when already up to date, and\nfor an existing default-path install it prompts before upgrading in an\ninteractive shell. Piped/non-interactive runs with no usable TTY still\nupgrade automatically (preserving prior behavior), and\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_YES=1` accepts the update without prompting. Pinned\nversions (`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_VERSION`) and pre-release strategies\n(`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_PRERELEASE`) express explicit intent and install\ndirectly without a prompt.\n\nA `can_prompt` helper verifies `/dev/tty` is actually openable, since\n`IS_INTERACTIVE` only access-checks it and can be wrong under\ncron/systemd/CI.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-15T23:10:43Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a5ec6dd0fec66ad321c1cc0f5e2f990c9026e03f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a5ec6dd0fec66ad321c1cc0f5e2f990c9026e03f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a5ec6dd0fec66ad321c1cc0f5e2f990c9026e03f/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7ff6e2224d7ba8462c073333da937c35831f9b34","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7ff6e2224d7ba8462c073333da937c35831f9b34","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7ff6e2224d7ba8462c073333da937c35831f9b34"}]},{"sha":"7ff6e2224d7ba8462c073333da937c35831f9b34","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDdmZjZlMjIyNGQ3YmE4NDYyYzA3MzMzM2RhOTM3YzM1ODMxZjliMzQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-15T22:28:12Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-15T22:28:12Z"},"message":"feat(code): make auto-update opt-out by default (#3994)\n\nAutomatic updates for `dcode` are now enabled by default; opt out with\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_AUTO_UPDATE=0` or `[update].auto_update = false`.\n\n---\n\nAuto-update for `dcode` previously defaulted to disabled (opt-in). This\nflips it to enabled by default so users stay current automatically,\nwhile keeping an easy escape hatch.\n\n`is_auto_update_enabled()` now defaults to `True` and recognizes falsy\nenv tokens, so users opt out via `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_AUTO_UPDATE=0` (or\n`false`/`no`/`off`/empty) or `[update].auto_update = false` in\n`config.toml`. Editable installs remain always disabled. The\n`update.auto_update` manifest default is updated to match.\n\n**Behavior change for existing installs:** anyone who never explicitly\nopted in will begin auto-updating on their next launch. The upgrade\nstill announces itself (`Updating dcode from vX to vY...`) before\nrunning and is fully overridable, so it is not a silent default. This is\nthe one default-enabled exception to the \"shell commands must not run\nsilently by default\" rule, now documented as such in\n`libs/code/AGENTS.md`.\n\n**Unrecognized env values fail safe-ish, not silent:** a value that is\nneither truthy nor falsy (e.g. a typo like `ture`) is ignored and falls\nthrough to config/default, but now emits a `logger.warning` mirroring\n`config_manifest._coerce_env`. Because the default is `True`, an ignored\ndisable attempt would otherwise leave auto-update on with no feedback;\nthe warning surfaces it. Note that since the default flipped, a corrupt\n`config.toml` (which `_read_update_config` logs and treats as empty) now\nfalls *open* to auto-update on rather than off — the env var still\noverrides.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"5a8e157ae1bc09f9b906eae853dbd4ab9432bf9f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/5a8e157ae1bc09f9b906eae853dbd4ab9432bf9f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/7ff6e2224d7ba8462c073333da937c35831f9b34","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMHx8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2gkQAE1vzp3BDw+VaLrYwGR+7y1R\neIL2l1W1YMwAJbqHNbIO3SEMxtxQlcbBqH+AwrudS1v7rf+s4T5iJI4V1fyH5sv1\ndomvtWa+DJJJhaPrZgXodH3c/9oNhw7ZSfaEM5l9pIN6X19bqVInY7KZSXa/Ryap\n7U2oANpDiiouDcIWus/IFmnqQzLS8uq/3OqK8wIDlXrybR9awl27PFiQMd+j00ym\n0NgdPUIW/F5hYWhLFMbACnGScrzG66bZ5mXGDDuqpbvj9625+7H3bREbCBzzMstd\nJNNQLwOSK5Qlrey/FLvGh4bVYrEiaUDCONr5oZRO57CwmjbCfuJMGVmrKv+rG5zQ\n7+0JiRuLYBBDTNILkx5vUz75VHggpyZ+Whibo3av+1XjeSaBQYUdkVvb9+8oWBDF\nY5gR2gMmqswQesfSksLHs5FXjrGsnj2cCds6zOcbSpPc6pKbvytHbXT+bPZrRypW\n8Yse801cg/+cxNaDc/rLTyE6TlEKhdeVqf3CBDkjTaLQ4UXkpnwp8GOKEOipPgHX\n1c9HPQdLrf0u4OPHQpELpXXk1QykfZUSHWtk66BFMKsZJ69GEDqVFx0tt0kO+rNC\nVYiLK/e7vurWqtNgpeYrTRVPWuPQ0/q4MeTlXg92GjTviDUj//NS+42habZYriSP\nWfK5kCZifVsUd3bTTAa3\n=wf2l\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5a8e157ae1bc09f9b906eae853dbd4ab9432bf9f\nparent e68e720e2c3caa4e4e7c5e937faf718db7ad2e98\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781562492 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781562492 -0400\n\nfeat(code): make auto-update opt-out by default (#3994)\n\nAutomatic updates for `dcode` are now enabled by default; opt out with\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_AUTO_UPDATE=0` or `[update].auto_update = false`.\n\n---\n\nAuto-update for `dcode` previously defaulted to disabled (opt-in). This\nflips it to enabled by default so users stay current automatically,\nwhile keeping an easy escape hatch.\n\n`is_auto_update_enabled()` now defaults to `True` and recognizes falsy\nenv tokens, so users opt out via `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_AUTO_UPDATE=0` (or\n`false`/`no`/`off`/empty) or `[update].auto_update = false` in\n`config.toml`. Editable installs remain always disabled. The\n`update.auto_update` manifest default is updated to match.\n\n**Behavior change for existing installs:** anyone who never explicitly\nopted in will begin auto-updating on their next launch. The upgrade\nstill announces itself (`Updating dcode from vX to vY...`) before\nrunning and is fully overridable, so it is not a silent default. This is\nthe one default-enabled exception to the \"shell commands must not run\nsilently by default\" rule, now documented as such in\n`libs/code/AGENTS.md`.\n\n**Unrecognized env values fail safe-ish, not silent:** a value that is\nneither truthy nor falsy (e.g. a typo like `ture`) is ignored and falls\nthrough to config/default, but now emits a `logger.warning` mirroring\n`config_manifest._coerce_env`. Because the default is `True`, an ignored\ndisable attempt would otherwise leave auto-update on with no feedback;\nthe warning surfaces it. Note that since the default flipped, a corrupt\n`config.toml` (which `_read_update_config` logs and treats as empty) now\nfalls *open* to auto-update on rather than off — the env var still\noverrides.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-15T22:28:13Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7ff6e2224d7ba8462c073333da937c35831f9b34","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7ff6e2224d7ba8462c073333da937c35831f9b34","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7ff6e2224d7ba8462c073333da937c35831f9b34/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e68e720e2c3caa4e4e7c5e937faf718db7ad2e98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e68e720e2c3caa4e4e7c5e937faf718db7ad2e98","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e68e720e2c3caa4e4e7c5e937faf718db7ad2e98"}]},{"sha":"e68e720e2c3caa4e4e7c5e937faf718db7ad2e98","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGU2OGU3MjBlMmMzY2FhNGU0ZTdjNWU5MzdmYWY3MThkYjdhZDJlOTg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-15T18:53:35Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-15T18:53:35Z"},"message":"feat(code): warn on `--interpreter-tools` without `--interpreter` (#3976)\n\nThe CLI now warns when `--interpreter-tools` is passed without\n`--interpreter`, since the flag has no effect on its own.\n\n---\n\nPassing `--interpreter-tools` configures the PTC allowlist for the\n`js_eval` interpreter, but that allowlist only takes effect when the\ninterpreter middleware is enabled via `--interpreter`. Previously the\nflag was silently parsed and ignored in that case, leaving users with no\nfeedback.\n\nThe advisory is surfaced on whichever path the user is on:\n\n- **Non-interactive (`-n`):** a one-line stderr warning —\n`--interpreter-tools has no effect unless --interpreter is set.` —\nemitted after argument validation. It does not exit nonzero and does not\ntrigger interpreter dependency verification.\n- **Interactive (TUI):** the same advisory as a startup notification. A\nstderr line printed just before the TUI launches is clobbered by the\nalternate screen and never seen, so the app emits a `warning`-severity\ntoast on mount instead. This reuses the interpreter values already\nhanded to the app, so no new plumbing or signature changes are needed.\n\nOnly the `--interpreter` CLI flag gates the advisory. `[interpreter]`\nconfig values are untouched, and invalid `--interpreter-tools` values\nkeep their existing usage-error behavior — those errors take precedence\nover the advisory.\n\n**Known limitation:** `--interpreter-tools` is a top-level flag, so\npassing it alongside a management subcommand (`threads`, `mcp`,\n`agents`, `skills`) does not warn — those paths exit before a session\nlaunches. Combining an interpreter flag with a management subcommand is\nan obvious no-op with no correctness impact.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"3a0cb4bee03950fcedb4b62b83a993144ba017bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/3a0cb4bee03950fcedb4b62b83a993144ba017bf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/e68e720e2c3caa4e4e7c5e937faf718db7ad2e98","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMEovCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANuEQAAkiNldCHl1QeYIYg8eUSal/\nNTLXnPKkRwmcHJxoBREOwNfsMUQOqcANrCohWuiCvxu5UTUhYOEYcznCyCFKaV02\n8cWmm+lgZHYr//rVxjlcaWE/PrHQydKtI+X25bXFmPn1V4Iih1kuFgt7AlwMe/Ck\nlU7IkefwSGLcjdzomc1qkMi/0BFzuG5m5H+P+J6J2ngZd6lAjeiAuaK59BpXyt9O\nS9ECsf8JETUxS7wXIezGe0rom7I4zIma6anvRmrbaeM1pwuqD8mRmo3JHMMohuF4\nArL6SIUWKM1dYTmoclo6L4NkjLOUqcZXn36roMv6+3vh+AQ6WT0laklpmFX3NlUL\n6zABSeGLs6+L2fCUXlpSCVj5Awy998WRH4a5feQ4yR+blp4ZjYenbBddqGCPpkoA\nFO2T0JVqdDD3l8SU8R6mdymgRs+AqZLPVPtLvINT/zvp+kWSDsP7+H9JqqtEoBpM\nwElEZLa70/yrimQINX44sExGVCBp6HONc0gOVZC0KH5xvnQbP+svw/+zwD29weXs\nseZGhHCgi+bb546MvsqM/zu1uH6KCY3u4P8xNaHq447oPibATMBOJxngTKBlxF41\n1CUQ3yE9XW9sUfsOfd4IAus36BFwRz+92vuL4jThCqQaltCdy6K69BAKLwq9KnwR\nIIZUvs2poekJNkEx4gI3\n=xnW2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3a0cb4bee03950fcedb4b62b83a993144ba017bf\nparent 63a9d5b1b68148e8931edfce9ab413325b344f35\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781549615 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781549615 -0400\n\nfeat(code): warn on `--interpreter-tools` without `--interpreter` (#3976)\n\nThe CLI now warns when `--interpreter-tools` is passed without\n`--interpreter`, since the flag has no effect on its own.\n\n---\n\nPassing `--interpreter-tools` configures the PTC allowlist for the\n`js_eval` interpreter, but that allowlist only takes effect when the\ninterpreter middleware is enabled via `--interpreter`. Previously the\nflag was silently parsed and ignored in that case, leaving users with no\nfeedback.\n\nThe advisory is surfaced on whichever path the user is on:\n\n- **Non-interactive (`-n`):** a one-line stderr warning —\n`--interpreter-tools has no effect unless --interpreter is set.` —\nemitted after argument validation. It does not exit nonzero and does not\ntrigger interpreter dependency verification.\n- **Interactive (TUI):** the same advisory as a startup notification. A\nstderr line printed just before the TUI launches is clobbered by the\nalternate screen and never seen, so the app emits a `warning`-severity\ntoast on mount instead. This reuses the interpreter values already\nhanded to the app, so no new plumbing or signature changes are needed.\n\nOnly the `--interpreter` CLI flag gates the advisory. `[interpreter]`\nconfig values are untouched, and invalid `--interpreter-tools` values\nkeep their existing usage-error behavior — those errors take precedence\nover the advisory.\n\n**Known limitation:** `--interpreter-tools` is a top-level flag, so\npassing it alongside a management subcommand (`threads`, `mcp`,\n`agents`, `skills`) does not warn — those paths exit before a session\nlaunches. Combining an interpreter flag with a management subcommand is\nan obvious no-op with no correctness impact.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-15T18:53:36Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e68e720e2c3caa4e4e7c5e937faf718db7ad2e98","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e68e720e2c3caa4e4e7c5e937faf718db7ad2e98","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e68e720e2c3caa4e4e7c5e937faf718db7ad2e98/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"63a9d5b1b68148e8931edfce9ab413325b344f35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/63a9d5b1b68148e8931edfce9ab413325b344f35","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/63a9d5b1b68148e8931edfce9ab413325b344f35"}]},{"sha":"63a9d5b1b68148e8931edfce9ab413325b344f35","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDYzYTlkNWIxYjY4MTQ4ZTg5MzFlZGZjZTlhYjQxMzMyNWIzNDRmMzU","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-15T18:50:12Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-15T18:50:12Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump pyjwt from 2.12.1 to 2.13.0 in /libs/code (#3985)\n\nBumps [pyjwt](https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt) from 2.12.1 to 2.13.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/releases\">pyjwt's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>2.13.0</h2>\n<h1>PyJWT 2.13.0 — Security Release</h1>\n<p>This release bundles five security fixes plus three additional\nhardening / spec-compliance changes. We recommend all users upgrade.</p>\n<h2>Security</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx\"><code>GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx</code></a>\n— JWK JSON accepted as HMAC secret (algorithm confusion).</strong>\n<code>HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key</code> previously rejected PEM- and\nSSH-formatted asymmetric keys but did not catch a JWK passed as a raw\nJSON string. In a verifier configured with both symmetric and asymmetric\nalgorithms in <code>algorithms=[…]</code> and a raw-JSON JWK as the key,\nan attacker could forge HS256 tokens using the JWK text as the HMAC\nsecret. The guard has been extended to reject any JWK-shaped JSON.\n<em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aradona91\"><code>@​aradona91</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f\"><code>GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f</code></a>\n— Algorithm allow-list bypass with <code>PyJWK</code> /\n<code>PyJWKClient</code>.</strong> When verifying with a\n<code>PyJWK</code>, the caller's <code>algorithms=[…]</code> allow-list\nwas checked against the token header <code>alg</code> as a string only;\nactual verification used the algorithm bound to the <code>PyJWK</code>.\nAn attacker who controlled a registered JWKS key could sign with one\nalgorithm and advertise another on the header. PyJWT now requires the\ntoken header <code>alg</code> to match the <code>PyJWK</code>'s\nalgorithm before verification. <em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sushi-gif\"><code>@​sushi-gif</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39\"><code>GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39</code></a>\n— DoS via base64 decode of unused payload segment when\n<code>b64=false</code>.</strong> For detached-payload JWS\n(<code>b64=false</code>), the compact-form payload segment was\nbase64-decoded before being discarded in favor of the caller-supplied\n<code>detached_payload</code>. An attacker could inflate the unused\nsegment to force CPU + memory cost without holding a valid signature.\nThe segment is now required to be empty per RFC 7515 Appendix F, and is\nno longer decoded. <em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/thesmartshadow\"><code>@​thesmartshadow</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4\"><code>GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4</code></a>\n— <code>PyJWKClient</code> accepts non-HTTP(S) URIs.</strong>\n<code>PyJWKClient.fetch_data</code> passed its URI to\n<code>urllib.request.urlopen</code>, which by default also handles\n<code>file://</code>, <code>ftp://</code>, and <code>data:</code>\nschemes. An application that fed an attacker-influenced URI into\n<code>PyJWKClient</code> could be coerced into reading local files or\nreaching other unintended schemes. <code>PyJWKClient</code> now rejects\nany URI whose scheme isn't <code>http</code> or <code>https</code>.\n<em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/KEIJOT\"><code>@​KEIJOT</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8\"><code>GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8</code></a>\n— <code>PyJWKClient</code> cache wiped on fetch error.</strong> A\n<code>finally</code>-block <code>put(jwk_set=None)</code> cleared the\nJWK Set cache whenever a fetch raised, turning a transient JWKS-endpoint\noutage into application-wide auth failure. The cache write was moved\ninto the success path; transient errors no longer evict valid cached\nkeys. <em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/eddieran\"><code>@​eddieran</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Fixed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Reject empty HMAC keys outright in\n<code>HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key</code> with <code>InvalidKeyError</code>\ninstead of accepting them with only a warning. Defends against the\n<code>os.getenv(&quot;JWT_SECRET&quot;, &quot;&quot;)</code> footgun.\n<em>Thanks to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/SnailSploit\"><code>@​SnailSploit</code></a> and\n<a href=\"https://github.com/spartan8806\"><code>@​spartan8806</code></a>\nfor the reports.</em></li>\n<li>Forward per-call <code>options</code> (including\n<code>enforce_minimum_key_length</code>) from <code>PyJWT.decode</code>\nthrough to <code>PyJWS._verify_signature</code>. The option was\npreviously silently dropped between the two layers, so it only took\neffect when set on the <code>PyJWT</code> instance. <em>Thanks to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/WLUB\"><code>@​WLUB</code></a> for the\nreport.</em></li>\n<li><strong>RFC 7797 §3 compliance for <code>b64=false</code>:</strong>\nthe encoder now auto-adds <code>&quot;b64&quot;</code> to\n<code>crit</code>, and the decoder rejects tokens that set\n<code>b64=false</code> without listing it in <code>crit</code>.\n<em>Thanks to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/MachineLearning-Nerd\"><code>@​MachineLearning-Nerd</code></a>\nfor the report.</em></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Migrate the <code>dev</code>, <code>docs</code>, and\n<code>tests</code> package extras to dependency groups, by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kurtmckee\"><code>@​kurtmckee</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/pull/1152\">#1152</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Upgrade notes</h2>\n<p>Most fixes are invisible to correctly-configured callers. A few\nbehavioral changes you may encounter:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Empty HMAC keys now raise.</strong> If your app passed\n<code>&quot;&quot;</code> or <code>b&quot;&quot;</code> as a secret\n(often via a missing env var, e.g.\n<code>os.getenv(&quot;JWT_SECRET&quot;, &quot;&quot;)</code>),\n<code>encode</code>/<code>decode</code> will now raise\n<code>InvalidKeyError</code>. This is the intended behavior — fix the\nconfiguration.</li>\n<li><strong><code>PyJWK</code> decoding now requires the token's\n<code>alg</code> to match the JWK's algorithm.</strong> Previously a\nmismatch was silently honored if the header <code>alg</code> appeared in\nthe allow-list. Tokens that relied on this mismatch will now fail with\n<code>InvalidAlgorithmError</code>.</li>\n<li><strong><code>PyJWKClient</code> now rejects non-HTTP(S) URIs at\nconstruction time.</strong> Tests or dev environments that fetched JWKS\nfrom <code>file://</code> URIs need to switch to a local HTTP server or\nload the JWKS by other means (e.g. construct\n<code>PyJWKSet.from_dict(...)</code> directly).</li>\n<li><strong><code>b64=false</code> tokens are now strictly RFC 7515 /\n7797 compliant.</strong> Tokens with a non-empty compact-form payload\nsegment, or that omit <code>&quot;b64&quot;</code> from\n<code>crit</code>, will be rejected. PyJWT-produced tokens always\nsatisfy both invariants, so round-trips through PyJWT are\nunaffected.</li>\n<li><strong><code>enforce_minimum_key_length</code> set per-call now\ntakes effect.</strong> Callers who passed\n<code>options={&quot;enforce_minimum_key_length&quot;: True}</code> to\n<code>jwt.decode()</code> previously got no enforcement; they will now\nget <code>InvalidKeyError</code> on undersized keys, as documented.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full changelog:</strong> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.1...2.13.0\">https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.1...2.13.0</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/blob/master/CHANGELOG.rst\">pyjwt's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2><code>v2.13.0\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.1...2.13.0&gt;</code>__</h2>\n<p>Security</p>\n<pre><code>\n- Reject JWK JSON documents passed as raw HMAC secrets in\n  ``HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key`` to close an algorithm-confusion gap that\n  the existing PEM/SSH guard did not cover. Reported by @aradona91 in\n`GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx&gt;`__.\n- Bind the JWT header ``alg`` to ``PyJWK.algorithm_name`` during\n  verification so the caller's ``algorithms=[...]`` allow-list cannot be\nbypassed when decoding with a ``PyJWK`` / ``PyJWKClient`` key. Reported\nby @sushi-gif in `GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f&gt;`__.\n- Reject non-``http(s)`` URI schemes in ``PyJWKClient`` so attacker-\ninfluenced URIs cannot read local files or reach unintended schemes via\nurllib's default ``file://`` / ``ftp://`` / ``data:`` handlers. Reported\nby @KEIJOT in `GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4&gt;`__.\n- Preserve the cached JWK Set on fetch errors in\n``PyJWKClient.fetch_data``.\n  The previous ``finally``-block ``put(None)`` pattern cleared the cache\non any transient outage, turning one bad JWKS request into application-\nwide auth failure. Reported by @eddieran in `GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8&gt;`__.\n- Skip the unconditional base64 decode of the compact-form payload\nsegment\n  when ``b64=false`` is set in the protected header, and require that\n  segment to be empty (RFC 7515 Appendix F detached form). Closes an\n  unauthenticated DoS amplifier. Reported by @thesmartshadow in\n`GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39&gt;`__.\n<p>Fixed</p>\n<pre><code>\n- Reject empty HMAC keys outright in ``HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key`` with\n  ``InvalidKeyError`` instead of accepting them with only a warning.\n  Thanks to @SnailSploit and @spartan8806 for independently flagging the\n  footgun.\n- Forward per-call ``options`` (including\n``enforce_minimum_key_length``)\n  from ``PyJWT.decode`` through to ``PyJWS._verify_signature`` so the\noption actually takes effect when set at the call site rather than only\n  on the ``PyJWT`` instance. Thanks to @WLUB for the report.\n- RFC 7797 §3 compliance for ``b64=false``: the encoder now auto-adds\n``&amp;quot;b64&amp;quot;`` to the ``crit`` header parameter, and the\ndecoder rejects\ntokens that set ``b64=false`` without listing it in ``crit``. Thanks to\n  @MachineLearning-Nerd for the report.\n\nChanged\n</code></pre>\n<ul>\n<li>Migrate the <code>dev</code>, <code>docs</code>, and\n<code>tests</code> package extras to dependency groups by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kurtmckee\"><code>@​kurtmckee</code></a> in\n<code>[#1152](https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1152)\n&amp;lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/pull/1152&amp;gt;</code>__\n</code></pre></li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/7144e4534c34810f4525dc4578a32addd8212cff\"><code>7144e45</code></a>\nApply ruff format</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/d2f4bec4963897c0ef96ef64a875894f2c8542ab\"><code>d2f4bec</code></a>\nRestore <code>cast()</code> calls with cross-version <code>type:\nignore</code> for <code>prepare_key</code></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/22f478cebddd8294259c30f037ecb92b0b348774\"><code>22f478c</code></a>\nRemove redundant casts in <code>RSAAlgorithm.prepare_key</code> and\n`ECAlgorithm.prepare...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/95791b1759b8aa4f2203575d344d5c78564cdc81\"><code>95791b1</code></a>\nBundle security fixes and hardening into 2.13.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/dcc27a9d3182a2349c30b160758785c6ce7a6508\"><code>dcc27a9</code></a>\n[pre-commit.ci] pre-commit autoupdate (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1155\">#1155</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/9d08a9a1896845ed8eaf88e6f6ac61e5800c3e7a\"><code>9d08a9a</code></a>\n[pre-commit.ci] pre-commit autoupdate (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1146\">#1146</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/b87c10014d4109f0214fea188d00faaaf8a80e64\"><code>b87c100</code></a>\nBump codecov/codecov-action from 5 to 6 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1154\">#1154</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/40e3147eb5f790d8d041772e5fc00728a176c812\"><code>40e3147</code></a>\nMigrate development extras to dependency groups (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1152\">#1152</a>)</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.1...2.13.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"5b55c09f3519290a6874727b6b16ea5c576012ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/5b55c09f3519290a6874727b6b16ea5c576012ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/63a9d5b1b68148e8931edfce9ab413325b344f35","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMElkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4tsQAExyWkGp53NEwoS6gIEeh/Iv\nks3h1k9Kw38d192ona3O8+8QRINyqId/5nfVDPUShRYeUOhP8/Pa/iBf5+FQkNCQ\nliSc8ThsizMfh+lCvjgX2EIAm7KNXVm0ge+wvv5S9JFqypxeUqwqVCY6iTaVvEhy\nP0VYf++R4jxQ6ovlzjrVQt7WiCzQNMV+ZHDlpnm68HTlsrzf/l9YPzRn9SHrKYKi\nQ93YZQI3Rk30qLCTyBrnSBtYePQKiYmWPpfjYOuyNF5laNR+le2oOUw1eEWB+MV2\ntuH8mbFs8nrJEc4QJnHMcDj8HHzAZonyBo2tVJPwA9JmH41uZ3cXa7LYDZZ1/uDJ\naw84hBsYaOa7I7ABKcRAsO+4INQBU3tf53zvul1/hLYMWdqc0Y8cDZwTI4P/4Ebz\nOJ0AxpY2wxh6cp0NtLVEl4JBrJBllN5c6QeznXmJMZyel6Ktl55wPc79KQYtVjrM\nUl8wJ1mMut5lT296faLxsEcH3q+xv9crrazO6CYNRrl566RKeGo17BjNjck4+6sF\nx2pDpbAI2DYcdv6qG8r+LM9qTOLeZzMzOzGFVVSkK8elvVk49KFHHwUSx0Iy3S9l\nLcXhiy8fOQliMed294vjZFMfIQ8KrmRZrv08a0/+reGb3Mv64pKcSaaw8sU2nFe2\nS/v6svGYDBsx3LUcjjMd\n=u3s1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5b55c09f3519290a6874727b6b16ea5c576012ae\nparent 9b6b9039d98d502e884ccc8eb88e56221819c6ea\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1781549412 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781549412 -0400\n\nchore(deps): bump pyjwt from 2.12.1 to 2.13.0 in /libs/code (#3985)\n\nBumps [pyjwt](https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt) from 2.12.1 to 2.13.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/releases\">pyjwt's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>2.13.0</h2>\n<h1>PyJWT 2.13.0 — Security Release</h1>\n<p>This release bundles five security fixes plus three additional\nhardening / spec-compliance changes. We recommend all users upgrade.</p>\n<h2>Security</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx\"><code>GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx</code></a>\n— JWK JSON accepted as HMAC secret (algorithm confusion).</strong>\n<code>HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key</code> previously rejected PEM- and\nSSH-formatted asymmetric keys but did not catch a JWK passed as a raw\nJSON string. In a verifier configured with both symmetric and asymmetric\nalgorithms in <code>algorithms=[…]</code> and a raw-JSON JWK as the key,\nan attacker could forge HS256 tokens using the JWK text as the HMAC\nsecret. The guard has been extended to reject any JWK-shaped JSON.\n<em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aradona91\"><code>@​aradona91</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f\"><code>GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f</code></a>\n— Algorithm allow-list bypass with <code>PyJWK</code> /\n<code>PyJWKClient</code>.</strong> When verifying with a\n<code>PyJWK</code>, the caller's <code>algorithms=[…]</code> allow-list\nwas checked against the token header <code>alg</code> as a string only;\nactual verification used the algorithm bound to the <code>PyJWK</code>.\nAn attacker who controlled a registered JWKS key could sign with one\nalgorithm and advertise another on the header. PyJWT now requires the\ntoken header <code>alg</code> to match the <code>PyJWK</code>'s\nalgorithm before verification. <em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sushi-gif\"><code>@​sushi-gif</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39\"><code>GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39</code></a>\n— DoS via base64 decode of unused payload segment when\n<code>b64=false</code>.</strong> For detached-payload JWS\n(<code>b64=false</code>), the compact-form payload segment was\nbase64-decoded before being discarded in favor of the caller-supplied\n<code>detached_payload</code>. An attacker could inflate the unused\nsegment to force CPU + memory cost without holding a valid signature.\nThe segment is now required to be empty per RFC 7515 Appendix F, and is\nno longer decoded. <em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/thesmartshadow\"><code>@​thesmartshadow</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4\"><code>GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4</code></a>\n— <code>PyJWKClient</code> accepts non-HTTP(S) URIs.</strong>\n<code>PyJWKClient.fetch_data</code> passed its URI to\n<code>urllib.request.urlopen</code>, which by default also handles\n<code>file://</code>, <code>ftp://</code>, and <code>data:</code>\nschemes. An application that fed an attacker-influenced URI into\n<code>PyJWKClient</code> could be coerced into reading local files or\nreaching other unintended schemes. <code>PyJWKClient</code> now rejects\nany URI whose scheme isn't <code>http</code> or <code>https</code>.\n<em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/KEIJOT\"><code>@​KEIJOT</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8\"><code>GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8</code></a>\n— <code>PyJWKClient</code> cache wiped on fetch error.</strong> A\n<code>finally</code>-block <code>put(jwk_set=None)</code> cleared the\nJWK Set cache whenever a fetch raised, turning a transient JWKS-endpoint\noutage into application-wide auth failure. The cache write was moved\ninto the success path; transient errors no longer evict valid cached\nkeys. <em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/eddieran\"><code>@​eddieran</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Fixed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Reject empty HMAC keys outright in\n<code>HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key</code> with <code>InvalidKeyError</code>\ninstead of accepting them with only a warning. Defends against the\n<code>os.getenv(&quot;JWT_SECRET&quot;, &quot;&quot;)</code> footgun.\n<em>Thanks to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/SnailSploit\"><code>@​SnailSploit</code></a> and\n<a href=\"https://github.com/spartan8806\"><code>@​spartan8806</code></a>\nfor the reports.</em></li>\n<li>Forward per-call <code>options</code> (including\n<code>enforce_minimum_key_length</code>) from <code>PyJWT.decode</code>\nthrough to <code>PyJWS._verify_signature</code>. The option was\npreviously silently dropped between the two layers, so it only took\neffect when set on the <code>PyJWT</code> instance. <em>Thanks to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/WLUB\"><code>@​WLUB</code></a> for the\nreport.</em></li>\n<li><strong>RFC 7797 §3 compliance for <code>b64=false</code>:</strong>\nthe encoder now auto-adds <code>&quot;b64&quot;</code> to\n<code>crit</code>, and the decoder rejects tokens that set\n<code>b64=false</code> without listing it in <code>crit</code>.\n<em>Thanks to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/MachineLearning-Nerd\"><code>@​MachineLearning-Nerd</code></a>\nfor the report.</em></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Migrate the <code>dev</code>, <code>docs</code>, and\n<code>tests</code> package extras to dependency groups, by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kurtmckee\"><code>@​kurtmckee</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/pull/1152\">#1152</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Upgrade notes</h2>\n<p>Most fixes are invisible to correctly-configured callers. A few\nbehavioral changes you may encounter:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Empty HMAC keys now raise.</strong> If your app passed\n<code>&quot;&quot;</code> or <code>b&quot;&quot;</code> as a secret\n(often via a missing env var, e.g.\n<code>os.getenv(&quot;JWT_SECRET&quot;, &quot;&quot;)</code>),\n<code>encode</code>/<code>decode</code> will now raise\n<code>InvalidKeyError</code>. This is the intended behavior — fix the\nconfiguration.</li>\n<li><strong><code>PyJWK</code> decoding now requires the token's\n<code>alg</code> to match the JWK's algorithm.</strong> Previously a\nmismatch was silently honored if the header <code>alg</code> appeared in\nthe allow-list. Tokens that relied on this mismatch will now fail with\n<code>InvalidAlgorithmError</code>.</li>\n<li><strong><code>PyJWKClient</code> now rejects non-HTTP(S) URIs at\nconstruction time.</strong> Tests or dev environments that fetched JWKS\nfrom <code>file://</code> URIs need to switch to a local HTTP server or\nload the JWKS by other means (e.g. construct\n<code>PyJWKSet.from_dict(...)</code> directly).</li>\n<li><strong><code>b64=false</code> tokens are now strictly RFC 7515 /\n7797 compliant.</strong> Tokens with a non-empty compact-form payload\nsegment, or that omit <code>&quot;b64&quot;</code> from\n<code>crit</code>, will be rejected. PyJWT-produced tokens always\nsatisfy both invariants, so round-trips through PyJWT are\nunaffected.</li>\n<li><strong><code>enforce_minimum_key_length</code> set per-call now\ntakes effect.</strong> Callers who passed\n<code>options={&quot;enforce_minimum_key_length&quot;: True}</code> to\n<code>jwt.decode()</code> previously got no enforcement; they will now\nget <code>InvalidKeyError</code> on undersized keys, as documented.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full changelog:</strong> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.1...2.13.0\">https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.1...2.13.0</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/blob/master/CHANGELOG.rst\">pyjwt's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2><code>v2.13.0\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.1...2.13.0&gt;</code>__</h2>\n<p>Security</p>\n<pre><code>\n- Reject JWK JSON documents passed as raw HMAC secrets in\n  ``HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key`` to close an algorithm-confusion gap that\n  the existing PEM/SSH guard did not cover. Reported by @aradona91 in\n`GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx&gt;`__.\n- Bind the JWT header ``alg`` to ``PyJWK.algorithm_name`` during\n  verification so the caller's ``algorithms=[...]`` allow-list cannot be\nbypassed when decoding with a ``PyJWK`` / ``PyJWKClient`` key. Reported\nby @sushi-gif in `GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f&gt;`__.\n- Reject non-``http(s)`` URI schemes in ``PyJWKClient`` so attacker-\ninfluenced URIs cannot read local files or reach unintended schemes via\nurllib's default ``file://`` / ``ftp://`` / ``data:`` handlers. Reported\nby @KEIJOT in `GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4&gt;`__.\n- Preserve the cached JWK Set on fetch errors in\n``PyJWKClient.fetch_data``.\n  The previous ``finally``-block ``put(None)`` pattern cleared the cache\non any transient outage, turning one bad JWKS request into application-\nwide auth failure. Reported by @eddieran in `GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8&gt;`__.\n- Skip the unconditional base64 decode of the compact-form payload\nsegment\n  when ``b64=false`` is set in the protected header, and require that\n  segment to be empty (RFC 7515 Appendix F detached form). Closes an\n  unauthenticated DoS amplifier. Reported by @thesmartshadow in\n`GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39&gt;`__.\n<p>Fixed</p>\n<pre><code>\n- Reject empty HMAC keys outright in ``HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key`` with\n  ``InvalidKeyError`` instead of accepting them with only a warning.\n  Thanks to @SnailSploit and @spartan8806 for independently flagging the\n  footgun.\n- Forward per-call ``options`` (including\n``enforce_minimum_key_length``)\n  from ``PyJWT.decode`` through to ``PyJWS._verify_signature`` so the\noption actually takes effect when set at the call site rather than only\n  on the ``PyJWT`` instance. Thanks to @WLUB for the report.\n- RFC 7797 §3 compliance for ``b64=false``: the encoder now auto-adds\n``&amp;quot;b64&amp;quot;`` to the ``crit`` header parameter, and the\ndecoder rejects\ntokens that set ``b64=false`` without listing it in ``crit``. Thanks to\n  @MachineLearning-Nerd for the report.\n\nChanged\n</code></pre>\n<ul>\n<li>Migrate the <code>dev</code>, <code>docs</code>, and\n<code>tests</code> package extras to dependency groups by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kurtmckee\"><code>@​kurtmckee</code></a> in\n<code>[#1152](https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1152)\n&amp;lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/pull/1152&amp;gt;</code>__\n</code></pre></li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/7144e4534c34810f4525dc4578a32addd8212cff\"><code>7144e45</code></a>\nApply ruff format</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/d2f4bec4963897c0ef96ef64a875894f2c8542ab\"><code>d2f4bec</code></a>\nRestore <code>cast()</code> calls with cross-version <code>type:\nignore</code> for <code>prepare_key</code></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/22f478cebddd8294259c30f037ecb92b0b348774\"><code>22f478c</code></a>\nRemove redundant casts in <code>RSAAlgorithm.prepare_key</code> and\n`ECAlgorithm.prepare...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/95791b1759b8aa4f2203575d344d5c78564cdc81\"><code>95791b1</code></a>\nBundle security fixes and hardening into 2.13.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/dcc27a9d3182a2349c30b160758785c6ce7a6508\"><code>dcc27a9</code></a>\n[pre-commit.ci] pre-commit autoupdate (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1155\">#1155</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/9d08a9a1896845ed8eaf88e6f6ac61e5800c3e7a\"><code>9d08a9a</code></a>\n[pre-commit.ci] pre-commit autoupdate (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1146\">#1146</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/b87c10014d4109f0214fea188d00faaaf8a80e64\"><code>b87c100</code></a>\nBump codecov/codecov-action from 5 to 6 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1154\">#1154</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/40e3147eb5f790d8d041772e5fc00728a176c812\"><code>40e3147</code></a>\nMigrate development extras to dependency groups (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1152\">#1152</a>)</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.1...2.13.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-15T18:50:12Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/63a9d5b1b68148e8931edfce9ab413325b344f35","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/63a9d5b1b68148e8931edfce9ab413325b344f35","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/63a9d5b1b68148e8931edfce9ab413325b344f35/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9b6b9039d98d502e884ccc8eb88e56221819c6ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9b6b9039d98d502e884ccc8eb88e56221819c6ea","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9b6b9039d98d502e884ccc8eb88e56221819c6ea"}]},{"sha":"9b6b9039d98d502e884ccc8eb88e56221819c6ea","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDliNmI5MDM5ZDk4ZDUwMmU4ODRjY2M4ZWI4OGU1NjIyMTgxOWM2ZWE","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-15T18:50:03Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-15T18:50:03Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump pyjwt from 2.12.1 to 2.13.0 in /examples/nvidia_deep_agent (#3986)\n\nBumps [pyjwt](https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt) from 2.12.1 to 2.13.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/releases\">pyjwt's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>2.13.0</h2>\n<h1>PyJWT 2.13.0 — Security Release</h1>\n<p>This release bundles five security fixes plus three additional\nhardening / spec-compliance changes. We recommend all users upgrade.</p>\n<h2>Security</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx\"><code>GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx</code></a>\n— JWK JSON accepted as HMAC secret (algorithm confusion).</strong>\n<code>HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key</code> previously rejected PEM- and\nSSH-formatted asymmetric keys but did not catch a JWK passed as a raw\nJSON string. In a verifier configured with both symmetric and asymmetric\nalgorithms in <code>algorithms=[…]</code> and a raw-JSON JWK as the key,\nan attacker could forge HS256 tokens using the JWK text as the HMAC\nsecret. The guard has been extended to reject any JWK-shaped JSON.\n<em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aradona91\"><code>@​aradona91</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f\"><code>GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f</code></a>\n— Algorithm allow-list bypass with <code>PyJWK</code> /\n<code>PyJWKClient</code>.</strong> When verifying with a\n<code>PyJWK</code>, the caller's <code>algorithms=[…]</code> allow-list\nwas checked against the token header <code>alg</code> as a string only;\nactual verification used the algorithm bound to the <code>PyJWK</code>.\nAn attacker who controlled a registered JWKS key could sign with one\nalgorithm and advertise another on the header. PyJWT now requires the\ntoken header <code>alg</code> to match the <code>PyJWK</code>'s\nalgorithm before verification. <em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sushi-gif\"><code>@​sushi-gif</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39\"><code>GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39</code></a>\n— DoS via base64 decode of unused payload segment when\n<code>b64=false</code>.</strong> For detached-payload JWS\n(<code>b64=false</code>), the compact-form payload segment was\nbase64-decoded before being discarded in favor of the caller-supplied\n<code>detached_payload</code>. An attacker could inflate the unused\nsegment to force CPU + memory cost without holding a valid signature.\nThe segment is now required to be empty per RFC 7515 Appendix F, and is\nno longer decoded. <em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/thesmartshadow\"><code>@​thesmartshadow</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4\"><code>GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4</code></a>\n— <code>PyJWKClient</code> accepts non-HTTP(S) URIs.</strong>\n<code>PyJWKClient.fetch_data</code> passed its URI to\n<code>urllib.request.urlopen</code>, which by default also handles\n<code>file://</code>, <code>ftp://</code>, and <code>data:</code>\nschemes. An application that fed an attacker-influenced URI into\n<code>PyJWKClient</code> could be coerced into reading local files or\nreaching other unintended schemes. <code>PyJWKClient</code> now rejects\nany URI whose scheme isn't <code>http</code> or <code>https</code>.\n<em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/KEIJOT\"><code>@​KEIJOT</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8\"><code>GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8</code></a>\n— <code>PyJWKClient</code> cache wiped on fetch error.</strong> A\n<code>finally</code>-block <code>put(jwk_set=None)</code> cleared the\nJWK Set cache whenever a fetch raised, turning a transient JWKS-endpoint\noutage into application-wide auth failure. The cache write was moved\ninto the success path; transient errors no longer evict valid cached\nkeys. <em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/eddieran\"><code>@​eddieran</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Fixed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Reject empty HMAC keys outright in\n<code>HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key</code> with <code>InvalidKeyError</code>\ninstead of accepting them with only a warning. Defends against the\n<code>os.getenv(&quot;JWT_SECRET&quot;, &quot;&quot;)</code> footgun.\n<em>Thanks to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/SnailSploit\"><code>@​SnailSploit</code></a> and\n<a href=\"https://github.com/spartan8806\"><code>@​spartan8806</code></a>\nfor the reports.</em></li>\n<li>Forward per-call <code>options</code> (including\n<code>enforce_minimum_key_length</code>) from <code>PyJWT.decode</code>\nthrough to <code>PyJWS._verify_signature</code>. The option was\npreviously silently dropped between the two layers, so it only took\neffect when set on the <code>PyJWT</code> instance. <em>Thanks to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/WLUB\"><code>@​WLUB</code></a> for the\nreport.</em></li>\n<li><strong>RFC 7797 §3 compliance for <code>b64=false</code>:</strong>\nthe encoder now auto-adds <code>&quot;b64&quot;</code> to\n<code>crit</code>, and the decoder rejects tokens that set\n<code>b64=false</code> without listing it in <code>crit</code>.\n<em>Thanks to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/MachineLearning-Nerd\"><code>@​MachineLearning-Nerd</code></a>\nfor the report.</em></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Migrate the <code>dev</code>, <code>docs</code>, and\n<code>tests</code> package extras to dependency groups, by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kurtmckee\"><code>@​kurtmckee</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/pull/1152\">#1152</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Upgrade notes</h2>\n<p>Most fixes are invisible to correctly-configured callers. A few\nbehavioral changes you may encounter:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Empty HMAC keys now raise.</strong> If your app passed\n<code>&quot;&quot;</code> or <code>b&quot;&quot;</code> as a secret\n(often via a missing env var, e.g.\n<code>os.getenv(&quot;JWT_SECRET&quot;, &quot;&quot;)</code>),\n<code>encode</code>/<code>decode</code> will now raise\n<code>InvalidKeyError</code>. This is the intended behavior — fix the\nconfiguration.</li>\n<li><strong><code>PyJWK</code> decoding now requires the token's\n<code>alg</code> to match the JWK's algorithm.</strong> Previously a\nmismatch was silently honored if the header <code>alg</code> appeared in\nthe allow-list. Tokens that relied on this mismatch will now fail with\n<code>InvalidAlgorithmError</code>.</li>\n<li><strong><code>PyJWKClient</code> now rejects non-HTTP(S) URIs at\nconstruction time.</strong> Tests or dev environments that fetched JWKS\nfrom <code>file://</code> URIs need to switch to a local HTTP server or\nload the JWKS by other means (e.g. construct\n<code>PyJWKSet.from_dict(...)</code> directly).</li>\n<li><strong><code>b64=false</code> tokens are now strictly RFC 7515 /\n7797 compliant.</strong> Tokens with a non-empty compact-form payload\nsegment, or that omit <code>&quot;b64&quot;</code> from\n<code>crit</code>, will be rejected. PyJWT-produced tokens always\nsatisfy both invariants, so round-trips through PyJWT are\nunaffected.</li>\n<li><strong><code>enforce_minimum_key_length</code> set per-call now\ntakes effect.</strong> Callers who passed\n<code>options={&quot;enforce_minimum_key_length&quot;: True}</code> to\n<code>jwt.decode()</code> previously got no enforcement; they will now\nget <code>InvalidKeyError</code> on undersized keys, as documented.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full changelog:</strong> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.1...2.13.0\">https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.1...2.13.0</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/blob/master/CHANGELOG.rst\">pyjwt's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2><code>v2.13.0\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.1...2.13.0&gt;</code>__</h2>\n<p>Security</p>\n<pre><code>\n- Reject JWK JSON documents passed as raw HMAC secrets in\n  ``HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key`` to close an algorithm-confusion gap that\n  the existing PEM/SSH guard did not cover. Reported by @aradona91 in\n`GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx&gt;`__.\n- Bind the JWT header ``alg`` to ``PyJWK.algorithm_name`` during\n  verification so the caller's ``algorithms=[...]`` allow-list cannot be\nbypassed when decoding with a ``PyJWK`` / ``PyJWKClient`` key. Reported\nby @sushi-gif in `GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f&gt;`__.\n- Reject non-``http(s)`` URI schemes in ``PyJWKClient`` so attacker-\ninfluenced URIs cannot read local files or reach unintended schemes via\nurllib's default ``file://`` / ``ftp://`` / ``data:`` handlers. Reported\nby @KEIJOT in `GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4&gt;`__.\n- Preserve the cached JWK Set on fetch errors in\n``PyJWKClient.fetch_data``.\n  The previous ``finally``-block ``put(None)`` pattern cleared the cache\non any transient outage, turning one bad JWKS request into application-\nwide auth failure. Reported by @eddieran in `GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8&gt;`__.\n- Skip the unconditional base64 decode of the compact-form payload\nsegment\n  when ``b64=false`` is set in the protected header, and require that\n  segment to be empty (RFC 7515 Appendix F detached form). Closes an\n  unauthenticated DoS amplifier. Reported by @thesmartshadow in\n`GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39&gt;`__.\n<p>Fixed</p>\n<pre><code>\n- Reject empty HMAC keys outright in ``HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key`` with\n  ``InvalidKeyError`` instead of accepting them with only a warning.\n  Thanks to @SnailSploit and @spartan8806 for independently flagging the\n  footgun.\n- Forward per-call ``options`` (including\n``enforce_minimum_key_length``)\n  from ``PyJWT.decode`` through to ``PyJWS._verify_signature`` so the\noption actually takes effect when set at the call site rather than only\n  on the ``PyJWT`` instance. Thanks to @WLUB for the report.\n- RFC 7797 §3 compliance for ``b64=false``: the encoder now auto-adds\n``&amp;quot;b64&amp;quot;`` to the ``crit`` header parameter, and the\ndecoder rejects\ntokens that set ``b64=false`` without listing it in ``crit``. Thanks to\n  @MachineLearning-Nerd for the report.\n\nChanged\n</code></pre>\n<ul>\n<li>Migrate the <code>dev</code>, <code>docs</code>, and\n<code>tests</code> package extras to dependency groups by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kurtmckee\"><code>@​kurtmckee</code></a> in\n<code>[#1152](https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1152)\n&amp;lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/pull/1152&amp;gt;</code>__\n</code></pre></li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/7144e4534c34810f4525dc4578a32addd8212cff\"><code>7144e45</code></a>\nApply ruff format</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/d2f4bec4963897c0ef96ef64a875894f2c8542ab\"><code>d2f4bec</code></a>\nRestore <code>cast()</code> calls with cross-version <code>type:\nignore</code> for <code>prepare_key</code></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/22f478cebddd8294259c30f037ecb92b0b348774\"><code>22f478c</code></a>\nRemove redundant casts in <code>RSAAlgorithm.prepare_key</code> and\n`ECAlgorithm.prepare...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/95791b1759b8aa4f2203575d344d5c78564cdc81\"><code>95791b1</code></a>\nBundle security fixes and hardening into 2.13.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/dcc27a9d3182a2349c30b160758785c6ce7a6508\"><code>dcc27a9</code></a>\n[pre-commit.ci] pre-commit autoupdate (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1155\">#1155</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/9d08a9a1896845ed8eaf88e6f6ac61e5800c3e7a\"><code>9d08a9a</code></a>\n[pre-commit.ci] pre-commit autoupdate (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1146\">#1146</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/b87c10014d4109f0214fea188d00faaaf8a80e64\"><code>b87c100</code></a>\nBump codecov/codecov-action from 5 to 6 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1154\">#1154</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/40e3147eb5f790d8d041772e5fc00728a176c812\"><code>40e3147</code></a>\nMigrate development extras to dependency groups (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1152\">#1152</a>)</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.1...2.13.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=pyjwt&package-manager=uv&previous-version=2.12.1&new-version=2.13.0)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"57d9928bfa28f999cc7726d085d82910cd210d28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/57d9928bfa28f999cc7726d085d82910cd210d28"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/9b6b9039d98d502e884ccc8eb88e56221819c6ea","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMElbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALzcQACnghK6ZUJOiLDQhsX/zE1Xb\ntLSyjQ8Ar1aEnsdPg58HRxqwngZ4Ls867hSiUbc06Wxq8HRYHUbZp6o+HU4j8pAS\nlAftcCda6lFxjCPo+xGUBXJRJvM9ug4rPlOjuvC4bum9ytDQewiIkWLc7XlyfTDP\nlFq2ubDL2Es1dHbo+/aYkdUmdrR8/vBeVP2dI3H3eCV7lm4hfS+zeseSQvtIzMht\nZjvL+xnLDSdeNjy6C3f6OXrDCKEPOq+N0ogBym7fsgBpRyf1IF1LUgQKuoAuVAGg\nZTI4onuOtwKpyo1iNn2KWJB5mltC7jEalyUH9IQo9xstutX7b1Hl7T2Us+u6eKTQ\nxiANV4p41EUkwuxnNwAstj7PgzrEQo5pxh7zGPcUC099IL46qVYCgeVRrfEDEBLy\nOXly4aKsY8k4Ce1sO2GNQulBcqNLmOKPkQkI3ejVpO72bSjueFsCDx88Nu/2wcWD\neUXLJZ545OIqYRlPD5P840SPH2KNYkpcJgjTn4lKdHspV9bBhlv+6YjCB2XAc6Sk\nJBGufbgaTgeRDIhCU/yNVJBfQUHjiS/Kq4e54+CV2Di+BZM70X3vJyd1slzqcxAI\np9ILoboTBUZUdo1CXc5GI/zuvrsYhfiQLcc89gd4IOlBZ8dMYjy32vffxFnjTJRL\nM9vi7mrzmSpp+j0GDJhX\n=RpvD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 57d9928bfa28f999cc7726d085d82910cd210d28\nparent 5e116e83fa3db1c8acdd0cb163170dbf47c50ec2\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1781549403 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781549403 -0400\n\nchore(deps): bump pyjwt from 2.12.1 to 2.13.0 in /examples/nvidia_deep_agent (#3986)\n\nBumps [pyjwt](https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt) from 2.12.1 to 2.13.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/releases\">pyjwt's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>2.13.0</h2>\n<h1>PyJWT 2.13.0 — Security Release</h1>\n<p>This release bundles five security fixes plus three additional\nhardening / spec-compliance changes. We recommend all users upgrade.</p>\n<h2>Security</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx\"><code>GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx</code></a>\n— JWK JSON accepted as HMAC secret (algorithm confusion).</strong>\n<code>HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key</code> previously rejected PEM- and\nSSH-formatted asymmetric keys but did not catch a JWK passed as a raw\nJSON string. In a verifier configured with both symmetric and asymmetric\nalgorithms in <code>algorithms=[…]</code> and a raw-JSON JWK as the key,\nan attacker could forge HS256 tokens using the JWK text as the HMAC\nsecret. The guard has been extended to reject any JWK-shaped JSON.\n<em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aradona91\"><code>@​aradona91</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f\"><code>GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f</code></a>\n— Algorithm allow-list bypass with <code>PyJWK</code> /\n<code>PyJWKClient</code>.</strong> When verifying with a\n<code>PyJWK</code>, the caller's <code>algorithms=[…]</code> allow-list\nwas checked against the token header <code>alg</code> as a string only;\nactual verification used the algorithm bound to the <code>PyJWK</code>.\nAn attacker who controlled a registered JWKS key could sign with one\nalgorithm and advertise another on the header. PyJWT now requires the\ntoken header <code>alg</code> to match the <code>PyJWK</code>'s\nalgorithm before verification. <em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sushi-gif\"><code>@​sushi-gif</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39\"><code>GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39</code></a>\n— DoS via base64 decode of unused payload segment when\n<code>b64=false</code>.</strong> For detached-payload JWS\n(<code>b64=false</code>), the compact-form payload segment was\nbase64-decoded before being discarded in favor of the caller-supplied\n<code>detached_payload</code>. An attacker could inflate the unused\nsegment to force CPU + memory cost without holding a valid signature.\nThe segment is now required to be empty per RFC 7515 Appendix F, and is\nno longer decoded. <em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/thesmartshadow\"><code>@​thesmartshadow</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4\"><code>GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4</code></a>\n— <code>PyJWKClient</code> accepts non-HTTP(S) URIs.</strong>\n<code>PyJWKClient.fetch_data</code> passed its URI to\n<code>urllib.request.urlopen</code>, which by default also handles\n<code>file://</code>, <code>ftp://</code>, and <code>data:</code>\nschemes. An application that fed an attacker-influenced URI into\n<code>PyJWKClient</code> could be coerced into reading local files or\nreaching other unintended schemes. <code>PyJWKClient</code> now rejects\nany URI whose scheme isn't <code>http</code> or <code>https</code>.\n<em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/KEIJOT\"><code>@​KEIJOT</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8\"><code>GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8</code></a>\n— <code>PyJWKClient</code> cache wiped on fetch error.</strong> A\n<code>finally</code>-block <code>put(jwk_set=None)</code> cleared the\nJWK Set cache whenever a fetch raised, turning a transient JWKS-endpoint\noutage into application-wide auth failure. The cache write was moved\ninto the success path; transient errors no longer evict valid cached\nkeys. <em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/eddieran\"><code>@​eddieran</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Fixed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Reject empty HMAC keys outright in\n<code>HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key</code> with <code>InvalidKeyError</code>\ninstead of accepting them with only a warning. Defends against the\n<code>os.getenv(&quot;JWT_SECRET&quot;, &quot;&quot;)</code> footgun.\n<em>Thanks to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/SnailSploit\"><code>@​SnailSploit</code></a> and\n<a href=\"https://github.com/spartan8806\"><code>@​spartan8806</code></a>\nfor the reports.</em></li>\n<li>Forward per-call <code>options</code> (including\n<code>enforce_minimum_key_length</code>) from <code>PyJWT.decode</code>\nthrough to <code>PyJWS._verify_signature</code>. The option was\npreviously silently dropped between the two layers, so it only took\neffect when set on the <code>PyJWT</code> instance. <em>Thanks to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/WLUB\"><code>@​WLUB</code></a> for the\nreport.</em></li>\n<li><strong>RFC 7797 §3 compliance for <code>b64=false</code>:</strong>\nthe encoder now auto-adds <code>&quot;b64&quot;</code> to\n<code>crit</code>, and the decoder rejects tokens that set\n<code>b64=false</code> without listing it in <code>crit</code>.\n<em>Thanks to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/MachineLearning-Nerd\"><code>@​MachineLearning-Nerd</code></a>\nfor the report.</em></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Migrate the <code>dev</code>, <code>docs</code>, and\n<code>tests</code> package extras to dependency groups, by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kurtmckee\"><code>@​kurtmckee</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/pull/1152\">#1152</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Upgrade notes</h2>\n<p>Most fixes are invisible to correctly-configured callers. A few\nbehavioral changes you may encounter:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Empty HMAC keys now raise.</strong> If your app passed\n<code>&quot;&quot;</code> or <code>b&quot;&quot;</code> as a secret\n(often via a missing env var, e.g.\n<code>os.getenv(&quot;JWT_SECRET&quot;, &quot;&quot;)</code>),\n<code>encode</code>/<code>decode</code> will now raise\n<code>InvalidKeyError</code>. This is the intended behavior — fix the\nconfiguration.</li>\n<li><strong><code>PyJWK</code> decoding now requires the token's\n<code>alg</code> to match the JWK's algorithm.</strong> Previously a\nmismatch was silently honored if the header <code>alg</code> appeared in\nthe allow-list. Tokens that relied on this mismatch will now fail with\n<code>InvalidAlgorithmError</code>.</li>\n<li><strong><code>PyJWKClient</code> now rejects non-HTTP(S) URIs at\nconstruction time.</strong> Tests or dev environments that fetched JWKS\nfrom <code>file://</code> URIs need to switch to a local HTTP server or\nload the JWKS by other means (e.g. construct\n<code>PyJWKSet.from_dict(...)</code> directly).</li>\n<li><strong><code>b64=false</code> tokens are now strictly RFC 7515 /\n7797 compliant.</strong> Tokens with a non-empty compact-form payload\nsegment, or that omit <code>&quot;b64&quot;</code> from\n<code>crit</code>, will be rejected. PyJWT-produced tokens always\nsatisfy both invariants, so round-trips through PyJWT are\nunaffected.</li>\n<li><strong><code>enforce_minimum_key_length</code> set per-call now\ntakes effect.</strong> Callers who passed\n<code>options={&quot;enforce_minimum_key_length&quot;: True}</code> to\n<code>jwt.decode()</code> previously got no enforcement; they will now\nget <code>InvalidKeyError</code> on undersized keys, as documented.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full changelog:</strong> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.1...2.13.0\">https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.1...2.13.0</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/blob/master/CHANGELOG.rst\">pyjwt's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2><code>v2.13.0\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.1...2.13.0&gt;</code>__</h2>\n<p>Security</p>\n<pre><code>\n- Reject JWK JSON documents passed as raw HMAC secrets in\n  ``HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key`` to close an algorithm-confusion gap that\n  the existing PEM/SSH guard did not cover. Reported by @aradona91 in\n`GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx&gt;`__.\n- Bind the JWT header ``alg`` to ``PyJWK.algorithm_name`` during\n  verification so the caller's ``algorithms=[...]`` allow-list cannot be\nbypassed when decoding with a ``PyJWK`` / ``PyJWKClient`` key. Reported\nby @sushi-gif in `GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f&gt;`__.\n- Reject non-``http(s)`` URI schemes in ``PyJWKClient`` so attacker-\ninfluenced URIs cannot read local files or reach unintended schemes via\nurllib's default ``file://`` / ``ftp://`` / ``data:`` handlers. Reported\nby @KEIJOT in `GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4&gt;`__.\n- Preserve the cached JWK Set on fetch errors in\n``PyJWKClient.fetch_data``.\n  The previous ``finally``-block ``put(None)`` pattern cleared the cache\non any transient outage, turning one bad JWKS request into application-\nwide auth failure. Reported by @eddieran in `GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8&gt;`__.\n- Skip the unconditional base64 decode of the compact-form payload\nsegment\n  when ``b64=false`` is set in the protected header, and require that\n  segment to be empty (RFC 7515 Appendix F detached form). Closes an\n  unauthenticated DoS amplifier. Reported by @thesmartshadow in\n`GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39&gt;`__.\n<p>Fixed</p>\n<pre><code>\n- Reject empty HMAC keys outright in ``HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key`` with\n  ``InvalidKeyError`` instead of accepting them with only a warning.\n  Thanks to @SnailSploit and @spartan8806 for independently flagging the\n  footgun.\n- Forward per-call ``options`` (including\n``enforce_minimum_key_length``)\n  from ``PyJWT.decode`` through to ``PyJWS._verify_signature`` so the\noption actually takes effect when set at the call site rather than only\n  on the ``PyJWT`` instance. Thanks to @WLUB for the report.\n- RFC 7797 §3 compliance for ``b64=false``: the encoder now auto-adds\n``&amp;quot;b64&amp;quot;`` to the ``crit`` header parameter, and the\ndecoder rejects\ntokens that set ``b64=false`` without listing it in ``crit``. Thanks to\n  @MachineLearning-Nerd for the report.\n\nChanged\n</code></pre>\n<ul>\n<li>Migrate the <code>dev</code>, <code>docs</code>, and\n<code>tests</code> package extras to dependency groups by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kurtmckee\"><code>@​kurtmckee</code></a> in\n<code>[#1152](https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1152)\n&amp;lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/pull/1152&amp;gt;</code>__\n</code></pre></li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/7144e4534c34810f4525dc4578a32addd8212cff\"><code>7144e45</code></a>\nApply ruff format</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/d2f4bec4963897c0ef96ef64a875894f2c8542ab\"><code>d2f4bec</code></a>\nRestore <code>cast()</code> calls with cross-version <code>type:\nignore</code> for <code>prepare_key</code></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/22f478cebddd8294259c30f037ecb92b0b348774\"><code>22f478c</code></a>\nRemove redundant casts in <code>RSAAlgorithm.prepare_key</code> and\n`ECAlgorithm.prepare...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/95791b1759b8aa4f2203575d344d5c78564cdc81\"><code>95791b1</code></a>\nBundle security fixes and hardening into 2.13.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/dcc27a9d3182a2349c30b160758785c6ce7a6508\"><code>dcc27a9</code></a>\n[pre-commit.ci] pre-commit autoupdate (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1155\">#1155</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/9d08a9a1896845ed8eaf88e6f6ac61e5800c3e7a\"><code>9d08a9a</code></a>\n[pre-commit.ci] pre-commit autoupdate (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1146\">#1146</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/b87c10014d4109f0214fea188d00faaaf8a80e64\"><code>b87c100</code></a>\nBump codecov/codecov-action from 5 to 6 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1154\">#1154</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/40e3147eb5f790d8d041772e5fc00728a176c812\"><code>40e3147</code></a>\nMigrate development extras to dependency groups (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1152\">#1152</a>)</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.1...2.13.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=pyjwt&package-manager=uv&previous-version=2.12.1&new-version=2.13.0)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-15T18:50:03Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9b6b9039d98d502e884ccc8eb88e56221819c6ea","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9b6b9039d98d502e884ccc8eb88e56221819c6ea","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9b6b9039d98d502e884ccc8eb88e56221819c6ea/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5e116e83fa3db1c8acdd0cb163170dbf47c50ec2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5e116e83fa3db1c8acdd0cb163170dbf47c50ec2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5e116e83fa3db1c8acdd0cb163170dbf47c50ec2"}]},{"sha":"5e116e83fa3db1c8acdd0cb163170dbf47c50ec2","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDVlMTE2ZTgzZmEzZGIxYzhhY2RkMGNiMTYzMTcwZGJmNDdjNTBlYzI","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-15T18:49:57Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-15T18:49:57Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump pyjwt from 2.12.1 to 2.13.0 in /examples/deep_research (#3987)\n\nBumps [pyjwt](https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt) from 2.12.1 to 2.13.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/releases\">pyjwt's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>2.13.0</h2>\n<h1>PyJWT 2.13.0 — Security Release</h1>\n<p>This release bundles five security fixes plus three additional\nhardening / spec-compliance changes. We recommend all users upgrade.</p>\n<h2>Security</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx\"><code>GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx</code></a>\n— JWK JSON accepted as HMAC secret (algorithm confusion).</strong>\n<code>HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key</code> previously rejected PEM- and\nSSH-formatted asymmetric keys but did not catch a JWK passed as a raw\nJSON string. In a verifier configured with both symmetric and asymmetric\nalgorithms in <code>algorithms=[…]</code> and a raw-JSON JWK as the key,\nan attacker could forge HS256 tokens using the JWK text as the HMAC\nsecret. The guard has been extended to reject any JWK-shaped JSON.\n<em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aradona91\"><code>@​aradona91</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f\"><code>GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f</code></a>\n— Algorithm allow-list bypass with <code>PyJWK</code> /\n<code>PyJWKClient</code>.</strong> When verifying with a\n<code>PyJWK</code>, the caller's <code>algorithms=[…]</code> allow-list\nwas checked against the token header <code>alg</code> as a string only;\nactual verification used the algorithm bound to the <code>PyJWK</code>.\nAn attacker who controlled a registered JWKS key could sign with one\nalgorithm and advertise another on the header. PyJWT now requires the\ntoken header <code>alg</code> to match the <code>PyJWK</code>'s\nalgorithm before verification. <em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sushi-gif\"><code>@​sushi-gif</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39\"><code>GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39</code></a>\n— DoS via base64 decode of unused payload segment when\n<code>b64=false</code>.</strong> For detached-payload JWS\n(<code>b64=false</code>), the compact-form payload segment was\nbase64-decoded before being discarded in favor of the caller-supplied\n<code>detached_payload</code>. An attacker could inflate the unused\nsegment to force CPU + memory cost without holding a valid signature.\nThe segment is now required to be empty per RFC 7515 Appendix F, and is\nno longer decoded. <em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/thesmartshadow\"><code>@​thesmartshadow</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4\"><code>GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4</code></a>\n— <code>PyJWKClient</code> accepts non-HTTP(S) URIs.</strong>\n<code>PyJWKClient.fetch_data</code> passed its URI to\n<code>urllib.request.urlopen</code>, which by default also handles\n<code>file://</code>, <code>ftp://</code>, and <code>data:</code>\nschemes. An application that fed an attacker-influenced URI into\n<code>PyJWKClient</code> could be coerced into reading local files or\nreaching other unintended schemes. <code>PyJWKClient</code> now rejects\nany URI whose scheme isn't <code>http</code> or <code>https</code>.\n<em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/KEIJOT\"><code>@​KEIJOT</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8\"><code>GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8</code></a>\n— <code>PyJWKClient</code> cache wiped on fetch error.</strong> A\n<code>finally</code>-block <code>put(jwk_set=None)</code> cleared the\nJWK Set cache whenever a fetch raised, turning a transient JWKS-endpoint\noutage into application-wide auth failure. The cache write was moved\ninto the success path; transient errors no longer evict valid cached\nkeys. <em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/eddieran\"><code>@​eddieran</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Fixed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Reject empty HMAC keys outright in\n<code>HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key</code> with <code>InvalidKeyError</code>\ninstead of accepting them with only a warning. Defends against the\n<code>os.getenv(&quot;JWT_SECRET&quot;, &quot;&quot;)</code> footgun.\n<em>Thanks to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/SnailSploit\"><code>@​SnailSploit</code></a> and\n<a href=\"https://github.com/spartan8806\"><code>@​spartan8806</code></a>\nfor the reports.</em></li>\n<li>Forward per-call <code>options</code> (including\n<code>enforce_minimum_key_length</code>) from <code>PyJWT.decode</code>\nthrough to <code>PyJWS._verify_signature</code>. The option was\npreviously silently dropped between the two layers, so it only took\neffect when set on the <code>PyJWT</code> instance. <em>Thanks to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/WLUB\"><code>@​WLUB</code></a> for the\nreport.</em></li>\n<li><strong>RFC 7797 §3 compliance for <code>b64=false</code>:</strong>\nthe encoder now auto-adds <code>&quot;b64&quot;</code> to\n<code>crit</code>, and the decoder rejects tokens that set\n<code>b64=false</code> without listing it in <code>crit</code>.\n<em>Thanks to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/MachineLearning-Nerd\"><code>@​MachineLearning-Nerd</code></a>\nfor the report.</em></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Migrate the <code>dev</code>, <code>docs</code>, and\n<code>tests</code> package extras to dependency groups, by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kurtmckee\"><code>@​kurtmckee</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/pull/1152\">#1152</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Upgrade notes</h2>\n<p>Most fixes are invisible to correctly-configured callers. A few\nbehavioral changes you may encounter:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Empty HMAC keys now raise.</strong> If your app passed\n<code>&quot;&quot;</code> or <code>b&quot;&quot;</code> as a secret\n(often via a missing env var, e.g.\n<code>os.getenv(&quot;JWT_SECRET&quot;, &quot;&quot;)</code>),\n<code>encode</code>/<code>decode</code> will now raise\n<code>InvalidKeyError</code>. This is the intended behavior — fix the\nconfiguration.</li>\n<li><strong><code>PyJWK</code> decoding now requires the token's\n<code>alg</code> to match the JWK's algorithm.</strong> Previously a\nmismatch was silently honored if the header <code>alg</code> appeared in\nthe allow-list. Tokens that relied on this mismatch will now fail with\n<code>InvalidAlgorithmError</code>.</li>\n<li><strong><code>PyJWKClient</code> now rejects non-HTTP(S) URIs at\nconstruction time.</strong> Tests or dev environments that fetched JWKS\nfrom <code>file://</code> URIs need to switch to a local HTTP server or\nload the JWKS by other means (e.g. construct\n<code>PyJWKSet.from_dict(...)</code> directly).</li>\n<li><strong><code>b64=false</code> tokens are now strictly RFC 7515 /\n7797 compliant.</strong> Tokens with a non-empty compact-form payload\nsegment, or that omit <code>&quot;b64&quot;</code> from\n<code>crit</code>, will be rejected. PyJWT-produced tokens always\nsatisfy both invariants, so round-trips through PyJWT are\nunaffected.</li>\n<li><strong><code>enforce_minimum_key_length</code> set per-call now\ntakes effect.</strong> Callers who passed\n<code>options={&quot;enforce_minimum_key_length&quot;: True}</code> to\n<code>jwt.decode()</code> previously got no enforcement; they will now\nget <code>InvalidKeyError</code> on undersized keys, as documented.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full changelog:</strong> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.1...2.13.0\">https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.1...2.13.0</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/blob/master/CHANGELOG.rst\">pyjwt's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2><code>v2.13.0\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.1...2.13.0&gt;</code>__</h2>\n<p>Security</p>\n<pre><code>\n- Reject JWK JSON documents passed as raw HMAC secrets in\n  ``HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key`` to close an algorithm-confusion gap that\n  the existing PEM/SSH guard did not cover. Reported by @aradona91 in\n`GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx&gt;`__.\n- Bind the JWT header ``alg`` to ``PyJWK.algorithm_name`` during\n  verification so the caller's ``algorithms=[...]`` allow-list cannot be\nbypassed when decoding with a ``PyJWK`` / ``PyJWKClient`` key. Reported\nby @sushi-gif in `GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f&gt;`__.\n- Reject non-``http(s)`` URI schemes in ``PyJWKClient`` so attacker-\ninfluenced URIs cannot read local files or reach unintended schemes via\nurllib's default ``file://`` / ``ftp://`` / ``data:`` handlers. Reported\nby @KEIJOT in `GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4&gt;`__.\n- Preserve the cached JWK Set on fetch errors in\n``PyJWKClient.fetch_data``.\n  The previous ``finally``-block ``put(None)`` pattern cleared the cache\non any transient outage, turning one bad JWKS request into application-\nwide auth failure. Reported by @eddieran in `GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8&gt;`__.\n- Skip the unconditional base64 decode of the compact-form payload\nsegment\n  when ``b64=false`` is set in the protected header, and require that\n  segment to be empty (RFC 7515 Appendix F detached form). Closes an\n  unauthenticated DoS amplifier. Reported by @thesmartshadow in\n`GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39&gt;`__.\n<p>Fixed</p>\n<pre><code>\n- Reject empty HMAC keys outright in ``HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key`` with\n  ``InvalidKeyError`` instead of accepting them with only a warning.\n  Thanks to @SnailSploit and @spartan8806 for independently flagging the\n  footgun.\n- Forward per-call ``options`` (including\n``enforce_minimum_key_length``)\n  from ``PyJWT.decode`` through to ``PyJWS._verify_signature`` so the\noption actually takes effect when set at the call site rather than only\n  on the ``PyJWT`` instance. Thanks to @WLUB for the report.\n- RFC 7797 §3 compliance for ``b64=false``: the encoder now auto-adds\n``&amp;quot;b64&amp;quot;`` to the ``crit`` header parameter, and the\ndecoder rejects\ntokens that set ``b64=false`` without listing it in ``crit``. Thanks to\n  @MachineLearning-Nerd for the report.\n\nChanged\n</code></pre>\n<ul>\n<li>Migrate the <code>dev</code>, <code>docs</code>, and\n<code>tests</code> package extras to dependency groups by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kurtmckee\"><code>@​kurtmckee</code></a> in\n<code>[#1152](https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1152)\n&amp;lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/pull/1152&amp;gt;</code>__\n</code></pre></li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/7144e4534c34810f4525dc4578a32addd8212cff\"><code>7144e45</code></a>\nApply ruff format</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/d2f4bec4963897c0ef96ef64a875894f2c8542ab\"><code>d2f4bec</code></a>\nRestore <code>cast()</code> calls with cross-version <code>type:\nignore</code> for <code>prepare_key</code></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/22f478cebddd8294259c30f037ecb92b0b348774\"><code>22f478c</code></a>\nRemove redundant casts in <code>RSAAlgorithm.prepare_key</code> and\n`ECAlgorithm.prepare...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/95791b1759b8aa4f2203575d344d5c78564cdc81\"><code>95791b1</code></a>\nBundle security fixes and hardening into 2.13.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/dcc27a9d3182a2349c30b160758785c6ce7a6508\"><code>dcc27a9</code></a>\n[pre-commit.ci] pre-commit autoupdate (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1155\">#1155</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/9d08a9a1896845ed8eaf88e6f6ac61e5800c3e7a\"><code>9d08a9a</code></a>\n[pre-commit.ci] pre-commit autoupdate (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1146\">#1146</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/b87c10014d4109f0214fea188d00faaaf8a80e64\"><code>b87c100</code></a>\nBump codecov/codecov-action from 5 to 6 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1154\">#1154</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/40e3147eb5f790d8d041772e5fc00728a176c812\"><code>40e3147</code></a>\nMigrate development extras to dependency groups (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1152\">#1152</a>)</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.1...2.13.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=pyjwt&package-manager=uv&previous-version=2.12.1&new-version=2.13.0)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"78f89a2cea5a3d2ff986467ef863435153dee888","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/78f89a2cea5a3d2ff986467ef863435153dee888"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/5e116e83fa3db1c8acdd0cb163170dbf47c50ec2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMElVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbhkQABDO3255cd7bR7Wz5ywHLOoK\nETLmbeIeNEsUtwtEda9uHZYXTEVbXGx+EzLMLy6XsP2Jp0d6ue+1aJUrTjaO6rl8\nxjCEB5z5GiCHyevOlk3MVCz0aUI7yDwmqMN26FgW69z7GOsbgdqxLYDvbRL46f7d\nU4ATog62Tkswx4e6brgeMWw2w6e13jjb6rkeTvJPh28FE2GPYrrYDjL9uqwkVUq+\nnKyTTQzvrms5YEtp4AFNqx6kJy9Wgww1U/Tu0+cCydINVXGDxciyNh2ajtVi5/1A\n8UVqQkWOw85u/rMqET+HVfCiD46dRFEt8nSK8bbME3rFC8OfsNGRfAtgBBxupL+y\noOudVYALprhVI5lvpjcIhRW+3q0CxDGznJHUSZlt/PNcPuZNyCvd0NVM55Q5eUbw\nVUmcNRW1pABmc/doc3h3fTlYyTCZ/6oY4m+tY5IS1AvzS2A3tn7gef5OO9aN6Kw4\n3DvNzRtHoMBt+7h4UUCSWVh6z1HyHeVmNX2a3fK8sRIWV9S2/qnHV2geUBU4GVex\nXaZzbqgfKMwbWAVunn85YujiIjzCWRcLT1oW1174Fy+EcytWj6vO6z0htrUuEjae\nhFkXgd3U7cQ0C7jGrtBMnIRkSYX4CHQA8gNxyEYVj8Inza3ZHbaTa1u+2I+BPyO/\n0Pj/hh5W02y4VjCmzTy2\n=RW7S\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 78f89a2cea5a3d2ff986467ef863435153dee888\nparent 79a7928aeb39fc682e83c42fb2a9bfa80f387978\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1781549397 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781549397 -0400\n\nchore(deps): bump pyjwt from 2.12.1 to 2.13.0 in /examples/deep_research (#3987)\n\nBumps [pyjwt](https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt) from 2.12.1 to 2.13.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/releases\">pyjwt's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>2.13.0</h2>\n<h1>PyJWT 2.13.0 — Security Release</h1>\n<p>This release bundles five security fixes plus three additional\nhardening / spec-compliance changes. We recommend all users upgrade.</p>\n<h2>Security</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx\"><code>GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx</code></a>\n— JWK JSON accepted as HMAC secret (algorithm confusion).</strong>\n<code>HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key</code> previously rejected PEM- and\nSSH-formatted asymmetric keys but did not catch a JWK passed as a raw\nJSON string. In a verifier configured with both symmetric and asymmetric\nalgorithms in <code>algorithms=[…]</code> and a raw-JSON JWK as the key,\nan attacker could forge HS256 tokens using the JWK text as the HMAC\nsecret. The guard has been extended to reject any JWK-shaped JSON.\n<em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aradona91\"><code>@​aradona91</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f\"><code>GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f</code></a>\n— Algorithm allow-list bypass with <code>PyJWK</code> /\n<code>PyJWKClient</code>.</strong> When verifying with a\n<code>PyJWK</code>, the caller's <code>algorithms=[…]</code> allow-list\nwas checked against the token header <code>alg</code> as a string only;\nactual verification used the algorithm bound to the <code>PyJWK</code>.\nAn attacker who controlled a registered JWKS key could sign with one\nalgorithm and advertise another on the header. PyJWT now requires the\ntoken header <code>alg</code> to match the <code>PyJWK</code>'s\nalgorithm before verification. <em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sushi-gif\"><code>@​sushi-gif</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39\"><code>GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39</code></a>\n— DoS via base64 decode of unused payload segment when\n<code>b64=false</code>.</strong> For detached-payload JWS\n(<code>b64=false</code>), the compact-form payload segment was\nbase64-decoded before being discarded in favor of the caller-supplied\n<code>detached_payload</code>. An attacker could inflate the unused\nsegment to force CPU + memory cost without holding a valid signature.\nThe segment is now required to be empty per RFC 7515 Appendix F, and is\nno longer decoded. <em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/thesmartshadow\"><code>@​thesmartshadow</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4\"><code>GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4</code></a>\n— <code>PyJWKClient</code> accepts non-HTTP(S) URIs.</strong>\n<code>PyJWKClient.fetch_data</code> passed its URI to\n<code>urllib.request.urlopen</code>, which by default also handles\n<code>file://</code>, <code>ftp://</code>, and <code>data:</code>\nschemes. An application that fed an attacker-influenced URI into\n<code>PyJWKClient</code> could be coerced into reading local files or\nreaching other unintended schemes. <code>PyJWKClient</code> now rejects\nany URI whose scheme isn't <code>http</code> or <code>https</code>.\n<em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/KEIJOT\"><code>@​KEIJOT</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8\"><code>GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8</code></a>\n— <code>PyJWKClient</code> cache wiped on fetch error.</strong> A\n<code>finally</code>-block <code>put(jwk_set=None)</code> cleared the\nJWK Set cache whenever a fetch raised, turning a transient JWKS-endpoint\noutage into application-wide auth failure. The cache write was moved\ninto the success path; transient errors no longer evict valid cached\nkeys. <em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/eddieran\"><code>@​eddieran</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Fixed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Reject empty HMAC keys outright in\n<code>HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key</code> with <code>InvalidKeyError</code>\ninstead of accepting them with only a warning. Defends against the\n<code>os.getenv(&quot;JWT_SECRET&quot;, &quot;&quot;)</code> footgun.\n<em>Thanks to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/SnailSploit\"><code>@​SnailSploit</code></a> and\n<a href=\"https://github.com/spartan8806\"><code>@​spartan8806</code></a>\nfor the reports.</em></li>\n<li>Forward per-call <code>options</code> (including\n<code>enforce_minimum_key_length</code>) from <code>PyJWT.decode</code>\nthrough to <code>PyJWS._verify_signature</code>. The option was\npreviously silently dropped between the two layers, so it only took\neffect when set on the <code>PyJWT</code> instance. <em>Thanks to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/WLUB\"><code>@​WLUB</code></a> for the\nreport.</em></li>\n<li><strong>RFC 7797 §3 compliance for <code>b64=false</code>:</strong>\nthe encoder now auto-adds <code>&quot;b64&quot;</code> to\n<code>crit</code>, and the decoder rejects tokens that set\n<code>b64=false</code> without listing it in <code>crit</code>.\n<em>Thanks to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/MachineLearning-Nerd\"><code>@​MachineLearning-Nerd</code></a>\nfor the report.</em></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Migrate the <code>dev</code>, <code>docs</code>, and\n<code>tests</code> package extras to dependency groups, by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kurtmckee\"><code>@​kurtmckee</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/pull/1152\">#1152</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Upgrade notes</h2>\n<p>Most fixes are invisible to correctly-configured callers. A few\nbehavioral changes you may encounter:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Empty HMAC keys now raise.</strong> If your app passed\n<code>&quot;&quot;</code> or <code>b&quot;&quot;</code> as a secret\n(often via a missing env var, e.g.\n<code>os.getenv(&quot;JWT_SECRET&quot;, &quot;&quot;)</code>),\n<code>encode</code>/<code>decode</code> will now raise\n<code>InvalidKeyError</code>. This is the intended behavior — fix the\nconfiguration.</li>\n<li><strong><code>PyJWK</code> decoding now requires the token's\n<code>alg</code> to match the JWK's algorithm.</strong> Previously a\nmismatch was silently honored if the header <code>alg</code> appeared in\nthe allow-list. Tokens that relied on this mismatch will now fail with\n<code>InvalidAlgorithmError</code>.</li>\n<li><strong><code>PyJWKClient</code> now rejects non-HTTP(S) URIs at\nconstruction time.</strong> Tests or dev environments that fetched JWKS\nfrom <code>file://</code> URIs need to switch to a local HTTP server or\nload the JWKS by other means (e.g. construct\n<code>PyJWKSet.from_dict(...)</code> directly).</li>\n<li><strong><code>b64=false</code> tokens are now strictly RFC 7515 /\n7797 compliant.</strong> Tokens with a non-empty compact-form payload\nsegment, or that omit <code>&quot;b64&quot;</code> from\n<code>crit</code>, will be rejected. PyJWT-produced tokens always\nsatisfy both invariants, so round-trips through PyJWT are\nunaffected.</li>\n<li><strong><code>enforce_minimum_key_length</code> set per-call now\ntakes effect.</strong> Callers who passed\n<code>options={&quot;enforce_minimum_key_length&quot;: True}</code> to\n<code>jwt.decode()</code> previously got no enforcement; they will now\nget <code>InvalidKeyError</code> on undersized keys, as documented.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full changelog:</strong> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.1...2.13.0\">https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.1...2.13.0</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/blob/master/CHANGELOG.rst\">pyjwt's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2><code>v2.13.0\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.1...2.13.0&gt;</code>__</h2>\n<p>Security</p>\n<pre><code>\n- Reject JWK JSON documents passed as raw HMAC secrets in\n  ``HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key`` to close an algorithm-confusion gap that\n  the existing PEM/SSH guard did not cover. Reported by @aradona91 in\n`GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx&gt;`__.\n- Bind the JWT header ``alg`` to ``PyJWK.algorithm_name`` during\n  verification so the caller's ``algorithms=[...]`` allow-list cannot be\nbypassed when decoding with a ``PyJWK`` / ``PyJWKClient`` key. Reported\nby @sushi-gif in `GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f&gt;`__.\n- Reject non-``http(s)`` URI schemes in ``PyJWKClient`` so attacker-\ninfluenced URIs cannot read local files or reach unintended schemes via\nurllib's default ``file://`` / ``ftp://`` / ``data:`` handlers. Reported\nby @KEIJOT in `GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4&gt;`__.\n- Preserve the cached JWK Set on fetch errors in\n``PyJWKClient.fetch_data``.\n  The previous ``finally``-block ``put(None)`` pattern cleared the cache\non any transient outage, turning one bad JWKS request into application-\nwide auth failure. Reported by @eddieran in `GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8&gt;`__.\n- Skip the unconditional base64 decode of the compact-form payload\nsegment\n  when ``b64=false`` is set in the protected header, and require that\n  segment to be empty (RFC 7515 Appendix F detached form). Closes an\n  unauthenticated DoS amplifier. Reported by @thesmartshadow in\n`GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39&gt;`__.\n<p>Fixed</p>\n<pre><code>\n- Reject empty HMAC keys outright in ``HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key`` with\n  ``InvalidKeyError`` instead of accepting them with only a warning.\n  Thanks to @SnailSploit and @spartan8806 for independently flagging the\n  footgun.\n- Forward per-call ``options`` (including\n``enforce_minimum_key_length``)\n  from ``PyJWT.decode`` through to ``PyJWS._verify_signature`` so the\noption actually takes effect when set at the call site rather than only\n  on the ``PyJWT`` instance. Thanks to @WLUB for the report.\n- RFC 7797 §3 compliance for ``b64=false``: the encoder now auto-adds\n``&amp;quot;b64&amp;quot;`` to the ``crit`` header parameter, and the\ndecoder rejects\ntokens that set ``b64=false`` without listing it in ``crit``. Thanks to\n  @MachineLearning-Nerd for the report.\n\nChanged\n</code></pre>\n<ul>\n<li>Migrate the <code>dev</code>, <code>docs</code>, and\n<code>tests</code> package extras to dependency groups by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kurtmckee\"><code>@​kurtmckee</code></a> in\n<code>[#1152](https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1152)\n&amp;lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/pull/1152&amp;gt;</code>__\n</code></pre></li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/7144e4534c34810f4525dc4578a32addd8212cff\"><code>7144e45</code></a>\nApply ruff format</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/d2f4bec4963897c0ef96ef64a875894f2c8542ab\"><code>d2f4bec</code></a>\nRestore <code>cast()</code> calls with cross-version <code>type:\nignore</code> for <code>prepare_key</code></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/22f478cebddd8294259c30f037ecb92b0b348774\"><code>22f478c</code></a>\nRemove redundant casts in <code>RSAAlgorithm.prepare_key</code> and\n`ECAlgorithm.prepare...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/95791b1759b8aa4f2203575d344d5c78564cdc81\"><code>95791b1</code></a>\nBundle security fixes and hardening into 2.13.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/dcc27a9d3182a2349c30b160758785c6ce7a6508\"><code>dcc27a9</code></a>\n[pre-commit.ci] pre-commit autoupdate (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1155\">#1155</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/9d08a9a1896845ed8eaf88e6f6ac61e5800c3e7a\"><code>9d08a9a</code></a>\n[pre-commit.ci] pre-commit autoupdate (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1146\">#1146</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/b87c10014d4109f0214fea188d00faaaf8a80e64\"><code>b87c100</code></a>\nBump codecov/codecov-action from 5 to 6 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1154\">#1154</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/40e3147eb5f790d8d041772e5fc00728a176c812\"><code>40e3147</code></a>\nMigrate development extras to dependency groups (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1152\">#1152</a>)</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.1...2.13.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=pyjwt&package-manager=uv&previous-version=2.12.1&new-version=2.13.0)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-15T18:49:57Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5e116e83fa3db1c8acdd0cb163170dbf47c50ec2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5e116e83fa3db1c8acdd0cb163170dbf47c50ec2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5e116e83fa3db1c8acdd0cb163170dbf47c50ec2/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"79a7928aeb39fc682e83c42fb2a9bfa80f387978","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/79a7928aeb39fc682e83c42fb2a9bfa80f387978","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/79a7928aeb39fc682e83c42fb2a9bfa80f387978"}]},{"sha":"79a7928aeb39fc682e83c42fb2a9bfa80f387978","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDc5YTc5MjhhZWIzOWZjNjgyZTgzYzQyZmIyYTliZmE4MGYzODc5Nzg","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-15T17:52:49Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-15T17:52:49Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump pyjwt from 2.12.1 to 2.13.0 in /libs/evals (#3984)\n\nBumps [pyjwt](https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt) from 2.12.1 to 2.13.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/releases\">pyjwt's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>2.13.0</h2>\n<h1>PyJWT 2.13.0 — Security Release</h1>\n<p>This release bundles five security fixes plus three additional\nhardening / spec-compliance changes. We recommend all users upgrade.</p>\n<h2>Security</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx\"><code>GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx</code></a>\n— JWK JSON accepted as HMAC secret (algorithm confusion).</strong>\n<code>HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key</code> previously rejected PEM- and\nSSH-formatted asymmetric keys but did not catch a JWK passed as a raw\nJSON string. In a verifier configured with both symmetric and asymmetric\nalgorithms in <code>algorithms=[…]</code> and a raw-JSON JWK as the key,\nan attacker could forge HS256 tokens using the JWK text as the HMAC\nsecret. The guard has been extended to reject any JWK-shaped JSON.\n<em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aradona91\"><code>@​aradona91</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f\"><code>GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f</code></a>\n— Algorithm allow-list bypass with <code>PyJWK</code> /\n<code>PyJWKClient</code>.</strong> When verifying with a\n<code>PyJWK</code>, the caller's <code>algorithms=[…]</code> allow-list\nwas checked against the token header <code>alg</code> as a string only;\nactual verification used the algorithm bound to the <code>PyJWK</code>.\nAn attacker who controlled a registered JWKS key could sign with one\nalgorithm and advertise another on the header. PyJWT now requires the\ntoken header <code>alg</code> to match the <code>PyJWK</code>'s\nalgorithm before verification. <em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sushi-gif\"><code>@​sushi-gif</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39\"><code>GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39</code></a>\n— DoS via base64 decode of unused payload segment when\n<code>b64=false</code>.</strong> For detached-payload JWS\n(<code>b64=false</code>), the compact-form payload segment was\nbase64-decoded before being discarded in favor of the caller-supplied\n<code>detached_payload</code>. An attacker could inflate the unused\nsegment to force CPU + memory cost without holding a valid signature.\nThe segment is now required to be empty per RFC 7515 Appendix F, and is\nno longer decoded. <em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/thesmartshadow\"><code>@​thesmartshadow</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4\"><code>GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4</code></a>\n— <code>PyJWKClient</code> accepts non-HTTP(S) URIs.</strong>\n<code>PyJWKClient.fetch_data</code> passed its URI to\n<code>urllib.request.urlopen</code>, which by default also handles\n<code>file://</code>, <code>ftp://</code>, and <code>data:</code>\nschemes. An application that fed an attacker-influenced URI into\n<code>PyJWKClient</code> could be coerced into reading local files or\nreaching other unintended schemes. <code>PyJWKClient</code> now rejects\nany URI whose scheme isn't <code>http</code> or <code>https</code>.\n<em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/KEIJOT\"><code>@​KEIJOT</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8\"><code>GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8</code></a>\n— <code>PyJWKClient</code> cache wiped on fetch error.</strong> A\n<code>finally</code>-block <code>put(jwk_set=None)</code> cleared the\nJWK Set cache whenever a fetch raised, turning a transient JWKS-endpoint\noutage into application-wide auth failure. The cache write was moved\ninto the success path; transient errors no longer evict valid cached\nkeys. <em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/eddieran\"><code>@​eddieran</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Fixed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Reject empty HMAC keys outright in\n<code>HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key</code> with <code>InvalidKeyError</code>\ninstead of accepting them with only a warning. Defends against the\n<code>os.getenv(&quot;JWT_SECRET&quot;, &quot;&quot;)</code> footgun.\n<em>Thanks to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/SnailSploit\"><code>@​SnailSploit</code></a> and\n<a href=\"https://github.com/spartan8806\"><code>@​spartan8806</code></a>\nfor the reports.</em></li>\n<li>Forward per-call <code>options</code> (including\n<code>enforce_minimum_key_length</code>) from <code>PyJWT.decode</code>\nthrough to <code>PyJWS._verify_signature</code>. The option was\npreviously silently dropped between the two layers, so it only took\neffect when set on the <code>PyJWT</code> instance. <em>Thanks to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/WLUB\"><code>@​WLUB</code></a> for the\nreport.</em></li>\n<li><strong>RFC 7797 §3 compliance for <code>b64=false</code>:</strong>\nthe encoder now auto-adds <code>&quot;b64&quot;</code> to\n<code>crit</code>, and the decoder rejects tokens that set\n<code>b64=false</code> without listing it in <code>crit</code>.\n<em>Thanks to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/MachineLearning-Nerd\"><code>@​MachineLearning-Nerd</code></a>\nfor the report.</em></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Migrate the <code>dev</code>, <code>docs</code>, and\n<code>tests</code> package extras to dependency groups, by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kurtmckee\"><code>@​kurtmckee</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/pull/1152\">#1152</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Upgrade notes</h2>\n<p>Most fixes are invisible to correctly-configured callers. A few\nbehavioral changes you may encounter:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Empty HMAC keys now raise.</strong> If your app passed\n<code>&quot;&quot;</code> or <code>b&quot;&quot;</code> as a secret\n(often via a missing env var, e.g.\n<code>os.getenv(&quot;JWT_SECRET&quot;, &quot;&quot;)</code>),\n<code>encode</code>/<code>decode</code> will now raise\n<code>InvalidKeyError</code>. This is the intended behavior — fix the\nconfiguration.</li>\n<li><strong><code>PyJWK</code> decoding now requires the token's\n<code>alg</code> to match the JWK's algorithm.</strong> Previously a\nmismatch was silently honored if the header <code>alg</code> appeared in\nthe allow-list. Tokens that relied on this mismatch will now fail with\n<code>InvalidAlgorithmError</code>.</li>\n<li><strong><code>PyJWKClient</code> now rejects non-HTTP(S) URIs at\nconstruction time.</strong> Tests or dev environments that fetched JWKS\nfrom <code>file://</code> URIs need to switch to a local HTTP server or\nload the JWKS by other means (e.g. construct\n<code>PyJWKSet.from_dict(...)</code> directly).</li>\n<li><strong><code>b64=false</code> tokens are now strictly RFC 7515 /\n7797 compliant.</strong> Tokens with a non-empty compact-form payload\nsegment, or that omit <code>&quot;b64&quot;</code> from\n<code>crit</code>, will be rejected. PyJWT-produced tokens always\nsatisfy both invariants, so round-trips through PyJWT are\nunaffected.</li>\n<li><strong><code>enforce_minimum_key_length</code> set per-call now\ntakes effect.</strong> Callers who passed\n<code>options={&quot;enforce_minimum_key_length&quot;: True}</code> to\n<code>jwt.decode()</code> previously got no enforcement; they will now\nget <code>InvalidKeyError</code> on undersized keys, as documented.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full changelog:</strong> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.1...2.13.0\">https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.1...2.13.0</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/blob/master/CHANGELOG.rst\">pyjwt's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2><code>v2.13.0\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.1...2.13.0&gt;</code>__</h2>\n<p>Security</p>\n<pre><code>\n- Reject JWK JSON documents passed as raw HMAC secrets in\n  ``HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key`` to close an algorithm-confusion gap that\n  the existing PEM/SSH guard did not cover. Reported by @aradona91 in\n`GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx&gt;`__.\n- Bind the JWT header ``alg`` to ``PyJWK.algorithm_name`` during\n  verification so the caller's ``algorithms=[...]`` allow-list cannot be\nbypassed when decoding with a ``PyJWK`` / ``PyJWKClient`` key. Reported\nby @sushi-gif in `GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f&gt;`__.\n- Reject non-``http(s)`` URI schemes in ``PyJWKClient`` so attacker-\ninfluenced URIs cannot read local files or reach unintended schemes via\nurllib's default ``file://`` / ``ftp://`` / ``data:`` handlers. Reported\nby @KEIJOT in `GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4&gt;`__.\n- Preserve the cached JWK Set on fetch errors in\n``PyJWKClient.fetch_data``.\n  The previous ``finally``-block ``put(None)`` pattern cleared the cache\non any transient outage, turning one bad JWKS request into application-\nwide auth failure. Reported by @eddieran in `GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8&gt;`__.\n- Skip the unconditional base64 decode of the compact-form payload\nsegment\n  when ``b64=false`` is set in the protected header, and require that\n  segment to be empty (RFC 7515 Appendix F detached form). Closes an\n  unauthenticated DoS amplifier. Reported by @thesmartshadow in\n`GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39&gt;`__.\n<p>Fixed</p>\n<pre><code>\n- Reject empty HMAC keys outright in ``HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key`` with\n  ``InvalidKeyError`` instead of accepting them with only a warning.\n  Thanks to @SnailSploit and @spartan8806 for independently flagging the\n  footgun.\n- Forward per-call ``options`` (including\n``enforce_minimum_key_length``)\n  from ``PyJWT.decode`` through to ``PyJWS._verify_signature`` so the\noption actually takes effect when set at the call site rather than only\n  on the ``PyJWT`` instance. Thanks to @WLUB for the report.\n- RFC 7797 §3 compliance for ``b64=false``: the encoder now auto-adds\n``&amp;quot;b64&amp;quot;`` to the ``crit`` header parameter, and the\ndecoder rejects\ntokens that set ``b64=false`` without listing it in ``crit``. Thanks to\n  @MachineLearning-Nerd for the report.\n\nChanged\n</code></pre>\n<ul>\n<li>Migrate the <code>dev</code>, <code>docs</code>, and\n<code>tests</code> package extras to dependency groups by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kurtmckee\"><code>@​kurtmckee</code></a> in\n<code>[#1152](https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1152)\n&amp;lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/pull/1152&amp;gt;</code>__\n</code></pre></li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/7144e4534c34810f4525dc4578a32addd8212cff\"><code>7144e45</code></a>\nApply ruff format</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/d2f4bec4963897c0ef96ef64a875894f2c8542ab\"><code>d2f4bec</code></a>\nRestore <code>cast()</code> calls with cross-version <code>type:\nignore</code> for <code>prepare_key</code></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/22f478cebddd8294259c30f037ecb92b0b348774\"><code>22f478c</code></a>\nRemove redundant casts in <code>RSAAlgorithm.prepare_key</code> and\n`ECAlgorithm.prepare...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/95791b1759b8aa4f2203575d344d5c78564cdc81\"><code>95791b1</code></a>\nBundle security fixes and hardening into 2.13.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/dcc27a9d3182a2349c30b160758785c6ce7a6508\"><code>dcc27a9</code></a>\n[pre-commit.ci] pre-commit autoupdate (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1155\">#1155</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/9d08a9a1896845ed8eaf88e6f6ac61e5800c3e7a\"><code>9d08a9a</code></a>\n[pre-commit.ci] pre-commit autoupdate (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1146\">#1146</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/b87c10014d4109f0214fea188d00faaaf8a80e64\"><code>b87c100</code></a>\nBump codecov/codecov-action from 5 to 6 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1154\">#1154</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/40e3147eb5f790d8d041772e5fc00728a176c812\"><code>40e3147</code></a>\nMigrate development extras to dependency groups (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1152\">#1152</a>)</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.1...2.13.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=pyjwt&package-manager=uv&previous-version=2.12.1&new-version=2.13.0)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"60f4ac8ef8af4332fd0aefeea9687e1b25eb7aa2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/60f4ac8ef8af4332fd0aefeea9687e1b25eb7aa2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/79a7928aeb39fc682e83c42fb2a9bfa80f387978","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMDvxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADkgQAEJrwdWL8+KuUodOYOdPIohI\nwtL6FSUbNSmnCJpUazY8xBiqZlmu7NJ1JuXk0JZoY8kjKwm4ns3590wVKyqtRpr4\nYOtEB2LSOkWWl5QwPk0o+pcLJYnJ+zGBncJgAJ+pJiln+J3XzTE+qeHCjuyk2+GA\nIBiT9OxDzFbCFNyjS++LimVAnnlf7mH1dg3xmXZcpJuit9MnvOpdTjC+i9Xe5y3Q\npK/Nl9rVGPhwcCe7bd3Hw50k//Rcz4e0yQk1/lBpYzoTINzx3tf3oZ3CieFEB9Cy\nt6kHvTOVkaUtcUpVTxjmI2IORoYI228nw/7I3v5EuzuKAPQNlbrf4vZpLhP5abtL\nJgtFYiPjFigteqIeBSaHcsiPrKWXqlOTAoS024rA03rRWgeenMUQmmzArzHFlD3n\nNUGAbz1vNDxpNTIcsO380lXZcJDhFmCe6yt9KJHJH2J/JXab7/tjvJ1UUbdN5ix/\nHNJfXtBF8kCdQUHUECJm9mGz0tY/5E9NgDoMI3IyTCSnIZSKzZpDTP4Sl1RZKT73\nvHlOC0lYMwKgsD53bu4qpmxozG5AiDFAQYi8S7+sgGZkWvR2Yxx0sF4usH4mirFI\ngyEyNlFn/TF9J7z+fb3T2mvWjhu9k1Ltvmvm5U8701lG+io0HhTxp5HsHkKpIkZ+\n2IVGU4gqncgN4AtjlkBe\n=H2kx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 60f4ac8ef8af4332fd0aefeea9687e1b25eb7aa2\nparent ad41f06719cbf0e51b0dbc318ac36b79d252be04\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1781545969 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781545969 -0400\n\nchore(deps): bump pyjwt from 2.12.1 to 2.13.0 in /libs/evals (#3984)\n\nBumps [pyjwt](https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt) from 2.12.1 to 2.13.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/releases\">pyjwt's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>2.13.0</h2>\n<h1>PyJWT 2.13.0 — Security Release</h1>\n<p>This release bundles five security fixes plus three additional\nhardening / spec-compliance changes. We recommend all users upgrade.</p>\n<h2>Security</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx\"><code>GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx</code></a>\n— JWK JSON accepted as HMAC secret (algorithm confusion).</strong>\n<code>HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key</code> previously rejected PEM- and\nSSH-formatted asymmetric keys but did not catch a JWK passed as a raw\nJSON string. In a verifier configured with both symmetric and asymmetric\nalgorithms in <code>algorithms=[…]</code> and a raw-JSON JWK as the key,\nan attacker could forge HS256 tokens using the JWK text as the HMAC\nsecret. The guard has been extended to reject any JWK-shaped JSON.\n<em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aradona91\"><code>@​aradona91</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f\"><code>GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f</code></a>\n— Algorithm allow-list bypass with <code>PyJWK</code> /\n<code>PyJWKClient</code>.</strong> When verifying with a\n<code>PyJWK</code>, the caller's <code>algorithms=[…]</code> allow-list\nwas checked against the token header <code>alg</code> as a string only;\nactual verification used the algorithm bound to the <code>PyJWK</code>.\nAn attacker who controlled a registered JWKS key could sign with one\nalgorithm and advertise another on the header. PyJWT now requires the\ntoken header <code>alg</code> to match the <code>PyJWK</code>'s\nalgorithm before verification. <em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sushi-gif\"><code>@​sushi-gif</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39\"><code>GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39</code></a>\n— DoS via base64 decode of unused payload segment when\n<code>b64=false</code>.</strong> For detached-payload JWS\n(<code>b64=false</code>), the compact-form payload segment was\nbase64-decoded before being discarded in favor of the caller-supplied\n<code>detached_payload</code>. An attacker could inflate the unused\nsegment to force CPU + memory cost without holding a valid signature.\nThe segment is now required to be empty per RFC 7515 Appendix F, and is\nno longer decoded. <em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/thesmartshadow\"><code>@​thesmartshadow</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4\"><code>GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4</code></a>\n— <code>PyJWKClient</code> accepts non-HTTP(S) URIs.</strong>\n<code>PyJWKClient.fetch_data</code> passed its URI to\n<code>urllib.request.urlopen</code>, which by default also handles\n<code>file://</code>, <code>ftp://</code>, and <code>data:</code>\nschemes. An application that fed an attacker-influenced URI into\n<code>PyJWKClient</code> could be coerced into reading local files or\nreaching other unintended schemes. <code>PyJWKClient</code> now rejects\nany URI whose scheme isn't <code>http</code> or <code>https</code>.\n<em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/KEIJOT\"><code>@​KEIJOT</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8\"><code>GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8</code></a>\n— <code>PyJWKClient</code> cache wiped on fetch error.</strong> A\n<code>finally</code>-block <code>put(jwk_set=None)</code> cleared the\nJWK Set cache whenever a fetch raised, turning a transient JWKS-endpoint\noutage into application-wide auth failure. The cache write was moved\ninto the success path; transient errors no longer evict valid cached\nkeys. <em>Reported by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/eddieran\"><code>@​eddieran</code></a>.</em></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Fixed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Reject empty HMAC keys outright in\n<code>HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key</code> with <code>InvalidKeyError</code>\ninstead of accepting them with only a warning. Defends against the\n<code>os.getenv(&quot;JWT_SECRET&quot;, &quot;&quot;)</code> footgun.\n<em>Thanks to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/SnailSploit\"><code>@​SnailSploit</code></a> and\n<a href=\"https://github.com/spartan8806\"><code>@​spartan8806</code></a>\nfor the reports.</em></li>\n<li>Forward per-call <code>options</code> (including\n<code>enforce_minimum_key_length</code>) from <code>PyJWT.decode</code>\nthrough to <code>PyJWS._verify_signature</code>. The option was\npreviously silently dropped between the two layers, so it only took\neffect when set on the <code>PyJWT</code> instance. <em>Thanks to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/WLUB\"><code>@​WLUB</code></a> for the\nreport.</em></li>\n<li><strong>RFC 7797 §3 compliance for <code>b64=false</code>:</strong>\nthe encoder now auto-adds <code>&quot;b64&quot;</code> to\n<code>crit</code>, and the decoder rejects tokens that set\n<code>b64=false</code> without listing it in <code>crit</code>.\n<em>Thanks to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/MachineLearning-Nerd\"><code>@​MachineLearning-Nerd</code></a>\nfor the report.</em></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Migrate the <code>dev</code>, <code>docs</code>, and\n<code>tests</code> package extras to dependency groups, by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kurtmckee\"><code>@​kurtmckee</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/pull/1152\">#1152</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Upgrade notes</h2>\n<p>Most fixes are invisible to correctly-configured callers. A few\nbehavioral changes you may encounter:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Empty HMAC keys now raise.</strong> If your app passed\n<code>&quot;&quot;</code> or <code>b&quot;&quot;</code> as a secret\n(often via a missing env var, e.g.\n<code>os.getenv(&quot;JWT_SECRET&quot;, &quot;&quot;)</code>),\n<code>encode</code>/<code>decode</code> will now raise\n<code>InvalidKeyError</code>. This is the intended behavior — fix the\nconfiguration.</li>\n<li><strong><code>PyJWK</code> decoding now requires the token's\n<code>alg</code> to match the JWK's algorithm.</strong> Previously a\nmismatch was silently honored if the header <code>alg</code> appeared in\nthe allow-list. Tokens that relied on this mismatch will now fail with\n<code>InvalidAlgorithmError</code>.</li>\n<li><strong><code>PyJWKClient</code> now rejects non-HTTP(S) URIs at\nconstruction time.</strong> Tests or dev environments that fetched JWKS\nfrom <code>file://</code> URIs need to switch to a local HTTP server or\nload the JWKS by other means (e.g. construct\n<code>PyJWKSet.from_dict(...)</code> directly).</li>\n<li><strong><code>b64=false</code> tokens are now strictly RFC 7515 /\n7797 compliant.</strong> Tokens with a non-empty compact-form payload\nsegment, or that omit <code>&quot;b64&quot;</code> from\n<code>crit</code>, will be rejected. PyJWT-produced tokens always\nsatisfy both invariants, so round-trips through PyJWT are\nunaffected.</li>\n<li><strong><code>enforce_minimum_key_length</code> set per-call now\ntakes effect.</strong> Callers who passed\n<code>options={&quot;enforce_minimum_key_length&quot;: True}</code> to\n<code>jwt.decode()</code> previously got no enforcement; they will now\nget <code>InvalidKeyError</code> on undersized keys, as documented.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full changelog:</strong> <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.1...2.13.0\">https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.1...2.13.0</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/blob/master/CHANGELOG.rst\">pyjwt's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2><code>v2.13.0\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.1...2.13.0&gt;</code>__</h2>\n<p>Security</p>\n<pre><code>\n- Reject JWK JSON documents passed as raw HMAC secrets in\n  ``HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key`` to close an algorithm-confusion gap that\n  the existing PEM/SSH guard did not cover. Reported by @aradona91 in\n`GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx&gt;`__.\n- Bind the JWT header ``alg`` to ``PyJWK.algorithm_name`` during\n  verification so the caller's ``algorithms=[...]`` allow-list cannot be\nbypassed when decoding with a ``PyJWK`` / ``PyJWKClient`` key. Reported\nby @sushi-gif in `GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f&gt;`__.\n- Reject non-``http(s)`` URI schemes in ``PyJWKClient`` so attacker-\ninfluenced URIs cannot read local files or reach unintended schemes via\nurllib's default ``file://`` / ``ftp://`` / ``data:`` handlers. Reported\nby @KEIJOT in `GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4&gt;`__.\n- Preserve the cached JWK Set on fetch errors in\n``PyJWKClient.fetch_data``.\n  The previous ``finally``-block ``put(None)`` pattern cleared the cache\non any transient outage, turning one bad JWKS request into application-\nwide auth failure. Reported by @eddieran in `GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-fhv5-28vv-h8m8&gt;`__.\n- Skip the unconditional base64 decode of the compact-form payload\nsegment\n  when ``b64=false`` is set in the protected header, and require that\n  segment to be empty (RFC 7515 Appendix F detached form). Closes an\n  unauthenticated DoS amplifier. Reported by @thesmartshadow in\n`GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39\n&lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39&gt;`__.\n<p>Fixed</p>\n<pre><code>\n- Reject empty HMAC keys outright in ``HMACAlgorithm.prepare_key`` with\n  ``InvalidKeyError`` instead of accepting them with only a warning.\n  Thanks to @SnailSploit and @spartan8806 for independently flagging the\n  footgun.\n- Forward per-call ``options`` (including\n``enforce_minimum_key_length``)\n  from ``PyJWT.decode`` through to ``PyJWS._verify_signature`` so the\noption actually takes effect when set at the call site rather than only\n  on the ``PyJWT`` instance. Thanks to @WLUB for the report.\n- RFC 7797 §3 compliance for ``b64=false``: the encoder now auto-adds\n``&amp;quot;b64&amp;quot;`` to the ``crit`` header parameter, and the\ndecoder rejects\ntokens that set ``b64=false`` without listing it in ``crit``. Thanks to\n  @MachineLearning-Nerd for the report.\n\nChanged\n</code></pre>\n<ul>\n<li>Migrate the <code>dev</code>, <code>docs</code>, and\n<code>tests</code> package extras to dependency groups by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kurtmckee\"><code>@​kurtmckee</code></a> in\n<code>[#1152](https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1152)\n&amp;lt;https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/pull/1152&amp;gt;</code>__\n</code></pre></li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/7144e4534c34810f4525dc4578a32addd8212cff\"><code>7144e45</code></a>\nApply ruff format</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/d2f4bec4963897c0ef96ef64a875894f2c8542ab\"><code>d2f4bec</code></a>\nRestore <code>cast()</code> calls with cross-version <code>type:\nignore</code> for <code>prepare_key</code></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/22f478cebddd8294259c30f037ecb92b0b348774\"><code>22f478c</code></a>\nRemove redundant casts in <code>RSAAlgorithm.prepare_key</code> and\n`ECAlgorithm.prepare...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/95791b1759b8aa4f2203575d344d5c78564cdc81\"><code>95791b1</code></a>\nBundle security fixes and hardening into 2.13.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/dcc27a9d3182a2349c30b160758785c6ce7a6508\"><code>dcc27a9</code></a>\n[pre-commit.ci] pre-commit autoupdate (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1155\">#1155</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/9d08a9a1896845ed8eaf88e6f6ac61e5800c3e7a\"><code>9d08a9a</code></a>\n[pre-commit.ci] pre-commit autoupdate (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1146\">#1146</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/b87c10014d4109f0214fea188d00faaaf8a80e64\"><code>b87c100</code></a>\nBump codecov/codecov-action from 5 to 6 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1154\">#1154</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/commit/40e3147eb5f790d8d041772e5fc00728a176c812\"><code>40e3147</code></a>\nMigrate development extras to dependency groups (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/issues/1152\">#1152</a>)</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/compare/2.12.1...2.13.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=pyjwt&package-manager=uv&previous-version=2.12.1&new-version=2.13.0)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-15T17:52:50Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/79a7928aeb39fc682e83c42fb2a9bfa80f387978","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/79a7928aeb39fc682e83c42fb2a9bfa80f387978","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/79a7928aeb39fc682e83c42fb2a9bfa80f387978/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ad41f06719cbf0e51b0dbc318ac36b79d252be04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ad41f06719cbf0e51b0dbc318ac36b79d252be04","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ad41f06719cbf0e51b0dbc318ac36b79d252be04"}]},{"sha":"ad41f06719cbf0e51b0dbc318ac36b79d252be04","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGFkNDFmMDY3MTljYmYwZTUxYjBkYmMzMThhYzM2Yjc5ZDI1MmJlMDQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-15T17:50:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-15T17:50:20Z"},"message":"docs(ci): annotate non-default branch releases (#3982)\n\nManual releases now carry clearer provenance when they are cut from a\nversion-line or alpha branch instead of the repository default branch.\nThe alpha release runbook also now points maintainers at the version\nline they are actually releasing from, so validation artifacts include\nthe intended staged code.\n\n## Changes\n- Added release workflow inputs for `BASE_BRANCH`, `DEFAULT_BRANCH`, and\n`REPOSITORY` so the release body can identify non-default-branch\nreleases.\n- Added a `Released from` line to non-default-branch release notes that\nnames the source branch and links to the immutable release commit,\navoiding links to throwaway alpha branches that may be deleted.\n- Updated the alpha release instructions to branch from the relevant\n`vX.Y` version line when staging or maintaining a separate release line,\nwhile keeping `main` as the normal default.\n- Documented the expected release-note behavior for pre-releases,\nincluding the new source-branch provenance line.","tree":{"sha":"6f66eaf3f75448c5a8fa155ba7f452a4ca3c0b58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/6f66eaf3f75448c5a8fa155ba7f452a4ca3c0b58"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/ad41f06719cbf0e51b0dbc318ac36b79d252be04","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMDtcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcBAQADRKto/bJZYpguMS9PUbMSOC\n4xHv+OeeZ54k9gju40XBDj//4LRsB+5oPtDs+0tZ6+k5L5Nw2iMOWLZv1CwMo4Tc\nqYy05Gnq/v2Htu7DYETKYvdREnJhp/RQyhO/xb2fjGQGRTuShDl8neNPf0fjYuNI\nh4MtkUG2ae+OrxvScQMAbYQTtZ5EiHRg0jweCsmdxdxb24JoXeU3qd/7WZm5Uudp\nw+oGdLbRWm5HqMBsqC1Zmi5hgM6qJoiQEXBgahj1o7ouFtM9bUHTEN+4Mq6aJ1/l\nm9EZAn64+gcWrGH7jkppuRerBDE7R5gUUfDmZM2Wqfij5VUm/XPS75eT7k6buQFd\nC4ULbDbsfZiV9Mpg+GE+4XZuH/L7wBxQ4dmuQ8KvV5DcSOz3K8mgKmTO6odU4ZWG\n1JTJk8OTplwHUlJk5fFFPaCPVjz75vaoVUOtrzbC48FaZ2Itw6lxUEUJ/++o9Vx/\nk+RJQ+Vs+EcoK5qq8747bbJiK8JXk5idIH9a6yrEkrNS57G83i/ESxWbjP4omy0t\nRq6d+n5bAdC8pDm5SpXtJsACR4X21heQbleGspCMno8QAHH5B8wEq369LT85emym\niW8d4+2zZrnOvYiAQf1/TJoRNB+DIYVymeLAZv5Scn0gnWAEqGXoL38Ww5GRLxm0\n/OtQjT501hS4d6/lpuHn\n=oPsG\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6f66eaf3f75448c5a8fa155ba7f452a4ca3c0b58\nparent 4aa0bbc70fc109ee6b13189e458ef1d37e4f2a0f\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781545820 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781545820 -0400\n\ndocs(ci): annotate non-default branch releases (#3982)\n\nManual releases now carry clearer provenance when they are cut from a\nversion-line or alpha branch instead of the repository default branch.\nThe alpha release runbook also now points maintainers at the version\nline they are actually releasing from, so validation artifacts include\nthe intended staged code.\n\n## Changes\n- Added release workflow inputs for `BASE_BRANCH`, `DEFAULT_BRANCH`, and\n`REPOSITORY` so the release body can identify non-default-branch\nreleases.\n- Added a `Released from` line to non-default-branch release notes that\nnames the source branch and links to the immutable release commit,\navoiding links to throwaway alpha branches that may be deleted.\n- Updated the alpha release instructions to branch from the relevant\n`vX.Y` version line when staging or maintaining a separate release line,\nwhile keeping `main` as the normal default.\n- Documented the expected release-note behavior for pre-releases,\nincluding the new source-branch provenance line.","verified_at":"2026-06-15T17:50:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ad41f06719cbf0e51b0dbc318ac36b79d252be04","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ad41f06719cbf0e51b0dbc318ac36b79d252be04","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ad41f06719cbf0e51b0dbc318ac36b79d252be04/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4aa0bbc70fc109ee6b13189e458ef1d37e4f2a0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4aa0bbc70fc109ee6b13189e458ef1d37e4f2a0f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4aa0bbc70fc109ee6b13189e458ef1d37e4f2a0f"}]},{"sha":"4aa0bbc70fc109ee6b13189e458ef1d37e4f2a0f","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDRhYTBiYmM3MGZjMTA5ZWU2YjEzMTg5ZTQ1OGVmMWQzN2U0ZjJhMGY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-15T17:48:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-15T17:48:07Z"},"message":"refactor(code): remove superseded thread-population helpers (#3961)\n\nRemoves three unused functions in `sessions.py`\n(`populate_thread_message_counts`, `populate_thread_initial_prompts`,\n`_extract_initial_prompt`) plus a private helper\n(`_load_latest_checkpoint_summary`) that only the removed code used.\n\nHow we know it's dead: the `/threads` modal now enriches rows through\nthe newer batched `populate_thread_checkpoint_details` /\n`_populate_checkpoint_fields` path. A search across the whole package,\ntests, and examples found no remaining callers of any of these — only\ntheir own definitions. The shared lower-level helpers they relied on are\nstill used by the batched path, so nothing else is affected.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"f417e7944d3ef2df116c8e1b38726a6e5301c70d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/f417e7944d3ef2df116c8e1b38726a6e5301c70d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/4aa0bbc70fc109ee6b13189e458ef1d37e4f2a0f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMDrXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABzoQABn1FNWv1c0/1Xy7Qitwl6lH\ndyhKpTRdI7DR7kYPBDscgKgbTtbWf1YqE1QsEYAUffTxEFo/kOPEY0EscyP0R94e\nUztJImbgmjApt5AjQ/lTsNF0cl4+ZBgAOS6v2UQZIVgoT3alXuBR6Ies9oiKbsU9\nFWVckDZ36Lv8E4/ZpmVMLCfjpH+/7GFL6fhSKgZhegIP9VQydVbBH9q76s1DcNQz\nsd6/qttbtY7XgLcEknM4aR0Lo9OLCSMNvzLMJ4XsMUTt9J+VVH9GIPNX0A6Gezwi\n08OG3Wv86e/TBXmzbrwEI4l8PQQR36CLgMVaBfwzikjMzE9mygMFurNAFo1E/2yn\nWyVdE7fOMF29M9px/kKt6/XpwGU5N0FLNQqUNu+szBzmBQHjztnX8eSe9jP0mU1U\nHr9JsB1O9fw9BF+osnV6C4GxmpeTx6lSRtAPrV/2rw/IUzJ2AvWVaAWXoztevDqn\nNKAvC+t6QWLVpKthduyvmvO1pEbEfgAhPsU+wS46hp6uFh296uyCskPqc0CpAXDv\nBphoNDS7EQvRJZc76jUP9KN7SFbBhwveuV+l3hD6nugbVaaB1jHQnAoZS9Fb1JbZ\ntBHokm4xfgLQUyBjKt0K3M60rBNvgQmlWPeraYpw6qnrqgzZejO1JThhSxMG6dcz\nEju2XX5g9Psxgfh3ljob\n=IndF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f417e7944d3ef2df116c8e1b38726a6e5301c70d\nparent 7af13f6ec2440c2e3eb63bad2ff31e809f772804\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781545687 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781545687 -0400\n\nrefactor(code): remove superseded thread-population helpers (#3961)\n\nRemoves three unused functions in `sessions.py`\n(`populate_thread_message_counts`, `populate_thread_initial_prompts`,\n`_extract_initial_prompt`) plus a private helper\n(`_load_latest_checkpoint_summary`) that only the removed code used.\n\nHow we know it's dead: the `/threads` modal now enriches rows through\nthe newer batched `populate_thread_checkpoint_details` /\n`_populate_checkpoint_fields` path. A search across the whole package,\ntests, and examples found no remaining callers of any of these — only\ntheir own definitions. The shared lower-level helpers they relied on are\nstill used by the batched path, so nothing else is affected.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-15T17:48:08Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4aa0bbc70fc109ee6b13189e458ef1d37e4f2a0f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4aa0bbc70fc109ee6b13189e458ef1d37e4f2a0f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4aa0bbc70fc109ee6b13189e458ef1d37e4f2a0f/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7af13f6ec2440c2e3eb63bad2ff31e809f772804","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7af13f6ec2440c2e3eb63bad2ff31e809f772804","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7af13f6ec2440c2e3eb63bad2ff31e809f772804"}]},{"sha":"7af13f6ec2440c2e3eb63bad2ff31e809f772804","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDdhZjEzZjZlYzI0NDBjMmUzZWI2M2JhZDJmZjMxZTgwOWY3NzI4MDQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-15T17:36:26Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-15T17:36:26Z"},"message":"fix(code): guard restart-prompt import against in-place self-upgrade (#3980)\n\nRunning `/install` could crash the whole TUI with `ModuleNotFoundError:\nNo module named 'deepagents_code.widgets.restart_prompt'`. The install\ncommand runs `uv tool install -U 'deepagents-code[...]'`, which\nreinstalls deepagents-code and rewrites its own on-disk package tree\n*while the process is running*. The post-install restart prompt was then\nimported for the first time off that just-mutated tree, so the import\nfailed and took the app down. Modules already resident in `sys.modules`\nsurvived from memory, which is why `app.py` ran fine right up to the\nfailing lazy import.\n\n## Changes\n- Load the `restart_prompt` modal into memory *before*\n`perform_install_extra`/`perform_install_package` rewrite the package\ntree, via `_ensure_restart_prompt_loaded()`, so the later import in\n`_offer_restart_after_install` is served from cache.\n- Wrap the post-install import in `_offer_restart_after_install` in a\nguard that degrades to the already-mounted manual `/restart` hint\ninstead of crashing when the module can't be loaded (e.g. a genuine\nversion upgrade mid-session). `RestartChoice` moves to the\n`TYPE_CHECKING` block to keep the annotation valid.","tree":{"sha":"95a67d4e832f83e1a2937176d74b469b0dca78e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/95a67d4e832f83e1a2937176d74b469b0dca78e2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/7af13f6ec2440c2e3eb63bad2ff31e809f772804","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMDgaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAU7cQADaGi1el+RcNHoru3n8HDo0r\neNKUKaj8CyivU3Qzr7w8aoYHtU/NniLeHGZZbsfFVdpasYL44u3rmXnqXdHiUXTx\nknEl1kEH0Ee020g+1KopMFfdueBZ3rwacSulApy2HYpCQh5W4fvSNfM17ZdAA5bM\npQ+/QhT1IB5JpgWIM+CxDgJtLZ1a5NuUl6yzG23XSyVBaI5c2Kp8lUhBwip2nC6f\nfWBIbXe9JLIoA/8XB6jCq/IYKwtIdw63UOLj2xbgcc3yJsyi72x8bU2312MAm3E7\nAF1qbcJnZbnaDVnz7jENKWMEIHfbj9fvWNzdDcWzc5JZ/5+rCGSW4RF9zI1Fuks8\nDnFXgVMvjSr8XNT13SsnJiNbPVTJWHH7oS2cfE2GCaVxfKEb0EaTdQuLllkGdgEe\nSYWcrK+1nb1kWWtIZa5RJNLQ8BHIoGZhU7JdvuA/K/jSgfNdh7ccaVnPsUyzvvgi\nodEyujUXn/374phl+REwQbIaytVLL6Ic6hLZmwMr4F0RDojGIhKVS9C9B1vy2l+x\n3Fa6y09oGrP8FmRt+6iLLj6wjLBHNxHDbE7neCyGtIdHqjC0+nZJDi8pyGQ6wOTf\n/kpEF4OuMcYbskpPVTaTEhn2mfqR7NIxneQfMN+MRmSSN1+2iAkB2053hZ7ibIi0\nhEUOYf8JnUzzM2SA43uR\n=q4tI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 95a67d4e832f83e1a2937176d74b469b0dca78e2\nparent 6a0b0ba8eec832887d493e97071a292472b73171\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781544986 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781544986 -0400\n\nfix(code): guard restart-prompt import against in-place self-upgrade (#3980)\n\nRunning `/install` could crash the whole TUI with `ModuleNotFoundError:\nNo module named 'deepagents_code.widgets.restart_prompt'`. The install\ncommand runs `uv tool install -U 'deepagents-code[...]'`, which\nreinstalls deepagents-code and rewrites its own on-disk package tree\n*while the process is running*. The post-install restart prompt was then\nimported for the first time off that just-mutated tree, so the import\nfailed and took the app down. Modules already resident in `sys.modules`\nsurvived from memory, which is why `app.py` ran fine right up to the\nfailing lazy import.\n\n## Changes\n- Load the `restart_prompt` modal into memory *before*\n`perform_install_extra`/`perform_install_package` rewrite the package\ntree, via `_ensure_restart_prompt_loaded()`, so the later import in\n`_offer_restart_after_install` is served from cache.\n- Wrap the post-install import in `_offer_restart_after_install` in a\nguard that degrades to the already-mounted manual `/restart` hint\ninstead of crashing when the module can't be loaded (e.g. a genuine\nversion upgrade mid-session). `RestartChoice` moves to the\n`TYPE_CHECKING` block to keep the annotation valid.","verified_at":"2026-06-15T17:36:26Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7af13f6ec2440c2e3eb63bad2ff31e809f772804","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7af13f6ec2440c2e3eb63bad2ff31e809f772804","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7af13f6ec2440c2e3eb63bad2ff31e809f772804/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6a0b0ba8eec832887d493e97071a292472b73171","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6a0b0ba8eec832887d493e97071a292472b73171","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/6a0b0ba8eec832887d493e97071a292472b73171"}]},{"sha":"6a0b0ba8eec832887d493e97071a292472b73171","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDZhMGIwYmE4ZWVjODMyODg3ZDQ5M2U5NzA3MWEyOTI0NzJiNzMxNzE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Nishitha M","email":"32355027+imnishitha@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-15T16:33:50Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-15T16:33:50Z"},"message":"fix(sdk): resolve virtual route paths in `CompositeBackend.execute` (#3762)\n\nFixes #3050\n\n## Issue:\n`CompositeBackend.execute()` always forwards the command string directly\nto the default backend's shell.\n\nSo when the agent runs:\n`python /common/skills/yyy/xxx.py`\nthe shell receives that exact string and tries to execute a real OS path\nnamed `/common/skills/yyy/xxx.py`.\n\nBut `/common/` is only a virtual mount inside `CompositeBackend`. It\ndoes not exist on the host filesystem. The actual file lives somewhere\nlike `/Users/.../shared/skills/yyy/xxx.py`.\n\nThe root cause is a mismatch the agent can't see: the file tools present\nrouted **virtual** paths (`/common/x.py`), but `execute`/`aexecute` run\non the backend's **host** shell, and the agent is never told the host\npath. Rather than\nrewriting the command string which can't be done correctly for\narbi(`$VAR`/`$(...)` expansion, here-docs, quoting, `cd`, dynamically\nbuilt paths), this fixes it at the prompting layer: tell the model each\nroute's hos\nforms the correct command itself.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added `_route_host_path_prompt(backend)` in the filesystem middleware.\nFor a`CompositeBackend`, it builds a \"Shell paths vs. virtual paths\"\nprompt section that maps each routed virtual prefix to its host path.\n- Routes backed by a host filesystem (those exposing a `cwd` and running\nin `virtual_mode`) get an explicit `virtual → host` mapping the model\nshould use\n    in shell commands.\n- Routes with no host path (e.g. `StoreBackend`) are listed as\nshell-inaccessible, steering the model to the file tools\n(`read_file`/`write_file`/`edit_file`/`grep`/`glob`) for those instead.\n- `wrap_model_call`/`awrap_model_call` append this section right after\nEXECUTION_SYSTEM_PROMPT`, only when the execute tool is present and the\nbacken supports execution. Returns an empty string (no-op) for\nnon-composite backends or backends with no routes.\n\n## Why prompting instead of command rewriting\n\nA regex rewrite of the command string can't be made correct: it can't\nsee variable/command substitution, here-docs, or paths the command\nbuilds itself, and it risks corrupting legitimately literal occurrences.\nSteering the model at the prompt acts on whole path tokens the model\nitself produces, so it composes naturally with quoting, `cd`, and\nsubstitution, none of which a string rewrite handles.\n\n## How I verified\n\n- Added `tests/unit_tests/middleware/test_execute_route_prompt.py`\ncovering:\nnon-composite backends and route-less composites (no-op), virtual\nfilesystem routes mapped to their resolved host path, store-backed\nroutes marked shell-inaccessible (and never offered as a mapping),\nnon-virtual filesystem\n  routes excluded from mappings, and a mixed host/non-host route set.\n- Ran `make format`, `make lint`, and `make test` from\n`libs/deepagents`.\n\nShoutout to @Smile0524 for raising this issue!","tree":{"sha":"840c9c765c343eb32768bbd8737f6eddb43cdc88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/840c9c765c343eb32768bbd8737f6eddb43cdc88"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/6a0b0ba8eec832887d493e97071a292472b73171","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMCluCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZ6QQAC7G2BXLbyZzlu3YilSx1w53\nPRj29CJ8k2lCxbUPY0/WTC5jDgePvG2JFCJKleP6XhDwE2vc95/s6hD+CUeHDq2W\nV2hYp/mXyWxklhq/ArO9mGie4nYEjxZt+L4kSPOiBqmv81OPwvik8j+gcR9sm/6g\ndOjiiqu2/IpPiUKxTQ64TkbEdZ7gGpNuVupO2UImI3ZWs24R6O4kcL0RfGkm4PxA\nc6jBXW2Wc7lpEQBpIj0As7e66JybSK+3XjvC+laeLV3nYxz0ePRem5eQLHpHNZ5A\nSyBnB/uYt4HGg0NXL9BRVgTjL+8gv5tVFoCU31y+lV/48fenCk+VPhUIQszWW+3A\nvP+Ri2T+Itm2GQUv388V3LTkBxtR7dC94Ciqluw64G8IdF8GOLEPVccM7UASGi0V\nXJhgvosdVnxTNvVFoFAzaP8j1deUbmat6z5UXn9UVKgNSbR/C6xJT9xYU4/R2gqR\nfib87J124DIaV2FjkfDHjgkwAebMrb9F7Mgjb9lXMs8WSmADb3xkQ3AbgtVDHBLy\nfRIKIUXGgRPdhwjx+kAhADRlegjxcjov7cbOZpxCCKTcnH9qqNu6pylUsjSa34n/\nXowFpwWOsBPWCzVJFmwHugn0Z69MW+XbBSIrwFIAaetkC/p2nZb3w6qHqehFv2UK\nbKB1+aYD0Jc9B3XmVzd9\n=Tl0c\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 840c9c765c343eb32768bbd8737f6eddb43cdc88\nparent c99cc47f7919e4f8287cea64c3082d3803724d0d\nauthor Nishitha M <32355027+imnishitha@users.noreply.github.com> 1781541230 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781541230 -0400\n\nfix(sdk): resolve virtual route paths in `CompositeBackend.execute` (#3762)\n\nFixes #3050\n\n## Issue:\n`CompositeBackend.execute()` always forwards the command string directly\nto the default backend's shell.\n\nSo when the agent runs:\n`python /common/skills/yyy/xxx.py`\nthe shell receives that exact string and tries to execute a real OS path\nnamed `/common/skills/yyy/xxx.py`.\n\nBut `/common/` is only a virtual mount inside `CompositeBackend`. It\ndoes not exist on the host filesystem. The actual file lives somewhere\nlike `/Users/.../shared/skills/yyy/xxx.py`.\n\nThe root cause is a mismatch the agent can't see: the file tools present\nrouted **virtual** paths (`/common/x.py`), but `execute`/`aexecute` run\non the backend's **host** shell, and the agent is never told the host\npath. Rather than\nrewriting the command string which can't be done correctly for\narbi(`$VAR`/`$(...)` expansion, here-docs, quoting, `cd`, dynamically\nbuilt paths), this fixes it at the prompting layer: tell the model each\nroute's hos\nforms the correct command itself.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added `_route_host_path_prompt(backend)` in the filesystem middleware.\nFor a`CompositeBackend`, it builds a \"Shell paths vs. virtual paths\"\nprompt section that maps each routed virtual prefix to its host path.\n- Routes backed by a host filesystem (those exposing a `cwd` and running\nin `virtual_mode`) get an explicit `virtual → host` mapping the model\nshould use\n    in shell commands.\n- Routes with no host path (e.g. `StoreBackend`) are listed as\nshell-inaccessible, steering the model to the file tools\n(`read_file`/`write_file`/`edit_file`/`grep`/`glob`) for those instead.\n- `wrap_model_call`/`awrap_model_call` append this section right after\nEXECUTION_SYSTEM_PROMPT`, only when the execute tool is present and the\nbacken supports execution. Returns an empty string (no-op) for\nnon-composite backends or backends with no routes.\n\n## Why prompting instead of command rewriting\n\nA regex rewrite of the command string can't be made correct: it can't\nsee variable/command substitution, here-docs, or paths the command\nbuilds itself, and it risks corrupting legitimately literal occurrences.\nSteering the model at the prompt acts on whole path tokens the model\nitself produces, so it composes naturally with quoting, `cd`, and\nsubstitution, none of which a string rewrite handles.\n\n## How I verified\n\n- Added `tests/unit_tests/middleware/test_execute_route_prompt.py`\ncovering:\nnon-composite backends and route-less composites (no-op), virtual\nfilesystem routes mapped to their resolved host path, store-backed\nroutes marked shell-inaccessible (and never offered as a mapping),\nnon-virtual filesystem\n  routes excluded from mappings, and a mixed host/non-host route set.\n- Ran `make format`, `make lint`, and `make test` from\n`libs/deepagents`.\n\nShoutout to @Smile0524 for raising this issue!","verified_at":"2026-06-15T16:33:51Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6a0b0ba8eec832887d493e97071a292472b73171","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/6a0b0ba8eec832887d493e97071a292472b73171","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6a0b0ba8eec832887d493e97071a292472b73171/comments","author":{"login":"imnishitha","id":32355027,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzU1MDI3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32355027?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha","html_url":"https://github.com/imnishitha","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c99cc47f7919e4f8287cea64c3082d3803724d0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c99cc47f7919e4f8287cea64c3082d3803724d0d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c99cc47f7919e4f8287cea64c3082d3803724d0d"}]},{"sha":"c99cc47f7919e4f8287cea64c3082d3803724d0d","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGM5OWNjNDdmNzkxOWU0ZjgyODdjZWE2NGMzMDgyZDM4MDM3MjRkMGQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-15T14:26:03Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-15T14:26:03Z"},"message":"docs(code): list valid `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_EXTRAS` options in `install.sh` (#3975)\n\nThe install script documented the `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_EXTRAS` environment\nvariable but only pointed readers to `pyproject.toml` for valid values.\nThis enumerates the available extras directly in the header comment —\ngrouped into model providers, sandbox providers, and standalone\nintegrations — so users can discover supported options without leaving\nthe script. The authoritative list still lives in `pyproject.toml`,\nwhich the comment notes.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"1cb98cf898fd55b8b8920ed11714e6f0f9a657f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/1cb98cf898fd55b8b8920ed11714e6f0f9a657f3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/c99cc47f7919e4f8287cea64c3082d3803724d0d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMAt7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApQcQAB0inwJvrRZ3VBj1ZsejAGP1\n5iLvX49JGU1z5hfpS2Da79AskpkkozQaAajBp2ShnPKLGvtZ9PfGh/nxPxeUuevP\n3pcxkJZhMhWvm4NOAMejN6I6gsRCRRJ0J+y1ELA6u/HtYimoUZ97xHiDbhXWSMCf\n/LfvnZL4eA7ZKI+2g2swZpBOTP6ec4wxpxpOi4ckXdglGsdsXzwAPUNdkMTl8YzX\nEymvb9fuI3bPin0VKTTk3sDUPgzM9yqmPJHrFcyaTMhO0foGf0N53zv/AwXu46/u\nAk6307xspzOVWmOpbk5NUc7SQKW77RE2NRYQyvXNHvEEsgMmXBAwDsnIhr9Jkh6P\njKAaDqiMpTy3Tc40BC8cFSAPO8c0FvB85JSwBAqUKD5VYVkiOueDQP4zQJR1kz42\n0NgfkLfUhj1pDW2uegrV7BwaDpAu/VQSza4oqLxD7fAw9ZLCi6RP6Tn76KGhBZZE\nloIqxffYji9wITNlpughQC4hCG+oFKfRT+q+KH4iZ/wY59OGjtYYnQBuspcFtJ3h\nmmoswm/iSS/X5vPIwllne78El/tGVOq1NNV8BpoRPzTDDpSU9uQlG2YjZ9iyF1rZ\nDFL/PFFbE7QOJdXzpOd7OcC1uEF91nTlflw7dOzZmYAXDC72+Ls1ffMuQ8BnsamG\nlb/qFYmPuzytHY1+onC0\n=Q2L5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1cb98cf898fd55b8b8920ed11714e6f0f9a657f3\nparent 11a71bbf00c4e6c1f989e70fb3472a65c8d39662\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781533563 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781533563 -0400\n\ndocs(code): list valid `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_EXTRAS` options in `install.sh` (#3975)\n\nThe install script documented the `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_EXTRAS` environment\nvariable but only pointed readers to `pyproject.toml` for valid values.\nThis enumerates the available extras directly in the header comment —\ngrouped into model providers, sandbox providers, and standalone\nintegrations — so users can discover supported options without leaving\nthe script. The authoritative list still lives in `pyproject.toml`,\nwhich the comment notes.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-15T14:26:03Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c99cc47f7919e4f8287cea64c3082d3803724d0d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c99cc47f7919e4f8287cea64c3082d3803724d0d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c99cc47f7919e4f8287cea64c3082d3803724d0d/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"11a71bbf00c4e6c1f989e70fb3472a65c8d39662","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/11a71bbf00c4e6c1f989e70fb3472a65c8d39662","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/11a71bbf00c4e6c1f989e70fb3472a65c8d39662"}]},{"sha":"11a71bbf00c4e6c1f989e70fb3472a65c8d39662","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDExYTcxYmJmMDBjNGU2YzFmOTg5ZTcwZmIzNDcyYTY1YzhkMzk2NjI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-15T13:36:43Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-15T13:36:43Z"},"message":"feat(code): non-interactive `deepagents auth` subcommands (#3910)\n\nCloses #3121\n\nAdd `deepagents auth` CLI subcommands (`list`, `set`, `remove`,\n`status`, `path`) to manage stored provider credentials without\nlaunching the TUI.\n\n---\n\nThe in-TUI `/auth` flow is the only way to manage stored model-provider\ncredentials today, which leaves dotfile bootstrap, CI, and \"set this on\na remote box without launching the TUI\" with no scriptable path. This\nadds an `auth` command group that mirrors the modal verbs:\n\n- `auth list` / `auth status [<provider>]` — report the same resolution\nsource the TUI shows (`stored`, `env: VAR`, `missing`, ...).\n- `auth set <provider>` — reads the key from stdin by default so it\nnever lands in shell history or argv, and refuses an interactive TTY\n(use `--from-env VAR` to copy from a process env var instead). Routes\nthrough `auth_store.set_stored_key` so chmod warnings from the shared\n`WriteOutcome` path surface on stderr.\n- `auth remove <provider>` (aliases `rm`/`delete`) and `auth path`.\n\nThe group registers next to `mcp`/`config`/`threads` in `parse_args`, is\nwired into `_HELP_SPECS` for the startup fast-path help dispatch, and\ngets a hand-maintained `ui.show_auth_help` screen. A new public\n`auth_store.auth_path` backs `auth path`.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"97bebbfed4f0fecf40664299cc1710c2204f4e1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/97bebbfed4f0fecf40664299cc1710c2204f4e1a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/11a71bbf00c4e6c1f989e70fb3472a65c8d39662","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqL//rCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAviEQAFnG2Ty3/k2lV6Fylne/rVqo\nfTWKHnjAlrIamtCRoJFI462N1UtDZIXQHOF5J6wRMZO/GsAT2Rv0lez9+t405zHs\n0YGgwmgARcUS1bMOj2vLS3iI8dwOORpKrTcTrJJHw1L+HOMPgF3Si3qRYKXvSaVp\nicvVvJjq+txOFjryvZgHdvF47Y4NCXEWSPAVfs755XCpMEE98G/OQJTu+9QM0jqa\nkSSTN/LJGL8ExVJjdunMBfRAlCIoIuzlXqe3Hqk1G9u+UoLJ8jIMy21yu/4nwTao\nd3GA9BfKJt9upJKDQ4gRoGZqnZbva1+cLs9NafEJCD2ViEjahNEi+aNzG34qW6p+\nqd62joWh1zp3MV9PNCM3xHbm89nIfo5MUf3KhT61M2QsG3nxTZ4Wtjvv4XCgkj7v\nEbRAA2tgPLe2/D3rkKUUheFCmG689D6Ct8QWx4igZJ04hKkRrp/kJ5cAu8+zTqYt\nqibihOKiucXIoES7C6KbXhoXfBQeFYbc0Ob49S5BEkv8QFRIv0z9hsq/oSxRlDRd\nFYFn43zaf2enpwi5NIwBYE9Sv+KupyBt6jHVvdP44vuhKhU06MoX1xwu+WPv9nUG\nN9jazgAUB80mD1+e0MG+rkBnDDJ5AkI6LPsK3Wl+g5g//ji1DPeDxzNzXW5LyduA\nERFw//psrP9urm51/XMj\n=fVBp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 97bebbfed4f0fecf40664299cc1710c2204f4e1a\nparent 59755031482db7cfd7705f6a03c42e7a2dfd39a3\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781530603 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781530603 -0400\n\nfeat(code): non-interactive `deepagents auth` subcommands (#3910)\n\nCloses #3121\n\nAdd `deepagents auth` CLI subcommands (`list`, `set`, `remove`,\n`status`, `path`) to manage stored provider credentials without\nlaunching the TUI.\n\n---\n\nThe in-TUI `/auth` flow is the only way to manage stored model-provider\ncredentials today, which leaves dotfile bootstrap, CI, and \"set this on\na remote box without launching the TUI\" with no scriptable path. This\nadds an `auth` command group that mirrors the modal verbs:\n\n- `auth list` / `auth status [<provider>]` — report the same resolution\nsource the TUI shows (`stored`, `env: VAR`, `missing`, ...).\n- `auth set <provider>` — reads the key from stdin by default so it\nnever lands in shell history or argv, and refuses an interactive TTY\n(use `--from-env VAR` to copy from a process env var instead). Routes\nthrough `auth_store.set_stored_key` so chmod warnings from the shared\n`WriteOutcome` path surface on stderr.\n- `auth remove <provider>` (aliases `rm`/`delete`) and `auth path`.\n\nThe group registers next to `mcp`/`config`/`threads` in `parse_args`, is\nwired into `_HELP_SPECS` for the startup fast-path help dispatch, and\ngets a hand-maintained `ui.show_auth_help` screen. A new public\n`auth_store.auth_path` backs `auth path`.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-15T13:36:44Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/11a71bbf00c4e6c1f989e70fb3472a65c8d39662","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/11a71bbf00c4e6c1f989e70fb3472a65c8d39662","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/11a71bbf00c4e6c1f989e70fb3472a65c8d39662/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"59755031482db7cfd7705f6a03c42e7a2dfd39a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/59755031482db7cfd7705f6a03c42e7a2dfd39a3","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/59755031482db7cfd7705f6a03c42e7a2dfd39a3"}]},{"sha":"59755031482db7cfd7705f6a03c42e7a2dfd39a3","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDU5NzU1MDMxNDgyZGI3Y2ZkNzcwNWY2YTAzYzQyZTdhMmRmZDM5YTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-14T23:19:52Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-14T23:19:52Z"},"message":"refactor(code): remove unused `SessionState` class and key-presence properties (#3963)\n\nRemoves the `SessionState` class and the `has_openai` / `has_nvidia`\nproperties from `config.py`.\n\nHow we know it's dead: the session state actually used at runtime is a\nseparate class, `TextualSessionState`, defined in `app.py`. This\n`config.SessionState` class is never instantiated or imported anywhere,\nand the two API-key presence properties have no callers (other provider\nproperties like `has_anthropic` are kept since they are used). A search\nacross the package and tests turned up only the definitions themselves.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"30efe49066953585a0fc5f0c4fce428bf7eac50a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/30efe49066953585a0fc5f0c4fce428bf7eac50a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/59755031482db7cfd7705f6a03c42e7a2dfd39a3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLzcYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAl7sQAIgAcoDqeCemyhfaOZRd/8xN\naHkEos0IdW5Pe7fILRSZU+gCQa6FE7TItt31osvXeeDF7A8K2JxbBTXvokDBhE1s\nfFpEdHUasChu1uFZgKW+jjWnyg/GDqELObU4J783yTx9ezLd34Y4nGhPvatwfTzz\nQDNVgsGALHc69FQS/mFwh9yk9d5JKNb3yQVaa4ewKgEUaMTlYYpoETc9vNLDOA3L\nC8fClmU+hMmJpeTZ/CeUBOLQAqaGPa2eGftkiQI+KyEh08oUkZI7SxwCptqqUoyl\nAU8bEGGZmajKxhE6VEVPUugjLoEf7mxfhXK/A+TG3nfkUt1lGTgfj41AQO/hcbA2\n/6P1gPWn7uMFJSsuNKXxDW1EqW+izvsJSt6tpBW6vwC+yFsbbX3rdMQYQsI6oDcb\nS5Jm31Rxg+GiBrnMpqtx0sJQbkl1wOJAV0P+qB+daAATK19kOj0EaoiWVswDQ/Pz\nvQP2D9gkr5FDHbHZkbqkkSc5XSV9UR6U6Pf2Ud7pXXr8AaETTgPU8UKMculVf8Es\nrdqIH/od6RhDYbpUI43BDhPDKK3SXjB/fHEbKkcPNo+z9x1FcJVngNBWKHHSoe5Z\nErKEimt8hwVbrDtLzqjEyJ5koSdoaBZN5CfpcQgg4FhEUZoDFy2+caiOs0PA2LEN\n6kEMlp5MvQEJWcG4ZMk4\n=/D2w\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 30efe49066953585a0fc5f0c4fce428bf7eac50a\nparent aad3abf998324de366c793aa1e29856aadf6d4c3\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781479192 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781479192 -0400\n\nrefactor(code): remove unused `SessionState` class and key-presence properties (#3963)\n\nRemoves the `SessionState` class and the `has_openai` / `has_nvidia`\nproperties from `config.py`.\n\nHow we know it's dead: the session state actually used at runtime is a\nseparate class, `TextualSessionState`, defined in `app.py`. This\n`config.SessionState` class is never instantiated or imported anywhere,\nand the two API-key presence properties have no callers (other provider\nproperties like `has_anthropic` are kept since they are used). A search\nacross the package and tests turned up only the definitions themselves.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-14T23:19:53Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/59755031482db7cfd7705f6a03c42e7a2dfd39a3","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/59755031482db7cfd7705f6a03c42e7a2dfd39a3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/59755031482db7cfd7705f6a03c42e7a2dfd39a3/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"aad3abf998324de366c793aa1e29856aadf6d4c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/aad3abf998324de366c793aa1e29856aadf6d4c3","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/aad3abf998324de366c793aa1e29856aadf6d4c3"}]},{"sha":"aad3abf998324de366c793aa1e29856aadf6d4c3","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGFhZDNhYmY5OTgzMjRkZTM2NmM3OTNhYTFlMjk4NTZhYWRmNmQ0YzM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-14T23:19:23Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-14T23:19:23Z"},"message":"refactor(code): remove unused `DeepAgentsApp` helper methods (#3964)\n\nRemoves three private helper methods on the main app that are never\ncalled: `_prompt_launch_dependencies`, `_resolve_offload_budget_str`,\nand `_prompt_model_selector`.\n\nHow we know it's dead: each has a single match in the codebase — its own\ndefinition. The flows that look related are actually handled by sibling\nmethods that are still in use (`_prompt_launch_dependencies_then_model`\nfor onboarding, `_show_model_selector` for model selection), so these\nthree are leftovers. None are wired to a Textual event/action/key\nbinding. The full app unit-test suite passes after removal.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"4c00b5271525a8208048da0e972c48d463e3e61d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/4c00b5271525a8208048da0e972c48d463e3e61d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/aad3abf998324de366c793aa1e29856aadf6d4c3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLzb8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYzcQABbsH5FphDOGVSVMnoLTv5S5\n0HoE0GFyuCwVaG4YIlFEHKacASefYaM43bnkdb1S/Q0sgTEDnvfkl17OM8itwKsM\ncv9ejVOFUr7mLLmUYQwnARfemvAWx1v0ShKiXVqUHauDZkkTEEvTDssVAvfIheYE\nIU/Ex4IS2vwVNzqEVp/s6wNyckFwt1crseqode5EFLO+3mwPT8w5ushoObOfwhbI\n13HOAkWJDY54MEGg/+L5u4PHtsTS6lzcxrjK6Oo4VRkWu/iQaGTFnTvkaoUClNzq\nr5JNkQRrQ6RpjEXCbt7jh+hPrij9oI7XeAWH3fXa5McW8dzpHxkPfdTBjLboNpaK\nTcG/Z76QFD/Y5jPHmGbex7fY8Lp9CzqV81fqAlO229a6biqJoiH6eXKns4vnEQzD\n7gwCm2U1f3GZrRigm5qzcZDXO3KdwWAmjGTvpRpkitTHDG9Ma3Nvl0EsJiQ0PlM+\nSBCoz6DzASjmaZm7L8vrJ1xMEU2Z3fiF6QiLbhL8H+Lkv9gEkUeqSCWulmCRcBKp\nDVQmPnj3P2kIIMJPFJrClIG1N86jPA5tNsd6hIzuzKHGDLY9s+IvmNipJ0zR0IGM\nAxtIaESw/deKFQ9kd2ay018EQOQ68H/i6ncH94Bg3um3f1UX875KAg0eWPaXebh4\nlmxsrahROF4lv1JvF4Q5\n=S8tO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4c00b5271525a8208048da0e972c48d463e3e61d\nparent 661c034581b0500ae95a12815d4f4d3a09393801\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781479163 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781479163 -0400\n\nrefactor(code): remove unused `DeepAgentsApp` helper methods (#3964)\n\nRemoves three private helper methods on the main app that are never\ncalled: `_prompt_launch_dependencies`, `_resolve_offload_budget_str`,\nand `_prompt_model_selector`.\n\nHow we know it's dead: each has a single match in the codebase — its own\ndefinition. The flows that look related are actually handled by sibling\nmethods that are still in use (`_prompt_launch_dependencies_then_model`\nfor onboarding, `_show_model_selector` for model selection), so these\nthree are leftovers. None are wired to a Textual event/action/key\nbinding. The full app unit-test suite passes after removal.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-14T23:19:24Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/aad3abf998324de366c793aa1e29856aadf6d4c3","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/aad3abf998324de366c793aa1e29856aadf6d4c3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/aad3abf998324de366c793aa1e29856aadf6d4c3/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"661c034581b0500ae95a12815d4f4d3a09393801","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/661c034581b0500ae95a12815d4f4d3a09393801","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/661c034581b0500ae95a12815d4f4d3a09393801"}]},{"sha":"661c034581b0500ae95a12815d4f4d3a09393801","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDY2MWMwMzQ1ODFiMDUwMGFlOTVhMTI4MTVkNGY0ZDNhMDkzOTM4MDE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-14T23:17:35Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-14T23:17:35Z"},"message":"refactor(code): remove orphaned unused helper methods (#3965)\n\nRemoves four small helper functions/methods that are defined but never\ncalled:\n- `_get_available_sandbox_types` (`integrations/sandbox_factory.py`)\n- `MCPServerInfo.is_loaded` (`mcp_tools.py`)\n- `MessageStore.get_message_at_index` (`widgets/message_store.py`)\n- `InputState.get_media` (`input.py`)\n\nHow we know it's dead: each one has exactly one match in the whole\npackage, tests, and examples — its own definition. Their sibling helpers\nthat are actually used (e.g. `needs_attention`,\n`get_images`/`get_videos`) are left in place.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"2b2215f585a6a20d5ae54041f3574bdf11f3a0f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/2b2215f585a6a20d5ae54041f3574bdf11f3a0f2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/661c034581b0500ae95a12815d4f4d3a09393801","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLzaQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoxcQAJXninOUqHhwEZeyZXvaHKAV\nWJwy645TXUw5weE+oXpnu88UrZPE6WYmRcZryDG2f5wxcuk0x69JkDXsOCemKecG\ny3+tVV/b8QIj/EWa12PJycyGReDSvGrC2ANIKAYl072XISiqANYrp73URVfFRyr3\nwDtzH5VtguTflmA1kbk4RBG3FGODt0bg+7OQ6fRYdxcEQlAMLcuuZpHCfBWy2BxQ\ndfvvgo658G1CGMRlt3dCnzE4Ax63cr68db80TrnJf181iGUp6owPXBrdUFlK6A6H\nZ04emNqL/Cvo97FUQBvIDRsK8tvoZKxJtpphsRUXuPUQ2xqAzo1sLR0gHbljf4G1\nTmF7xFpHAdVNK53QCZI/9eu5hwofT7z/4xKbj07ir43DrgENV+WjjoM5VB/cYSNg\nUIaJeV7Vt11kJNMebE1NxoysDFUa+Za2CGn2CVAGzsDbU0al0l76gVYMaRP3b1Lf\neboYU355EtIYDic3sjWDKsP9HDmNmPllzbHJKEQaHm06o5MwLjU6zJmIKA596Bjq\n5c4PqAUU4QX6wLQ5N/xEHUGcNHAeHmRoq4vGWtifTcni336CRk7rs/xcfQe7fkiz\nXij+uXycH6wawtzUQJ4rmkhByNUu5HoQKK1kR3cuuzPMU0ImOdI+VlDMwQdO6PpX\n5xc0OsMWO04R5e2aVwGG\n=Oy/9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2b2215f585a6a20d5ae54041f3574bdf11f3a0f2\nparent 71b22aac2f6409fe73bf4d14f66e3bc86e787a71\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781479055 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781479055 -0400\n\nrefactor(code): remove orphaned unused helper methods (#3965)\n\nRemoves four small helper functions/methods that are defined but never\ncalled:\n- `_get_available_sandbox_types` (`integrations/sandbox_factory.py`)\n- `MCPServerInfo.is_loaded` (`mcp_tools.py`)\n- `MessageStore.get_message_at_index` (`widgets/message_store.py`)\n- `InputState.get_media` (`input.py`)\n\nHow we know it's dead: each one has exactly one match in the whole\npackage, tests, and examples — its own definition. Their sibling helpers\nthat are actually used (e.g. `needs_attention`,\n`get_images`/`get_videos`) are left in place.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-14T23:17:36Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/661c034581b0500ae95a12815d4f4d3a09393801","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/661c034581b0500ae95a12815d4f4d3a09393801","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/661c034581b0500ae95a12815d4f4d3a09393801/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"71b22aac2f6409fe73bf4d14f66e3bc86e787a71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/71b22aac2f6409fe73bf4d14f66e3bc86e787a71","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/71b22aac2f6409fe73bf4d14f66e3bc86e787a71"}]},{"sha":"71b22aac2f6409fe73bf4d14f66e3bc86e787a71","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDcxYjIyYWFjMmY2NDA5ZmU3M2JmNGQxNGY2NmUzYmM4NmU3ODdhNzE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-14T21:32:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-14T21:32:40Z"},"message":"style(code): dim cancelled user prompt on interrupt (#3906)\n\nInterrupted (`esc`) prompts are now dimmed to distinguish them from\ncompleted prompts.\n\n---\n\nWhen an agent turn is interrupted via `esc`, the prompt that started the\nturn now dims slightly (`opacity: 0.6`), making cancelled prompts\nvisually distinct from ones that ran to completion — mirroring the\nexisting dimmed treatment of queued messages. `UserMessage` gains a\n`set_cancelled()` helper that adds a `-cancelled` CSS class; the app\ntracks the in-flight prompt widget and dims it in `action_interrupt`'s\nagent-cancel branch, clearing the reference on turn cleanup.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"a8cb921246e723371cb515569b082bbcff71b087","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a8cb921246e723371cb515569b082bbcff71b087"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/71b22aac2f6409fe73bf4d14f66e3bc86e787a71","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLx34CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzqEQAKXrWG5SL/7Ni0pJT4nDYoTQ\nHw/ka8BwaLh/ySV+1uXU2pbylPqGqAUFM/2HeAL0FJbtQQ7rQHWSzsSUUVKH0V7l\nOmz4XrHB3aQiLhfU+l3mIJ8ju5MumpaidqOJ6tMP/vMYSoIX+sLkdbjPUDWxQj0T\n/wS+g53aLrzmlmMoo/GkMzWkPmw9eekndLPNQlmeoAIIkqHkWxRQmfP1qYKcdmlK\nP9VPmeyIti6qlZI3i9U1ImEage8zUwnIFm2ZIhgchAboU35L8u+ddV4orhOIFt/9\nAzoshQo9hoX+UGtXgUgDuyinQiHWNBa5JcYdMiiIetGNns3OSBPevNLctmg40BON\n86Z5bJL6hc562f5vv9Jdtvv2zTr4prxHQ8a4atFLCfRbsPI+nfua76c52CiUq6Ay\n47lAPqup5jYZNN7gq7qqwhJkgwPIFevRAq2xiubuxrZp4QDzbpbHV300YAo42DzO\nSK3ksn9WnixAQioUIE3f4Y0ik37DmWPOq2TA4ScspQAdAD5Ebwk0ZhlaXUkRdBul\n0Mi3fvm2g9260ZW8XlE/3FPqARSabcrbRWQZ46QiEN1PMRNYiQSwpkwq2JauZPrA\npFF0g1FeplrcloLvSI0eWceqGzD/khMeLEmSPLDyiBc4L9enWfZEZNhO2wriIk4I\nv2s3o7MlunFnkANR575w\n=RS9F\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a8cb921246e723371cb515569b082bbcff71b087\nparent 341a5cc55a30d808dbb366b396923c7801c431d2\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781472760 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781472760 -0400\n\nstyle(code): dim cancelled user prompt on interrupt (#3906)\n\nInterrupted (`esc`) prompts are now dimmed to distinguish them from\ncompleted prompts.\n\n---\n\nWhen an agent turn is interrupted via `esc`, the prompt that started the\nturn now dims slightly (`opacity: 0.6`), making cancelled prompts\nvisually distinct from ones that ran to completion — mirroring the\nexisting dimmed treatment of queued messages. `UserMessage` gains a\n`set_cancelled()` helper that adds a `-cancelled` CSS class; the app\ntracks the in-flight prompt widget and dims it in `action_interrupt`'s\nagent-cancel branch, clearing the reference on turn cleanup.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-14T21:32:41Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/71b22aac2f6409fe73bf4d14f66e3bc86e787a71","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/71b22aac2f6409fe73bf4d14f66e3bc86e787a71","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/71b22aac2f6409fe73bf4d14f66e3bc86e787a71/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"341a5cc55a30d808dbb366b396923c7801c431d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/341a5cc55a30d808dbb366b396923c7801c431d2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/341a5cc55a30d808dbb366b396923c7801c431d2"}]},{"sha":"341a5cc55a30d808dbb366b396923c7801c431d2","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDM0MWE1Y2M1NWEzMGQ4MDhkYmIzNjZiMzk2OTIzYzc4MDFjNDMxZDI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-14T21:19:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-14T21:19:16Z"},"message":"feat(code): add pre-release update support (#3960)\n\nStable `dcode` installs can now opt into alpha/beta/rc updates from both\nheadless CLI flows and the interactive `/update` command. Pre-release\nupgrade attempts are limited to `uv tool` installs so users do not get\nsilently routed through an installer that cannot honor the requested\nrelease channel.","tree":{"sha":"8b441f8ccd128c8518b07c9eea94fa0689e70e37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/8b441f8ccd128c8518b07c9eea94fa0689e70e37"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/341a5cc55a30d808dbb366b396923c7801c431d2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLxrUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjkAQAD8NPNnTCAheHbpvnhVU5e7q\nNQCTOCrxNJjaUjJFxZxYIWZOMIj17pE0MgekAHkawEWGOdNnpfi1IAI6uNIbEj3U\neKqypUhvh78YF3ci+cEEb9WCZ03sK0OwlFQR3qyV+wfo0jw2T2neDhUiIiBCNMSI\nrTUBCyzyfoN62Bij0yHZG308sq0juuZv1BMEDjiRaB25Ar5btft2v8vEI7f/fpQr\nKuIU9oCKT8XtsBqq9nQ9aw1JW5cEXKnrpMpfOWOqj+aQ35zwjnnVSgwmkhCqdzjd\nX4n4BchWCQtc4hPvM7ElOS4CsZU9hITBD5K1pQZlhjjHdshaRDx7i0SOMObjvino\nPklDk3VsmBCBjz8zlZUa1jcpEoIz7JI8to6F0Z/sqZ+RgGmjhR8FIKoLOCb9xifJ\nGe31GwPA4ILfAYeR7ZTBZwcRGJwXvBPulChDiAOxAleYGjgDUiq52Edi0uefysma\nErjxiaSwOv+aPqwBVm4eRVQ8lFtqwbEZF0pIkeRr1pGVZAph9yKh9/3DrK+kXes2\nontc0jBD91u5mbSayEm7vLjQ/7Zp6p5XS2KbYC8AynCcecTES035A+6MDkx1Gmx9\nj4JrPmOUyTqAoK25u1iM6m1vefZLNavAIq0T4R7Ju/RQ5j11Rbz23u21586yMhnX\n34QA5ARdIhik10cwxVxO\n=TFBR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8b441f8ccd128c8518b07c9eea94fa0689e70e37\nparent 3ba347138ac61a474bad58365fdeaa0d00cc1a42\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781471956 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781471956 -0400\n\nfeat(code): add pre-release update support (#3960)\n\nStable `dcode` installs can now opt into alpha/beta/rc updates from both\nheadless CLI flows and the interactive `/update` command. Pre-release\nupgrade attempts are limited to `uv tool` installs so users do not get\nsilently routed through an installer that cannot honor the requested\nrelease channel.","verified_at":"2026-06-14T21:19:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/341a5cc55a30d808dbb366b396923c7801c431d2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/341a5cc55a30d808dbb366b396923c7801c431d2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/341a5cc55a30d808dbb366b396923c7801c431d2/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3ba347138ac61a474bad58365fdeaa0d00cc1a42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3ba347138ac61a474bad58365fdeaa0d00cc1a42","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3ba347138ac61a474bad58365fdeaa0d00cc1a42"}]},{"sha":"3ba347138ac61a474bad58365fdeaa0d00cc1a42","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDNiYTM0NzEzOGFjNjFhNDc0YmFkNTgzNjVmZGVhYTBkMDBjYzFhNDI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-14T20:37:00Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-14T20:37:00Z"},"message":"fix(code): skip startup auto-update when already updated in-session (#3915)\n\nFixed a spurious \"Auto-updating ... before startup\" message/restart on\nlaunch after updating via `/update` in the same session.\n\n---\n\nAfter running `/update` inside the TUI, the on-disk install advances but\nthe running process keeps its baked-in `__version__`. The startup\nauto-update compares the cache against `__version__`, so on the next\nlaunch it redundantly re-ran the upgrade and restarted (\"Auto-updating\n... before startup ... Restarting...\"). This adds an\n`is_installed_version_at_least(latest)` guard to\n`_run_startup_auto_update`, mirroring the existing exit-banner check, so\nan already-installed version is skipped.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"252452f779f2b8d4f3b40c1e4b0827dfecc99dd8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/252452f779f2b8d4f3b40c1e4b0827dfecc99dd8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/3ba347138ac61a474bad58365fdeaa0d00cc1a42","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLxDsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARzIQAEKKV0fallru9V38IMCla1u0\nJv1XFERy3K+0vKQQXH3X9iYAZ0GsZ1wPFjqRKb9wNxUbyow8sn90RanfCFeufy7/\n9DPpHVngMqw+vI9bJo5AP4Uo1zZJe9Q+iyddWOgjn71Xe7Fj3jA5puqGuOPIxruz\nukYYvMaotwTkvmJ0rUA6b27ugQkPTtdNyNhapH3lCzZhsoqV+tIf1/ioUzjHP6Lr\nOAs7Sk1UcLaar6ey7yu2yd9g7VjvLGqyNkdJfJtSXdm02H4T3zMi8uCDuW7g/bNV\n0qutFEeeN75pAlf+QhtisM8wZ1hmwzINCUbhUaGeQm6RR6ftIbfKAm5AAt3zxf8m\nPgdfMkpWaSZCja0HllRVGfvkE6s5VBf873KV9GVIymUZt660d88861W9D565oSz9\ncvJMe4QzRaxKAR16ynaPe2A5d9SOuJWK0p5Y/jABnouhg+p5YnXsZUPRiw4Ogsro\nRlMVVqzCbz6WUGa0soqhFdqFmWXX4CDDy/TPfok81Vh27/DF4QTOFRR7WvMDcvTF\nGgI6jCe5gJ4bPJ+dPx1uZwJK3FSOzEpPyV4/YJdAC3UPDr4qS8Gi5iNsfxjYU4Iw\ngeMVu1IuuaKUZ2xgV6O9qGGy9YzoxTvNXzW7rNuNuklxdHMTckA2zq44QD0oI/4A\nPPMd/rhZZ9/6d3FAqu9N\n=k6Sx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 252452f779f2b8d4f3b40c1e4b0827dfecc99dd8\nparent d1c6946218b4f0f86ab7b02b6bb6af1e4b75cede\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781469420 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781469420 -0400\n\nfix(code): skip startup auto-update when already updated in-session (#3915)\n\nFixed a spurious \"Auto-updating ... before startup\" message/restart on\nlaunch after updating via `/update` in the same session.\n\n---\n\nAfter running `/update` inside the TUI, the on-disk install advances but\nthe running process keeps its baked-in `__version__`. The startup\nauto-update compares the cache against `__version__`, so on the next\nlaunch it redundantly re-ran the upgrade and restarted (\"Auto-updating\n... before startup ... Restarting...\"). This adds an\n`is_installed_version_at_least(latest)` guard to\n`_run_startup_auto_update`, mirroring the existing exit-banner check, so\nan already-installed version is skipped.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-14T20:37:01Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3ba347138ac61a474bad58365fdeaa0d00cc1a42","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3ba347138ac61a474bad58365fdeaa0d00cc1a42","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3ba347138ac61a474bad58365fdeaa0d00cc1a42/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d1c6946218b4f0f86ab7b02b6bb6af1e4b75cede","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d1c6946218b4f0f86ab7b02b6bb6af1e4b75cede","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d1c6946218b4f0f86ab7b02b6bb6af1e4b75cede"}]},{"sha":"d1c6946218b4f0f86ab7b02b6bb6af1e4b75cede","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGQxYzY5NDYyMThiNGYwZjg2YWI3YjAyYjZiYjZhZjFlNGI3NWNlZGU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-13T06:58:27Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-13T06:58:27Z"},"message":"chore(code): support pinned and pre-release installs (#3945)\n\nThe `dcode` install script can now install exact `deepagents-code`\nversions or ask `uv` to resolve pre-release versions using an explicit\nstrategy. Invalid version pins, invalid pre-release strategies, and\nconflicting version/pre-release settings fail before invoking `uv` so\nthe installer does not forward ambiguous or unsafe arguments.","tree":{"sha":"216301c12407f10caab775f2c3938fa903fc65f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/216301c12407f10caab775f2c3938fa903fc65f9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/d1c6946218b4f0f86ab7b02b6bb6af1e4b75cede","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLP+TCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8RoQABJ7r9jZ8RteNWvncyHhuqxj\njtAJo3MF0cSHteFRcBeQrTBNNO8HJeTpKguaDH2NeNGGGy8eBwKMIgBa/a93knEA\nFgwIoWUTvBS7iUXhVEMdPtAbcrr77Nk+2ec5H6qEUg63RhkI0cNZAmRl+7zuj8cn\nvJm0auWDXQF/TFlH8V0cLSlcJHAmyNTzSNxOzQryBwixEaaWvtWgn/+59evm3ecX\n+H5UDTvzzAmyNZe5+uQhDvLhnMt/7iEng5LAZ/K4QHN2Dss1L2ys1UZ3kUaZW1QL\nksNxDJJA+rm5N1YRdFoYQFQtXsBTR+As/5tjyEGi1PyvY66B3dZ1BQSdRqVW23Pb\nysvfVanaCDHC04KLjXLM3iLxgQRkykkpL2I3dFYutNgXmEPQdZyREL8o4QlQ9JRo\nI/1Vhfs9awQtfC31nidRciUnCHtz9b1sCFpBC/0Jxu0wfmmTvaRFa68TWD9fQQK8\nZ6RKxwVK2O2co15oSI1Kp6GtqmNjodBe1S8tH/THMY0UFkj/zm8ihpGWhSIEO/+v\ngcRAjJ+pKeK/B6qeN2xxkYq8vPdNt9/6Mh5pg+FjymMUcu+TDYxPiW2aFR4lZon1\nR2FygMu18seaAbP9i073SXNYsD4hAzyoEl4J9+Y5Wb0x5vfAnBi9jbKwkBwte8+3\nMCfzNkA5lD1SBbhD9z2J\n=Wx4Y\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 216301c12407f10caab775f2c3938fa903fc65f9\nparent b6fe5d86a1cc3fcdd95771f0ee050701fe7d5c58\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781333907 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781333907 -0400\n\nchore(code): support pinned and pre-release installs (#3945)\n\nThe `dcode` install script can now install exact `deepagents-code`\nversions or ask `uv` to resolve pre-release versions using an explicit\nstrategy. Invalid version pins, invalid pre-release strategies, and\nconflicting version/pre-release settings fail before invoking `uv` so\nthe installer does not forward ambiguous or unsafe arguments.","verified_at":"2026-06-13T06:58:27Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d1c6946218b4f0f86ab7b02b6bb6af1e4b75cede","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d1c6946218b4f0f86ab7b02b6bb6af1e4b75cede","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d1c6946218b4f0f86ab7b02b6bb6af1e4b75cede/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzc