:** add default `subagent` bridge\n([#3850](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3850))\n([85fd7c2](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/85fd7c283da6744e403a01861e17e99e13e0f481))\n\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n* **quickjs:** remove `skills_backend`\n([#3843](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3843))\n([1159e50](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1159e504abaeec4f81d5e777ecde6a6cee641edb))\n\n---\n\n_Everything above this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-12T20:57:31Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/64b4b9cee7f6c6699c91b863b8dcbfb27e8fa69d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/64b4b9cee7f6c6699c91b863b8dcbfb27e8fa69d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/64b4b9cee7f6c6699c91b863b8dcbfb27e8fa69d/comments","author":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"27f38c51f960941e102dfc2f9c0220bc16736749","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/27f38c51f960941e102dfc2f9c0220bc16736749","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/27f38c51f960941e102dfc2f9c0220bc16736749"}]},{"sha":"27f38c51f960941e102dfc2f9c0220bc16736749","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDI3ZjM4YzUxZjk2MDk0MWUxMDJkZmMyZjljMDIyMGJjMTY3MzY3NDk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-12T18:52:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-12T18:52:41Z"},"message":"fix(sdk,code): rename trace version metadata to `lc_versions` (#3928)\n\nPackage-version trace metadata is now reported under\n`metadata[\"lc_versions\"]` instead of `metadata[\"versions\"]`.\n\n---\n\nFollows langchain-ai/langchain#38110, which moved package-version trace\nmetadata from the user-owned `metadata[\"versions\"]` key to the\nLangChain-owned `metadata[\"lc_versions\"]` key.\n\n`langchain-core` now only accumulates nested mappings under\n`lc_versions` when merging metadata (generic keys are last-writer-wins).\nThe SDK (`create_deep_agent`) and the `dcode` CLI\n(`build_stream_config`) both seed package versions into trace metadata,\nso they must use `lc_versions` for those entries to survive the merge\nand coexist with core/partner versions.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"8d2e6381a77059c38a27a806a3d69de080ba1551","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/8d2e6381a77059c38a27a806a3d69de080ba1551"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/27f38c51f960941e102dfc2f9c0220bc16736749","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLFV5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5P8QAB/9y8zB3E87M0dd2nuX4zn5\ncsJ9meTjw5ZVsEt9MdfRYBUiqqpooVl15xwuAUWSxzwN2hGPVkZkheqfPhNkfgSj\n2YUw0K2orcb34Y6UVALJ5HVRCZ4hVzYdctvtC/iF7jvjKM8x4PEPKxEN5m9lbebN\n6jkvR0BZKFN3piMbsEpm8xaUIFh6U6GaK4GDGeSFL04DjDjm9rET+1P9zW/d6agw\nBzPh1UIYke3cbeYOZICs1YsEbxnqv3lhBJg7m15k7nVEWMBY9Xs+v7+YjdhMRceM\nxyMLjtx8KdiRMhvdd92+vyHgbIAXEw2f15ersxaT4HO0xZzrulGWx16dYCkkFV20\nI3Rff20xJpqBz1jblxe+6c3ekJtlCtU2PsPtuJli5EYXaGRej/uFh01apTsZU48B\n8l7NWyFAuBme1tglRO4aPbB5NdNSCyKrgmol9HRtbH5euRjFu23QeMXgaSL+HMNs\nVHhqH5tEDMAK1aD5Xk/3hbdYGMUKJ0Nc4QmbqvEP53vfYr3iLp7tzj59qYuc9CeF\n9mvN44C11/L/5JUzhSK4zln+3OvQYrgeJqnmRcwtdHuYKr/c5oJJDSiyKOVXRlP9\n7b4prpUaGjjytYNXoNmMwpyIvvsxGjnO2uP2OHf7F6rv2S2M70JvIxUaw9t7Fppc\nk44RuQ3P3EGGUw/XZ1GZ\n=jUv4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8d2e6381a77059c38a27a806a3d69de080ba1551\nparent a6ec9d0e797a8b8a7d53d7debb197bb25e80be41\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781290361 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781290361 -0400\n\nfix(sdk,code): rename trace version metadata to `lc_versions` (#3928)\n\nPackage-version trace metadata is now reported under\n`metadata[\"lc_versions\"]` instead of `metadata[\"versions\"]`.\n\n---\n\nFollows langchain-ai/langchain#38110, which moved package-version trace\nmetadata from the user-owned `metadata[\"versions\"]` key to the\nLangChain-owned `metadata[\"lc_versions\"]` key.\n\n`langchain-core` now only accumulates nested mappings under\n`lc_versions` when merging metadata (generic keys are last-writer-wins).\nThe SDK (`create_deep_agent`) and the `dcode` CLI\n(`build_stream_config`) both seed package versions into trace metadata,\nso they must use `lc_versions` for those entries to survive the merge\nand coexist with core/partner versions.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-12T18:52:41Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/27f38c51f960941e102dfc2f9c0220bc16736749","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/27f38c51f960941e102dfc2f9c0220bc16736749","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/27f38c51f960941e102dfc2f9c0220bc16736749/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a6ec9d0e797a8b8a7d53d7debb197bb25e80be41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a6ec9d0e797a8b8a7d53d7debb197bb25e80be41","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a6ec9d0e797a8b8a7d53d7debb197bb25e80be41"}]},{"sha":"a6ec9d0e797a8b8a7d53d7debb197bb25e80be41","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGE2ZWM5ZDBlNzk3YThiOGE3ZDUzZDdkZWJiMTk3YmIyNWU4MGJlNDE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-12T18:39:48Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-12T18:39:48Z"},"message":"fix(sdk): don't swallow `TypeError` from custom `token_counter` (#3927)\n\n`SummarizationMiddleware` decides when to compact a conversation by\nasking a `token_counter` how large the history is. It tries to call that\ncounter *with* the tool definitions, and previously wrapped the call in\na `try/except TypeError` that retried without tools on failure. The\ncatch couldn't tell \"this counter's signature doesn't accept `tools`\"\napart from \"this counter has a real bug\" — so a `TypeError` raised\ninside a user-supplied counter (a tokenizer choking on an odd tool\nschema, a `None` where a string was expected, etc.) was silently\nswallowed and retried in a degraded mode that returned an undercount.\nThe agent would then never compact and overflow the context window, or\ncompact at the wrong moment, with no error, log, or traceback pointing\nat the actual culprit — turning a one-line bug into hours of wrong-tree\ndebugging.\n\n## Changes\n- Replace the call-and-catch probe in `_count_tokens` with explicit\nsignature introspection: a new `_token_counter_accepts_tools` helper\ninspects the counter once and returns whether it declares a `tools`\nparameter (or `**kwargs`).\n- Resolve that decision a single time in\n`SummarizationMiddleware.__init__` and store it, so the per-call\ncounting path — the hot path optimized in #3877 — pays no `inspect`\ncost.\n- Counters that accept `tools` are now called with them and any in-body\n`TypeError` propagates loudly; counters that clearly don't are called\nwithout them; only genuinely un-introspectable callables (e.g. C-level)\nfall back to the old defensive probe. The default\n`count_tokens_approximately` declares `tools`, so its behavior is\nunchanged.","tree":{"sha":"da79a56e5f740d12d275a5604728476aebbd38f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/da79a56e5f740d12d275a5604728476aebbd38f5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/a6ec9d0e797a8b8a7d53d7debb197bb25e80be41","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLFJ0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASXkQABguTkftuGy/w5Sd9f3Zg+su\nx5txyJrkJ6oXD0Bkspr0OGe8OYpWuH4mWvW3DDcVLUnW9fHY7495qhND3BJAnSPq\nju0XqdQrbjEh5CzugWCTMTcp8IJO2wSQuwueWEZerQCzMYxuNYykvYhdL6uKz4Sz\nj2X2mA5OvbviRLGSXSPJZ3YfckqAqYJDYiIOKh0aY9lHnJZw8d1WgRSpRSpkjlCN\nWY9Nj4FgRjXfLCTqckLCffKkRntL68s90Sbt/Dm0pY7srhWHzC3Fq5KODRx7nBjj\nK7yEpB+3YyiE/aMCDXlwDt85KU3BuSsENRcNBHHDxW7vlCrjmArxpo1BxEdv8N2M\nm6NapB1JZFPdiajbMIPm8C24/KcLIhQMn7h9NULJjd8QYOkNQEQAfdejhhBQpnS/\nC1kynt9SPvLfV7pKUKwBYynE5RFz25RRUiPL/J3tCH+lCvwi8Jd2mcH0EPyMv5Y+\n8zE+0A3sBmA9k+WtGBUdtAa1KirFrzV7ubPFm8HMF0CrvxPYAHqDMswXHW56KR7j\nCxyObsCvF7D+h6yzseV8KalKg3fcgF3y1XSLabe7nz6IyGgytGt4MWf+MZud3gL2\ns1buhZdLmuhWhiH1cjlF8BdaXQdxn1MUlo9TIB2o9DikXGh78m5tqCw5Z1vd8m+I\nNljNLOl6HE+YKZHMhBKi\n=RneS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree da79a56e5f740d12d275a5604728476aebbd38f5\nparent d13f3fdea8db20477fc5a440d9a10e454643ae2b\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781289588 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781289588 -0400\n\nfix(sdk): don't swallow `TypeError` from custom `token_counter` (#3927)\n\n`SummarizationMiddleware` decides when to compact a conversation by\nasking a `token_counter` how large the history is. It tries to call that\ncounter *with* the tool definitions, and previously wrapped the call in\na `try/except TypeError` that retried without tools on failure. The\ncatch couldn't tell \"this counter's signature doesn't accept `tools`\"\napart from \"this counter has a real bug\" — so a `TypeError` raised\ninside a user-supplied counter (a tokenizer choking on an odd tool\nschema, a `None` where a string was expected, etc.) was silently\nswallowed and retried in a degraded mode that returned an undercount.\nThe agent would then never compact and overflow the context window, or\ncompact at the wrong moment, with no error, log, or traceback pointing\nat the actual culprit — turning a one-line bug into hours of wrong-tree\ndebugging.\n\n## Changes\n- Replace the call-and-catch probe in `_count_tokens` with explicit\nsignature introspection: a new `_token_counter_accepts_tools` helper\ninspects the counter once and returns whether it declares a `tools`\nparameter (or `**kwargs`).\n- Resolve that decision a single time in\n`SummarizationMiddleware.__init__` and store it, so the per-call\ncounting path — the hot path optimized in #3877 — pays no `inspect`\ncost.\n- Counters that accept `tools` are now called with them and any in-body\n`TypeError` propagates loudly; counters that clearly don't are called\nwithout them; only genuinely un-introspectable callables (e.g. C-level)\nfall back to the old defensive probe. The default\n`count_tokens_approximately` declares `tools`, so its behavior is\nunchanged.","verified_at":"2026-06-12T18:39:49Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a6ec9d0e797a8b8a7d53d7debb197bb25e80be41","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a6ec9d0e797a8b8a7d53d7debb197bb25e80be41","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a6ec9d0e797a8b8a7d53d7debb197bb25e80be41/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d13f3fdea8db20477fc5a440d9a10e454643ae2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d13f3fdea8db20477fc5a440d9a10e454643ae2b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d13f3fdea8db20477fc5a440d9a10e454643ae2b"}]},{"sha":"d13f3fdea8db20477fc5a440d9a10e454643ae2b","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGQxM2YzZmRlYThkYjIwNDc3ZmM1YTQ0MGQ5YTEwZTQ1NDY0M2FlMmI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-12T18:19:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-12T18:19:44Z"},"message":"test(sdk): rename benchmark event loop fixture (#3925)\n\nThe summarization middleware benchmarks now avoid overriding\npytest-asyncio's reserved `event_loop` fixture, which is deprecated and\nmay break as pytest-asyncio changes that customization path. The\nbenchmark module also points contributors at the package Makefile\ntargets that match the local and CodSpeed benchmark entry points.","tree":{"sha":"572da359ad917641dc38ca1cb9c1c5cb2909fe60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/572da359ad917641dc38ca1cb9c1c5cb2909fe60"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/d13f3fdea8db20477fc5a440d9a10e454643ae2b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLE3ACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAO2oQAFYXtOYWq7dl0C3GkV7M4M8Y\ni/UJk+wa5R7rClV1ATugBV/yX3FPqEn1CldKv/+0pmD8CrD5CUtCcFMtSPbpdl98\nIAFWFjYtHqMY2PIRz7NubmT+r1NO8f827XJPoCP17a/3HoIBLnwhCWW2/C67FP0+\ntf03yWOm/QOjybsqld3A0rg+q79NP91eidipP5Ysj34uwR4sycDqwrrfrn3DFOKE\nkO2MeR83Z2PM6QgbuctDaB8Sn0SRbF5fOnCCUBBdA9Wr+8DTXb94Kesz7ELwBHR2\nxRaUWbqzo7bSc8GHvpFBTYEeC5xrveWpl1N1oJVl/EPmPH5/xv2u/PDUwYURo+Gf\nDyU979LlsAxSfUtRfiubRe79rBBLdv3xxM32+VKhPybojmLcCI1d8SYDCfyHwF7u\nRPPfdSr8HzzLxCSY3XQV2V+3Aeav+zcQJ4HcFLFFk8sv/77HkhCWJ7ADtlWWuslq\nLsDl4D+Ju8fx0HpqWsCFSkTXuMX10LvytH1YvYyDApxF+sLmZ3KDT5Eh5vOnT+kN\nc6gKv80rEMNh8MDT9VI3Nm7M50nXghcPxmQLrSDtIFmU2JVdToNS/Q7qU4YjMUEi\n5UPRAzqhfXnp3sRPEwuq/Ue9Cg6iJ4JWAFCSs6D5E7BHXwVWf4HWlosElYm5pfgT\nLtJpc2MZ5Y0au2ScHcoW\n=qpaU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 572da359ad917641dc38ca1cb9c1c5cb2909fe60\nparent 3396b442b22b2ff76cb7c656afa3b24735e1395d\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781288384 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781288384 -0400\n\ntest(sdk): rename benchmark event loop fixture (#3925)\n\nThe summarization middleware benchmarks now avoid overriding\npytest-asyncio's reserved `event_loop` fixture, which is deprecated and\nmay break as pytest-asyncio changes that customization path. The\nbenchmark module also points contributors at the package Makefile\ntargets that match the local and CodSpeed benchmark entry points.","verified_at":"2026-06-12T18:19:44Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d13f3fdea8db20477fc5a440d9a10e454643ae2b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d13f3fdea8db20477fc5a440d9a10e454643ae2b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d13f3fdea8db20477fc5a440d9a10e454643ae2b/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3396b442b22b2ff76cb7c656afa3b24735e1395d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3396b442b22b2ff76cb7c656afa3b24735e1395d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3396b442b22b2ff76cb7c656afa3b24735e1395d"}]},{"sha":"3396b442b22b2ff76cb7c656afa3b24735e1395d","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDMzOTZiNDQyYjIyYjJmZjc2Y2I3YzY1NmFmYTNiMjQ3MzVlMTM5NWQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-12T18:17:03Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-12T18:17:03Z"},"message":"ci(infra): deep-link dispatched `release.yml` runs from the `trigger-releases` summary (#3916)\n\nWhen a release PR merges, `trigger-releases` dispatches `release.yml`\nper package via `gh workflow run`, but the `workflow_dispatch` API\ndoesn't return the created run's ID — so the step summary could only\nlink the `release.yml` workflow *page*, leaving the operator to hunt for\nthe run that was just kicked off. Each dispatched run now gets a direct,\nclickable link in the summary.\n\n## Changes\n- Correlate each dispatch to its run by polling `gh run list` and\nmatching on `release.yml`'s `run-name` (`release(<package>):\n<version>`), then render the result as a markdown deep-link in\n`$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY`. The lookup passes `package`/`version` to `jq`\nvia `--arg` (data, not program) and matches on exact `displayTitle` so\n`deepagents` and `deepagents-code` can't cross-match.\n- Run correlation as a second pass (`locate_run`) *after* every dispatch\nrather than inline, so a slow or missed lookup can never delay — or, if\nthe job times out mid-poll, starve — the dispatch of later packages. A\nsingle backdated `DISPATCH_STARTED` timestamp bounds the search window\nagainst clock skew.\n- Keep it strictly best-effort: the poll is bounded (`max_poll=90s`),\nand a miss emits a `::warning::` and falls back to plain text pointing\nat the workflow page. Nothing in the correlation path can fail the job\nor affect dispatch success/failure accounting.","tree":{"sha":"26d3cd8701d15da8337e6c652d9dbd26c152d1ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/26d3cd8701d15da8337e6c652d9dbd26c152d1ca"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/3396b442b22b2ff76cb7c656afa3b24735e1395d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLE0fCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6FoQAJlA1rB0MqeFdMQkcGRdYAtv\nvaJ1RVIiuX7stUsKwoKwVwEdE6nSO986pUjuLw0ovvq8uckltlbp45FOnIR1qqwH\nsIY8kBtD2ofPxdhsl27nYdOCgNek7hpYUp/U/7U/MYncDTjV1LDxdZ+K6ZnUjWMT\nzTA/RyGKughOY9qo9or11jQfrCFcRgZ62HTA0hiQRPj5RGjlnRH+hhOTXfXb/cdy\nmc4Pv+sKVfGuBg2IjAkEka6dCa5iWYvUPWXQAZhVl5VLysxZGqs+KwZRCAjcxtvi\nCOZ31SN6IwP8EnhwybyxOMoyNfHrHvVSXq2+K6wpODNwa9ECnX8QIeCX1iKxMF1U\nO2hTzYI1yb457NGvyOUl5kCPV9gQz38+NQtUMbxCxdsHCzl8YSps0id5Z1QMtyLj\njlF7p5QhcFIBf6VsgEYKIZ360pco7B2TVd+BGqSitFBDUYyYNsoVccUsnprbTCSe\nS17tiKKxOQfysesI+L/hG7mWYEIHihKHrCk9aadl2PxgMxChHu9LRE7Mg+49kZcb\nNMBDM5gpncZkbWW02lZy1OAeB42BZ5LPSbRl82DHAkOgdp1WsVMkEkAIsKC7qlpn\nQox8Id2//JnG/T59Og27n9TAHdJe7Ymz1L1bqT3wbubuZhd687Y05zTNKoUqOYo5\nSKngF/RcdDjKjbDkyVzA\n=1qKu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 26d3cd8701d15da8337e6c652d9dbd26c152d1ca\nparent 6558c8ca3d8e10e3309f95c807e740914af3175f\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781288223 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781288223 -0400\n\nci(infra): deep-link dispatched `release.yml` runs from the `trigger-releases` summary (#3916)\n\nWhen a release PR merges, `trigger-releases` dispatches `release.yml`\nper package via `gh workflow run`, but the `workflow_dispatch` API\ndoesn't return the created run's ID — so the step summary could only\nlink the `release.yml` workflow *page*, leaving the operator to hunt for\nthe run that was just kicked off. Each dispatched run now gets a direct,\nclickable link in the summary.\n\n## Changes\n- Correlate each dispatch to its run by polling `gh run list` and\nmatching on `release.yml`'s `run-name` (`release(<package>):\n<version>`), then render the result as a markdown deep-link in\n`$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY`. The lookup passes `package`/`version` to `jq`\nvia `--arg` (data, not program) and matches on exact `displayTitle` so\n`deepagents` and `deepagents-code` can't cross-match.\n- Run correlation as a second pass (`locate_run`) *after* every dispatch\nrather than inline, so a slow or missed lookup can never delay — or, if\nthe job times out mid-poll, starve — the dispatch of later packages. A\nsingle backdated `DISPATCH_STARTED` timestamp bounds the search window\nagainst clock skew.\n- Keep it strictly best-effort: the poll is bounded (`max_poll=90s`),\nand a miss emits a `::warning::` and falls back to plain text pointing\nat the workflow page. Nothing in the correlation path can fail the job\nor affect dispatch success/failure accounting.","verified_at":"2026-06-12T18:17:04Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3396b442b22b2ff76cb7c656afa3b24735e1395d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3396b442b22b2ff76cb7c656afa3b24735e1395d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3396b442b22b2ff76cb7c656afa3b24735e1395d/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6558c8ca3d8e10e3309f95c807e740914af3175f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6558c8ca3d8e10e3309f95c807e740914af3175f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/6558c8ca3d8e10e3309f95c807e740914af3175f"}]},{"sha":"6558c8ca3d8e10e3309f95c807e740914af3175f","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDY1NThjOGNhM2Q4ZTEwZTMzMDlmOTVjODA3ZTc0MDkxNGFmMzE3NWY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Nick Hollon","email":"nick.hollon@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-12T17:54:10Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-12T17:54:10Z"},"message":"perf(sdk): count tokens once per model call in summarization middleware (#3877)\n\n`SummarizationMiddleware.wrap_model_call` / `awrap_model_call` counted\ntokens over the full effective history twice on every model call — once\ninside `_truncate_args` and again for the should-summarize check — even\non the common path where nothing is truncated or summarized. The count\nis expensive because counting with `tools=` converts every tool schema\non every invocation; in a production deep-agent trace with 23 tools this\nmiddleware added roughly 280ms to every model call, and the duplicate\ncount is half of that.\n\nThe count now runs once per call and is passed into `_truncate_args` via\na new keyword-only `total_tokens` parameter that defaults to computing\nitself, so existing direct callers are unaffected. A recount happens\nonly when truncation actually modified messages (which changes the\ntotal).\n\nRelated: langchain-ai/langchain#38073 addresses the underlying\nper-conversion tool-schema cost.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","tree":{"sha":"a2f214593ea2424e832f6edb6f9138e812976de4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a2f214593ea2424e832f6edb6f9138e812976de4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/6558c8ca3d8e10e3309f95c807e740914af3175f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLEfCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjBYQAGcIRjcb69+Nmw/KrpJbFbKv\njyzCCFTOVc14W6y+TwNmrdPPq7x9uYQ/7JpWQ80wtNdER5yybN/dtj3/dzREJNq1\nQpBMoUYhSTbq0JeNElYRkSIPYZu6dbuT6vnupT7KR8KHkSjht3f6rj0DZh/5OIWc\nFNIkIyQkL0A+u359kJIr98kZBaBZVJ0v4Kr0+lWcZk2HCuZk3z3F3szQF/bAHM4a\nXMZm5+ViaSvJcUsTP4M/jjZavjmA1QscyOM1nPEf6MnTR6xb81njLN4oTEKjypJl\nC6rQrc1DaS1Id5ErR30DifIcvxFN//lrUXMDzWCqD+WJGQEVTw+eShDphEBSVjMd\n1maBe9RZILxsUCYQDPGm9069pJuRy5sxO57IoLoIOG5jZJ/7/V7/aoU3ic3F+nLC\nBqerciBHzKx1fyFij63NMnbhNK8DCCqkrr8mgl/JwsqkUGR79IQIbUb3+vO0u7vE\nzK4GNRf5yyu4XXUerJ7esaK642jMtus2cQipfgE12BMIthqn21r/C1SVFoYfW9y2\na6GfDHEmgp/wJfhAUAIWEObCPwjuLu2aOyiOCS10lVeN214yxJXn/8K+969tQshG\ncvvOSr2ao/EyV5PDWhxegAI0HiqPTT7vq9jyTUabhhjdNYDS/xOY4YcLQkA7XBGZ\nsXoBWUzmMk4rLxzASg/E\n=2RAX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a2f214593ea2424e832f6edb6f9138e812976de4\nparent 9dbf1d25d63cd539921b33bac9270234614c6fff\nauthor Nick Hollon <nick.hollon@langchain.dev> 1781286850 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781286850 -0400\n\nperf(sdk): count tokens once per model call in summarization middleware (#3877)\n\n`SummarizationMiddleware.wrap_model_call` / `awrap_model_call` counted\ntokens over the full effective history twice on every model call — once\ninside `_truncate_args` and again for the should-summarize check — even\non the common path where nothing is truncated or summarized. The count\nis expensive because counting with `tools=` converts every tool schema\non every invocation; in a production deep-agent trace with 23 tools this\nmiddleware added roughly 280ms to every model call, and the duplicate\ncount is half of that.\n\nThe count now runs once per call and is passed into `_truncate_args` via\na new keyword-only `total_tokens` parameter that defaults to computing\nitself, so existing direct callers are unaffected. A recount happens\nonly when truncation actually modified messages (which changes the\ntotal).\n\nRelated: langchain-ai/langchain#38073 addresses the underlying\nper-conversion tool-schema cost.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","verified_at":"2026-06-12T17:54:11Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6558c8ca3d8e10e3309f95c807e740914af3175f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/6558c8ca3d8e10e3309f95c807e740914af3175f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6558c8ca3d8e10e3309f95c807e740914af3175f/comments","author":{"login":"nick-hollon-lc","id":274035459,"node_id":"U_kgDOEFVzAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274035459?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc","html_url":"https://github.com/nick-hollon-lc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9dbf1d25d63cd539921b33bac9270234614c6fff","url":"https://api.github.com/re