.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/7c9eb0090880d0beeb494c7679573640c82132b2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqK4stCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0swQAIy5aVfIPm8lkISuDURtiPvD\n5UbbIimgdB8NEQ0HSg0T1uEqTmpHEp6l6vw3+JxGQ3anyoG5cGoX1Yc1kurnQKGw\nhlaLP8Ko9k6cLkut+U8keGyhZ5skKP3+ncF4BDLYBvIWHM5l074SvZXFrO/1zuTv\nQcN0y7lCf2fu9e/XxKFKtSy895LQOxrYKbdLEAGTbhthEWRtzST2oc+JGAko3WXw\n1BkuC4zNYJYZO5zJfr22xpj/6rz+bCROI0IERRI2LaukHCP2Vp1j1XRk8D6yriuH\n4duRY2+XQmOK6rqNaZ2HpuNj72YBZWMuMDjymTYfy7PEF+QWUYd0ZVG3PZNQP7ab\ngXutT2AYQh5WEewJX5cETFA4PpS7tieIz5TI6eV+CoB3X9UZSzh6rTJasgqzqrj+\nlVdxVNx0pGMUrivdm7hZwk/nU9mAhxiNZeqFPvdVxh+u4dzEebGt/vN4jfcHhuaM\nuWHS2p/1HtXAGNiVc1Gc8VejN/AU2vZccv+sZEqYjh/WMtTXnlTY0q2uPi8VFcwS\noAAboQRD/NgJWf7odtO4NqMHkxVLyCaWkylgSqYE/dTU7Ss1V4cN899l/Vm635Ms\nV+8BQVP1mjVkslFeUjMkhNrhQ1HUMJhLxg0MnMY2vyN7pn0d4VlZoOc4jnxflEs1\nBEdDzoglsG+KCihJA2TF\n=+nsO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3fbac8699d9a32983cb3b9674f885cb91784d888\nparent b79e54b4c372fa773848ea84a9e1803278f23e7f\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781238573 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781238573 -0400\n\nchore(sdk): use public agent state exports (#3904)\n\nDeep Agents now references LangChain's public agent state type exports\ninstead of the deprecated private aliases. The `create_deep_agent` type\nsurface stays the same conceptually, but no longer depends on names\nLangChain plans to remove.","verified_at":"2026-06-12T04:29:34Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7c9eb0090880d0beeb494c7679573640c82132b2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7c9eb0090880d0beeb494c7679573640c82132b2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7c9eb0090880d0beeb494c7679573640c82132b2/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b79e54b4c372fa773848ea84a9e1803278f23e7f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b79e54b4c372fa773848ea84a9e1803278f23e7f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b79e54b4c372fa773848ea84a9e1803278f23e7f"}]},{"sha":"b79e54b4c372fa773848ea84a9e1803278f23e7f","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGI3OWU1NGI0YzM3MmZhNzczODQ4ZWE4NGE5ZTE4MDMyNzhmMjNlN2Y","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-12T04:27:57Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-12T04:27:57Z"},"message":"refactor(ci): simplify release dep check to direct PyPI resolution (#3890)\n\nBecause `release-please-config.json` sets `separate-pull-requests:\ntrue`, a release PR only ever bumps a single package, so the\nsame-PR-bump detection and dependency-pin stripping never fired (the\nbump set was always just the released package, which can't depend on\nitself). This removes that dead machinery (`detect_package_bumps`,\n`PackageBump`, the requirement/pin filtering) and resolves each changed\nrelease manifest directly against real PyPI after stripping local\n`[tool.uv.sources]`. Supersedes #3885.\n\nNote: the `.github/workflows/check_release_deps.yml` header comment\nstill describes the old behavior; it couldn't be updated here because\nthe bot lacks `workflows` push permission.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [ ] `build_resolver_manifest` keeps all deps and drops\n`[tool.uv.sources]` while preserving resolver `[tool.uv]` keys\n- [ ] `check_release_dependencies` resolves each changed manifest and is\na no-op when none changed\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"95ea9f3dee78e7e005d637f159361b4cca6c5b8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/95ea9f3dee78e7e005d637f159361b4cca6c5b8e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/b79e54b4c372fa773848ea84a9e1803278f23e7f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqK4rNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApp8QAC/DjvqIZcdINfCHbY9m2vFC\nYo8ZQeE0C0h41bQjOEF0I6Fu9TcGMdmPm69hdppuAaOC/agwuDFFgo74IxcCOG7D\ndaTfueIhZTbS/PJdvifK0X+fcOczk5C3fDulqjCZugPPoOb/Unc3rNAfDnPgEotC\nrqkM89si+yOCxSv6DSdQGgnj/6+oD62gDM18hLUCp2nDhwZ1xSGEkkFqH1dW8vL2\nh7BtcjlvTf+Md8TF6Z1fSLsii0N6hh9g5yClZtVoEFDr87N51UDtgz/Pph42529l\nobemDE4aPb32IHxillOL/W03VSuHcFnMszrjOpBoNbzP3CpocOfWZf2kJfWsqBDb\nE/Laz9OF3QSarp2Z5+iAgejF1eVqfyqEMhl2NKNdl3nPLFsLvVVP0LxgIJtTqQOo\npQwRFMogER0jaD7NE30y/y9MOiviC2NMG6mbPGbeI1MAkZSb+hS+0wMkl/rDMMu6\nuPwqXHrMliBukITjAqjKthEhacfo9bklnBBaKglpp+1WQJznAMZA6k8On3qAHI6V\nzBJaVkOvKWiMsKd3blMbqe5qCQ/4wLiq04SkepoXKmi3ur6liWdOrUenzCuicnaM\niajFlN0BHXzx8/LfCrUqf/itLnsSYWk7CXXG7dFHLcL5EkchkJD4HM5v1NzKcnV+\nik15NkLFv4sUonLCSAWp\n=f9Cn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 95ea9f3dee78e7e005d637f159361b4cca6c5b8e\nparent d4f5a12cc6d73dc19d24d5748242705d79fa65bf\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781238477 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781238477 -0400\n\nrefactor(ci): simplify release dep check to direct PyPI resolution (#3890)\n\nBecause `release-please-config.json` sets `separate-pull-requests:\ntrue`, a release PR only ever bumps a single package, so the\nsame-PR-bump detection and dependency-pin stripping never fired (the\nbump set was always just the released package, which can't depend on\nitself). This removes that dead machinery (`detect_package_bumps`,\n`PackageBump`, the requirement/pin filtering) and resolves each changed\nrelease manifest directly against real PyPI after stripping local\n`[tool.uv.sources]`. Supersedes #3885.\n\nNote: the `.github/workflows/check_release_deps.yml` header comment\nstill describes the old behavior; it couldn't be updated here because\nthe bot lacks `workflows` push permission.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [ ] `build_resolver_manifest` keeps all deps and drops\n`[tool.uv.sources]` while preserving resolver `[tool.uv]` keys\n- [ ] `check_release_dependencies` resolves each changed manifest and is\na no-op when none changed\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-12T04:27:57Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b79e54b4c372fa773848ea84a9e1803278f23e7f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b79e54b4c372fa773848ea84a9e1803278f23e7f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b79e54b4c372fa773848ea84a9e1803278f23e7f/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d4f5a12cc6d73dc19d24d5748242705d79fa65bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d4f5a12cc6d73dc19d24d5748242705d79fa65bf","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d4f5a12cc6d73dc19d24d5748242705d79fa65bf"}]},{"sha":"d4f5a12cc6d73dc19d24d5748242705d79fa65bf","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGQ0ZjVhMTJjYzZkNzNkYzE5ZDI0ZDU3NDgyNDI3MDVkNzlmYTY1YmY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-12T04:21:21Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-12T04:21:21Z"},"message":"feat(code): surface editable mode and core deps in `/version` (#3898)\n\n`/version` and `dcode -v` now report editable-install status and core\nLangChain dependency versions when running from a local checkout.\n\n---\n\nWhen `deepagents-code` runs from an editable install, both the\n`/version` slash command and the `dcode -v` / `--version` CLI flag now\nindicate editable mode (including the contracted source path) and list\nthe resolved versions of the core LangChain-ecosystem dependencies —\n`langchain`, `langchain-core`, `langgraph`, `langgraph-checkpoint`,\n`langgraph-prebuilt`, `langgraph-sdk`, and `langsmith`.\n\nLocal checkouts frequently pin or override these packages, so surfacing\nthem makes editable environments much easier to diagnose. Non-editable\ninstalls are unchanged. A new `build_version_text` helper centralizes\nthe CLI version string so the fast path and the argparse `version`\naction stay in sync, and a plain-text core-dependency formatter sits\nalongside the existing extras helpers (missing packages render as `not\ninstalled`). Both surfaces emit sections in the same order (versions,\neditable path, core dependencies, optional dependencies); `--version`\nomits the network-dependent release-age suffixes and update hint so it\nstays offline.\n\nOne behavior change worth calling out: consolidating the three former\n`--version` code paths into `build_version_text` means an *unexpected*\nerror while looking up the SDK version (i.e. anything other than\n`PackageNotFoundError`) is now logged at `warning` rather than `debug`,\nmatching how the `/version` slash command already logs it.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"a676fb1b3f40440c50fa4e4ea7ce9defb207f918","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a676fb1b3f40440c50fa4e4ea7ce9defb207f918"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/d4f5a12cc6d73dc19d24d5748242705d79fa65bf","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqK4lBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAne4QABRGeXDSHO3tqN8trwsKSAdR\nTlXuSkPeOaQ0jpeDmcbMhbKXGJDonyGvpF9wnYYY/R3/t798RMRJvCXadYsKPNrc\nHvxFYd7kNC/62VDSCTv/uSs5YGaRvYwGSQBPc9KloZ/C74Yznp7AY3FIzP5tnr+/\nW9dfJlVJtHkoyHdHnX6ig16CYdmJjNsx8xn/lnZ/qHKAY+/gyeSsZinajqAcDpuX\nr671/ns+3NfXY0YZBqoJQTmUdEmKOqNaadXBYZYTnmCc5H5fm1tUo3VuqaH9kCCg\nWc5aapUf0aOunOX0TeFpGIEK2irlQ+Dh1QTP8qwuA7RUR6WUNHPrRzfYdSE6H5SN\nbFn2qfdjHlAvDVBlf1ciUgSSkUvsyGFQfavuWXjdOEOFYKugdz6OxCXi3T+/dsxc\nCHUCIe3fQ+gvZWVQJQ8ROEO0oUkcvX2ZO7rJm0VUHKlOaM/xczeftQpDb3/SMa+U\nPyKK4fsngS2FbO+QPZNekII3oavReLrx87eQN9D6J7w7QhlmqkMW0QLZ85b/TpBs\ndRCUwlVG0iDi5HPWOSCqAFnC/y3G5++IfUAvF3pdKk+naSZhX79RCd1l4vCwriaF\n0ejjBM42d7Gv0CfjSDABPmTiQAc9455oZptuxxyjZHXrht7WKGbMxL1yCwG9QwQF\nHl5JOjJp/kSOWMxJouVA\n=6dZv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a676fb1b3f40440c50fa4e4ea7ce9defb207f918\nparent ac94dd6b139211187cad8685c1152f02c51ba086\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781238081 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781238081 -0400\n\nfeat(code): surface editable mode and core deps in `/version` (#3898)\n\n`/version` and `dcode -v` now report editable-install status and core\nLangChain dependency versions when running from a local checkout.\n\n---\n\nWhen `deepagents-code` runs from an editable install, both the\n`/version` slash command and the `dcode -v` / `--version` CLI flag now\nindicate editable mode (including the contracted source path) and list\nthe resolved versions of the core LangChain-ecosystem dependencies —\n`langchain`, `langchain-core`, `langgraph`, `langgraph-checkpoint`,\n`langgraph-prebuilt`, `langgraph-sdk`, and `langsmith`.\n\nLocal checkouts frequently pin or override these packages, so surfacing\nthem makes editable environments much easier to diagnose. Non-editable\ninstalls are unchanged. A new `build_version_text` helper centralizes\nthe CLI version string so the fast path and the argparse `version`\naction stay in sync, and a plain-text core-dependency formatter sits\nalongside the existing extras helpers (missing packages render as `not\ninstalled`). Both surfaces emit sections in the same order (versions,\neditable path, core dependencies, optional dependencies); `--version`\nomits the network-dependent release-age suffixes and update hint so it\nstays offline.\n\nOne behavior change worth calling out: consolidating the three former\n`--version` code paths into `build_version_text` means an *unexpected*\nerror while looking up the SDK version (i.e. anything other than\n`PackageNotFoundError`) is now logged at `warning` rather than `debug`,\nmatching how the `/version` slash command already logs it.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-12T04:21:22Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d4f5a12cc6d73dc19d24d5748242705d79fa65bf","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d4f5a12cc6d73dc19d24d5748242705d79fa65bf","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d4f5a12cc6d73dc19d24d5748242705d79fa65bf/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ac94dd6b139211187cad8685c1152f02c51ba086","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ac94dd6b139211187cad8685c1152f02c51ba086","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ac94dd6b139211187cad8685c1152f02c51ba086"}]},{"sha":"ac94dd6b139211187cad8685c1152f02c51ba086","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGFjOTRkZDZiMTM5MjExMTg3Y2FkODY4NWMxMTUyZjAyYzUxYmEwODY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-12T04:04:02Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-12T04:04:02Z"},"message":"fix(code): set dcode agent names in trace metadata (#3901)\n\nLangSmith trace metadata now separates dcode's selected agent name from\nAgent Server's `assistant_id`, avoiding collisions with the UUID\nassigned by LangSmith. Root dcode runs also pass the selected agent name\ninto `create_deep_agent`, so `lc_agent_name` is populated consistently\nwith LangChain's agent naming metadata.\n\n## Changes\n- Set `create_deep_agent(..., name=assistant_id)` in `create_cli_agent`\nso root runs report the selected dcode agent through `lc_agent_name`.\n- Replace dcode's custom `metadata[\"assistant_id\"]` value with\n`metadata[\"dcode_agent_name\"]`, leaving LangSmith/Agent Server ownership\nof `assistant_id` intact.\n- Keep `metadata[\"agent_name\"]` for compatibility while adding the more\nexplicit dcode-specific metadata key.\n- Clarify `build_stream_config` docs so `assistant_id` is described as\nthe dcode agent identifier in this code path.","tree":{"sha":"40d74e56375392b6aa2968d3800034fc7be709f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/40d74e56375392b6aa2968d3800034fc7be709f9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/ac94dd6b139211187cad8685c1152f02c51ba086","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqK4UyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAA58QADk1B0j5ougYIgQvHQ86Ai6i\nnZIVmyAZjk434dogYlE3ThvaYglJjLYVAPRQ89XjCUFXnxA+d4SyNIhvq81B0JCZ\nKhxjIj1G0VJJwfAhDN4qt9EmNAnPumriKLg04/nvn0MvE1c5TBnIZR2B2KiTwO1w\nV5assEX1iOagdiPDH9WgGJ+pDzCcpvH0J0O7ksQdwZ4DCaS+h1H2aGwcVs24AUos\ntPDZcFvKzYQTm44cEE371a3N+Cp342bHfrrPCqVH+NsWlAamf9DXTGmynhnfpR2v\nbulhIb8IfnAd0Dm3Uq7BM8VRlcEXmezI7rbQ81XBeqoLrUxgtJQsR0Wu9qrPi9dx\na4NgJpMrTP3tsW5npXiLnvkpXSv4RnyxkWkjLuwsFhyw6ZTfOJkp+Gp0D6ZA7nO6\nQRjNHTKYonez1pdZFfgZ74cIWvSMr9xQDldZWJl0AN5r9R9vduKT2JWFCVJbNG2e\nCTuM5a1AiicRb0NDhYcm1oJyXs7gjAPiJhG5kLtXFqVjQdfKVQ7WG/Z0jTr8HIl6\nYr2Po4adrUE5D8I1x9qx6Wl3E0YF5VK6U7zPukpzcou3y7cCJKX+7jYS5EA5FKiF\nwKR99/YhBq7TT88k/RN+0mHcDXxZpO0l4wsNRnurfkwfI3+/3CR+Lo7GL/kFKSnK\n1v54ljKjfTdq77SXZS6g\n=o8Dr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 40d74e56375392b6aa2968d3800034fc7be709f9\nparent 644498c8dd882c85d7f2e2b13536ac576b560afe\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781237042 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781237042 -0400\n\nfix(code): set dcode agent names in trace metadata (#3901)\n\nLangSmith trace metadata now separates dcode's selected agent name from\nAgent Server's `assistant_id`, avoiding collisions with the UUID\nassigned by LangSmith. Root dcode runs also pass the selected agent name\ninto `create_deep_agent`, so `lc_agent_name` is populated consistently\nwith LangChain's agent naming metadata.\n\n## Changes\n- Set `create_deep_agent(..., name=assistant_id)` in `create_cli_agent`\nso root runs report the selected dcode agent through `lc_agent_name`.\n- Replace dcode's custom `metadata[\"assistant_id\"]` value with\n`metadata[\"dcode_agent_name\"]`, leaving LangSmith/Agent Server ownership\nof `assistant_id` intact.\n- Keep `metadata[\"agent_name\"]` for compatibility while adding the more\nexplicit dcode-specific metadata key.\n- Clarify `build_stream_config` docs so `assistant_id` is described as\nthe dcode agent identifier in this code path.","verified_at":"2026-06-12T04:04:02Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ac94dd6b139211187cad8685c1152f02c51ba086","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ac94dd6b139211187cad8685c1152f02c51ba086","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ac94dd6b139211187cad8685c1152f02c51ba086/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"644498c8dd882c85d7f2e2b13536ac576b560afe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/644498c8dd882c85d7f2e2b13536ac576b560afe","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/644498c8dd882c85d7f2e2b13536ac576b560afe"}]},{"sha":"644498c8dd882c85d7f2e2b13536ac576b560afe","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDY0NDQ5OGM4ZGQ4ODJjODVkN2YyZTJiMTM1MzZhYzU3NmI1NjBhZmU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mukil Loganathan","email":"mukil@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-12T04:00:34Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-12T04:00:34Z"},"message":"fix(evals): make `DeepAgentsWrapper` temperature optional + fix langsmith make target (#3876)\n\n## Problem\n\n`DeepAgentsWrapper` passes `temperature=0.0` to `init_chat_model`\nunconditionally:\n\n```python\nself._model = init_chat_model(model_name, temperature=temperature, **model_kwargs)\n```\n\nAnthropic **Opus 4.7+ and Fable** removed sampling parameters and reject\n`temperature` with:\n\n```\nanthropic.BadRequestError: 400 - {'type': 'invalid_request_error',\n  'message': '`temperature` is deprecated for this model.'}\n```\n\nSo those models fail at the **first model call**. This includes\n`anthropic:claude-opus-4-7`, which is in the\n`.github/workflows/harbor.yml` model matrix — meaning Opus runs in CI\nhit this too.\n\nSurfaced while running terminal-bench on the LangSmith Harbor\nenvironment with `--model anthropic:claude-opus-4-8`.\n\n## Fix\n\nDefault `temperature` to `None` and forward it to `init_chat_model` only\nwhen explicitly set:\n\n```python\nif temperature is not None:\n    model_kwargs[\"temperature\"] = temperature\nself._model = init_chat_model(model_name, **model_kwargs)\n```\n\n- Models that accept `temperature` can still pass it (`--agent-kwarg\ntemperature=0.0`).\n- Models that reject it are no longer sent an invalid parameter.\n\nAdded unit tests covering omit-by-default and forward-when-set; updated\nthe existing happy-path assertion (`_temperature` now defaults to\n`None`). `ruff`, `ty`, and the wrapper unit tests pass.\n\n## 🙏 Looking for OSS input on the default\n\nThis changes the default from `temperature=0.0` → omitted. The upside is\nbroad model support out of the box (Opus 4.7+/Fable just work). The\ntradeoff: models that *do* accept `temperature` (e.g. Sonnet) are no\nlonger pinned to `0.0`, so they fall back to the provider default — a\nsmall **eval-reproducibility** shift.\n\nAlternatives considered:\n1. **This PR** — default `None` (omit), opt in per-run. Simple,\nmodel-agnostic.\n2. Keep `0.0` default but skip `temperature` for known-incompatible\nmodel families. More brittle (hardcodes model lists).\n3. Catch the 400 and retry without `temperature`. Hides the issue, costs\na round-trip.\n\nPreference / concerns welcome — happy to switch approaches.","tree":{"sha":"e28eccd628b5d16560f78066444a15d6e6f09cd2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/e28eccd628b5d16560f78066444a15d6e6f09cd2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/644498c8dd882c85d7f2e2b13536ac576b560afe","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqK4RiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcOQQAGN38Ha8xbS3805M3d1LmauZ\nEjUxUq+KSoXfTibfdjTm6aSeA9MFjbZNlH3VuOs49RvYmqDoTuAU0Lxy7PXkdeXw\n6d4TlJVqsZtCEA81P7b5rlLz3dRNheSNqqiyQ8TaE+liak63O82Wp82kMR05/6Zh\nWlwV2qQPaUXFSTQlPgMCrOuUc/HTadREyX5kJtR/cDdMu7B3Rmcs6D5t+OczQdl5\nxDJ3hsi0T2CJBsATAsP6I3V1Ojq4tPKSlA2yupmk3pIRGDzQdFlrlshwh6Avn2cM\ncB3EKcckr+A5nQMpvNFoqCAOVCfxu/inTnSis1c4awRn65AoPol5sSY6SQ1Hj2KA\n3tlonm6oFvLZglkaPEoS/yvZn+9gVQLsjQovTXuYGJPR81Su6VTE/akGDZi3kkOo\nnbfp38EDrLyHBJnJo1vL6ZgnB33kUGX0OWY8XqTrc7oqMcvtTzn22EFlMgRflBWi\nFS0wS2pzjo/EJl5OYRREwbhjsFw+rAmi5e2wJFG4wt35+YE+1HZHdqRlpAZtBx6T\nj3NJgZ4r8egRZN/QCSxAgJiuSZSTpEWzZVnMSXKSTIyR6bBgQk+je34PFEfNoL+6\nfWuwjyUBX4gfW2a+6cDp7902ic4WPAGLw6npY60J7a4jjfJRuz0Hp9teE8veqXTM\nkfMBjSWSg8QILddOKfgp\n=Ko6p\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e28eccd628b5d16560f78066444a15d6e6f09cd2\nparent 631bccbea7e717abfa3cf93b65afbae179f58150\nauthor Mukil Loganathan <mukil@langchain.dev> 1781236834 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781236834 -0400\n\nfix(evals): make `DeepAgentsWrapper` temperature optional + fix langsmith make target (#3876)\n\n## Problem\n\n`DeepAgentsWrapper` passes `temperature=0.0` to `init_chat_model`\nunconditionally:\n\n```python\nself._model = init_chat_model(model_name, temperature=temperature, **model_kwargs)\n```\n\nAnthropic **Opus 4.7+ and Fable** removed sampling parameters and reject\n`temperature` with:\n\n```\nanthropic.BadRequestError: 400 - {'type': 'invalid_request_error',\n  'message': '`temperature` is deprecated for this model.'}\n```\n\nSo those models fail at the **first model call**. This includes\n`anthropic:claude-opus-4-7`, which is in the\n`.github/workflows/harbor.yml` model matrix — meaning Opus runs in CI\nhit this too.\n\nSurfaced while running terminal-bench on the LangSmith Harbor\nenvironment with `--model anthropic:claude-opus-4-8`.\n\n## Fix\n\nDefault `temperature` to `None` and forward it to `init_chat_model` only\nwhen explicitly set:\n\n```python\nif temperature is not None:\n    model_kwargs[\"temperature\"] = temperature\nself._model = init_chat_model(model_name, **model_kwargs)\n```\n\n- Models that accept `temperature` can still pass it (`--agent-kwarg\ntemperature=0.0`).\n- Models that reject it are no longer sent an invalid parameter.\n\nAdded unit tests covering omit-by-default and forward-when-set; updated\nthe existing happy-path assertion (`_temperature` now defaults to\n`None`). `ruff`, `ty`, and the wrapper unit tests pass.\n\n## 🙏 Looking for OSS input on the default\n\nThis changes the default from `temperature=0.0` → omitted. The upside is\nbroad model support out of the box (Opus 4.7+/Fable just work). The\ntradeoff: models that *do* accept `temperature` (e.g. Sonnet) are no\nlonger pinned to `0.0`, so they fall back to the provider default — a\nsmall **eval-reproducibility** shift.\n\nAlternatives considered:\n1. **This PR** — default `None` (omit), opt in per-run. Simple,\nmodel-agnostic.\n2. Keep `0.0` default but skip `temperature` for known-incompatible\nmodel families. More brittle (hardcodes model lists).\n3. Catch the 400 and retry without `temperature`. Hides the issue, costs\na round-trip.\n\nPreference / concerns welcome — happy to switch approaches.","verified_at":"2026-06-12T04:00:35Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/644498c8dd882c85d7f2e2b13536ac576b560afe","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/644498c8dd882c85d7f2e2b13536ac576b560afe","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/644498c8dd882c85d7f2e2b13536ac576b560afe/comments","author":{"login":"langchain-infra","id":144731603,"node_id":"U_kgDOCKBt0w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/144731603?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-infra","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-infra","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-infra/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-infra/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-infra/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-infra/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-infra/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-infra/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-infra/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-infra/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-infra/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"631bccbea7e717abfa3cf93b65afbae179f58150","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/631bccbea7e717abfa3cf93b65afbae179f58150","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/631bccbea7e717abfa3cf93b65afbae179f58150"}]},{"sha":"631bccbea7e717abfa3cf93b65afbae179f58150","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDYzMWJjY2JlYTdlNzE3YWJmYTNjZjkzYjY1YWZiYWUxNzlmNTgxNTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-12T03:53:50Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-12T03:53:50Z"},"message":"refactor(code): make local context private state (#3900)\n\nLocal context is now cached under a private state field so it can still\nbe injected into model prompts without appearing in public graph outputs\nor trace state. This keeps the cached context available across local\ncontext refreshes while avoiding unnecessary state exposure.\n\n## Changes\n- Renamed the cached context state key from `local_context` to\n`_local_context` and marked it with `PrivateStateAttr` on\n`LocalContextState`.\n- Updated `LocalContextMiddleware.before_agent` and\n`LocalContextMiddleware.abefore_agent` to read, write, and preserve\n`_local_context` during initial detection and post-summarization\nrefreshes.\n- Kept refresh failure behavior unchanged: failed detections still\nrecord `_local_context_refreshed_at_cutoff` without overwriting the\nexisting cached context.\n- Updated prompt injection in\n`LocalContextMiddleware._get_modified_request` to source local context\nfrom the private state field.","tree":{"sha":"dfd99948514a72ea561b81c979f76f2124f22db8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/dfd99948514a72ea561b81c979f76f2124f22db8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/631bccbea7e717abfa3cf93b65afbae179f58150","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqK4LOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA91AQAI45yOENpIBHqWFD/GsIQa3V\nFa4zPlJA0px9w8f5vaCEBrN31YDeYzvVpArIGZ+pq1xaOQou9/nLHzq7IFQTXeIo\nYR9/avBwOdDyhkPP+At4UqwxOcN2zCEZ7abmk8wUc0brofNnX8dZoTfIZtc8mePi\nXOB+U7k1EvKEvyQ9A/rEWeU9dDCIfUPm9LCjoen8MaDxoHXWXiheoNUqt18JNIX/\neXen9Ox66Nl4hD5ry4UeJdFMofI8WXbWez7LnzTByvUxsxpAPhwGYYz3P635FHUL\nLyvAMU0wRCoHWE5wVHxSXDXGN7hy0OPOZNmpB6HxHCGtkPTQbYsl2UjJA1ydfHPo\n/anPvm+XgNcfzkn9HTEFpAhNhWF/S9+ddr58l/4EP/9cqQ52/DOx3N/WEYaFlvmv\nIqfSzeAD6PMvUO6U+jYb8j02IpZLPHZ4BVpQ+tET5vY/T5BL6YefKkDrxdu+BlYJ\njA99sZtbRzPQgNg9Q7PZ4o2ZpvSHSYqTfcil5ZsldxpuhFeq9y0lD/L0gIAT1AIU\nQPO9OQuxIEicvcb6V9GxjBXiQtVuTj2hXTeA0ymt5na8o+Se+mFu+xxV6dXs0XTd\n24kD2yTkdWslmRofqd74tnLe6SrvhkFymKG5a1XGE+ykRf/oDvqeQdIQ1uU/y9hW\nNvsVIoZvw9szQLpOZHUy\n=2VkJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree dfd99948514a72ea561b81c979f76f2124f22db8\nparent 394e67ec8fce2fe1b4ec8b73d717862ba42858d7\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781236430 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781236430 -0400\n\nrefactor(code): make local context private state (#3900)\n\nLocal context is now cached under a private state field so it can still\nbe injected into model prompts without appearing in public graph outputs\nor trace state. This keeps the cached context available across local\ncontext refreshes while avoiding unnecessary state exposure.\n\n## Changes\n- Renamed the cached context state key from `local_context` to\n`_local_context` and marked it with `PrivateStateAttr` on\n`LocalContextState`.\n- Updated `LocalContextMiddleware.before_agent` and\n`LocalContextMiddleware.abefore_agent` to read, write, and preserve\n`_local_context` during initial detection and post-summarization\nrefreshes.\n- Kept refresh failure behavior unchanged: failed detections still\nrecord `_local_context_refreshed_at_cutoff` without overwriting the\nexisting cached context.\n- Updated prompt injection in\n`LocalContextMiddleware._get_modified_request` to source local context\nfrom the private state field.","verified_at":"2026-06-12T03:53:51Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/631bccbea7e717abfa3cf93b65afbae179f58150","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/631bccbea7e717abfa3cf93b65afbae179f58150","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/631bccbea7e717abfa3cf93b65afbae179f58150/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"394e67ec8fce2fe1b4ec8b73d717862ba42858d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/394e67ec8fce2fe1b4ec8b73d717862ba42858d7","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/394e67ec8fce2fe1b4ec8b73d717862ba42858d7"}]},{"sha":"394e67ec8fce2fe1b4ec8b73d717862ba42858d7","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDM5NGU2N2VjOGZjZTJmZTFiNGVjOGI3M2Q3MTc4NjJiYTQyODU4ZDc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-12T03:26:28Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-12T03:26:28Z"},"message":"refactor(code): stop reinjecting SDK version metadata (#3896)\n\nWith LangChain's nested metadata merge available in the supported\n`langchain-core` range, dcode no longer needs to duplicate SDK version\nmetadata at stream time. Runtime configs now report the dcode version\nonly, while the compiled deep agent graph remains responsible for\ncontributing the SDK version.","tree":{"sha":"a1b0b15ce0421305d9db87bcedb6844b61084aaa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a1b0b15ce0421305d9db87bcedb6844b61084aaa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/394e67ec8fce2fe1b4ec8b73d717862ba42858d7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqK3xkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+SoQABO/YIInfmqRmTQ0Bi8d1zib\nayxV0cw5qAzHcZ+hbiPyb/Wk/cUu7Fbl1FAxx/55FNV+x/3ggMPCHCBhgKkkVJTg\naBhBWJu7IPsiyz6pWZWxdm3eUYYzd16dS8GBx0gZhxKHQ7wJOOkhNR5oKdU1uBV4\nnQuTtQj7F7SG5bf8LXkGWNnj+ZOr9S0/iz2qr26d43gQHkVwLqzflGEcMHkT5Le5\nDT8l1Pw6f93p4uFB0Cj1DOSiIJNTti2j/EtLDNzmz6Pt8EICrnSCUMivtfUmlJA4\nTeqc2cNAsR2z4J6cBm3okMUp2b6v9LH9dkfxjd6MZn74somTtNySTP4h330CqmSe\nL4E25kqZ23BEkAPRvFVmIcfVV+S/TmcWULcwlN/XMbAJozZpXU52+GORkdMAKZFs\nF7+YNoQqPCPxlm5yZufVZqDVpTvRlL2VClHeYIF36oIktvBYn99aPFnHIAHc4Egw\nc9QWr1DiM2QmCzvinU4iy3oVbdY20W77KhrEsoI7fZYCcAI93K1YdtYRn5dzaTuH\nqvsEsFINSLqJEfpvQGpsml1/w6bqj2PFytSADnCKsVZysqSO7Yg53YzkPVuXMUwz\n0D5LOc3DyUH6LrfRy7PcjnTtkuc0QfZL6phMjUgHQjamRL5vxlNun9c74C0wUgVa\n5nG663THUo2+4XoOHHrr\n=etkf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a1b0b15ce0421305d9db87bcedb6844b61084aaa\nparent b76788b7850e910fe2882cb1a62ffff6ff5085b0\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781234788 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781234788 -0400\n\nrefactor(code): stop reinjecting SDK version metadata (#3896)\n\nWith LangChain's nested metadata merge available in the supported\n`langchain-core` range, dcode no longer needs to duplicate SDK version\nmetadata at stream time. Runtime configs now report the dcode version\nonly, while the compiled deep agent graph remains responsible for\ncontributing the SDK version.","verified_at":"2026-06-12T03:26:29Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/394e67ec8fce2fe1b4ec8b73d717862ba42858d7","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/394e67ec8fce2fe1b4ec8b73d717862ba42858d7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/394e67ec8fce2fe1b4ec8b73d717862ba42858d7/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b76788b7850e910fe2882cb1a62ffff6ff5085b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b76788b7850e910fe2882cb1a62ffff6ff5085b0","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b76788b7850e910fe2882cb1a62ffff6ff5085b0"}]},{"sha":"b76788b7850e910fe2882cb1a62ffff6ff5085b0","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGI3Njc4OGI3ODUwZTkxMGZlMjg4MmNiMWE2MmZmZmY2ZmY1MDg1YjA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-12T02:44:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-12T02:44:16Z"},"message":"fix(code): don't move cursor on click that re-focuses terminal (#3893)\n\nClicking back into the terminal to refocus no longer moves the chat\ninput cursor.\n\n---\n\nWhen the terminal window is unfocused and the user clicks back into the\nchat input, that click previously both restored focus and moved the\ncursor to the click location. The `ChatTextArea` now tracks\n`AppBlur`/`AppFocus` and treats a mouse-down landing within a short\nwindow after a focus regain as focus-only, leaving the cursor where it\nwas. Clicks while the window is already focused behave normally.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"92221222dd268749a5aa14f13b7772e916f11a51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/92221222dd268749a5aa14f13b7772e916f11a51"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/b76788b7850e910fe2882cb1a62ffff6ff5085b0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqK3KACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbgAQAITex7l/JImbCYi10GS1nRWj\nxTXtE65Gb/CoJyK5oa1tMhFQX9997Nqhj3rgijOteQBjjejNUVX+JAV9SJDiWN1J\nioEos/XxTRFGSXg8SlR1pQzvWuO2rZkWhwRSosLrIqOAqV5ndl8Xjc8GTGl1Qhf/\niKgcaAm1eTeFhLWeYBb92ZUAZDax9UWArunjR/CluBkxinR+/MimmFWI1P7xKuMb\nJor94Ucukg1xK3UZGwYlrCT9J/fW6YpSmaf2X1QjmRyatN/LaWmQRSq0iuohngSG\n+KXebxova4Lsh2nL8hUBd3eAhpw2a7ORIuSzZMuENQYpTRncADs5rnCvS3JnSo2Q\nC7caZ9YwDw6Ehm75/HealT1dOKy1Ch9hsOnqVCDvjazSRlWkAp22lU6JjAn0352r\nDJIFq+oMTUxuIa0O2u6RNOlVNRWzJmzWEP97eXZRkg7zW2pEQla5bu9zt/g4i6dp\nKsbPzMWu9e0fA1XnwYqUwWW4UyQRA1j+hbln1VqTa6JHxvfiejPw6lUX33U1fazk\nNPWvDh+5ZDdS3+ojrcSDzQ0gNgsr0XLjCY5bakKxz+swcoIgZbMfJouEUMv3clka\nHj2voG4St9g4At0Ocq8T04a2GpJyCr4mR+cg6I/io4mTLJPK97xTr3Yvyn/QrJ7j\n727EBa9mdLK2rmK2mus/\n=7Waw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 92221222dd268749a5aa14f13b7772e916f11a51\nparent 70cd28643bc2ca7da5a61a7b7203c6de2266ca4e\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781232256 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781232256 -0400\n\nfix(code): don't move cursor on click that re-focuses terminal (#3893)\n\nClicking back into the terminal to refocus no longer moves the chat\ninput cursor.\n\n---\n\nWhen the terminal window is unfocused and the user clicks back into the\nchat input, that click previously both restored focus and moved the\ncursor to the click location. The `ChatTextArea` now tracks\n`AppBlur`/`AppFocus` and treats a mouse-down landing within a short\nwindow after a focus regain as focus-only, leaving the cursor where it\nwas. Clicks while the window is already focused behave normally.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-12T02:44:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b76788b7850e910fe2882cb1a62ffff6ff5085b0","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b76788b7850e910fe2882cb1a62ffff6ff5085b0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b76788b7850e910fe2882cb1a62ffff6ff5085b0/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"70cd28643bc2ca7da5a61a7b7203c6de2266ca4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/70cd28643bc2ca7da5a61a7b7203c6de2266ca4e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/70cd28643bc2ca7da5a61a7b7203c6de2266ca4e"}]},{"sha":"70cd28643bc2ca7da5a61a7b7203c6de2266ca4e","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDcwY2QyODY0M2JjMmNhN2RhNWE2MWE3YjcyMDNjNmRlMjI2NmNhNGU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-12T02:07:45Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-12T02:07:45Z"},"message":"fix(code): label `-r` resume as `\"Resuming...\"` in the status bar (#3892)\n\n`deepagents code -r` once again shows a \"Resuming\" status while resuming\na thread instead of a generic \"Connecting\".\n\n---\n\nWhen connection progress moved from the welcome banner into the bottom\nstatus bar, the resume-specific footer was lost. As a result `dcode -r`\nrendered the generic \"Connecting\" spinner instead of the previous\n\"Resuming\" label.\n\nThis reintroduces a dedicated `resuming` connection state on the\n`StatusBar` and arms a new `_resuming` flag from the `-r` resume intent\nduring the initial connect, mirroring how `_reconnecting` is handled.\nThe flag is cleared whenever the connection clears, and reconnect\nlabeling continues to take priority.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"76e26fd9a7a5578b014307303525cc78fc8ada4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/76e26fd9a7a5578b014307303525cc78fc8ada4a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/70cd28643bc2ca7da5a61a7b7203c6de2266ca4e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqK2nxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgBkQADD6RkVSby6zZl0VL2a45KS0\np1iqEshK8Hypx0SNpiEsXD3hK7SZ3vpOdiAnaGqaD0s3gEpTRlBQOiTdImEdIwUK\nPZ+zgaWDRvzOSu4i+g/lVvAASAdEcoyHKIDBqmo5DUJAFzyKBjrukm5L1tT2FQzn\nvBlVzbHZ1CapQbTFML/Jzx+HusO9CBMyFqhUo3Y05CzzwrZee6zvq6aLspBqu3+1\nKJwIk0onKH2w4DWFxz+3TJ/5+ArCviidAdhwtLPD7uHw0BCU5NeJ+yzcbl4Rs2yj\nig8SOI/eOs+hEMJq3OPiqcvdOKS9+TP26tZZsoDJuslTy9MakkJlVwr4bM+ay+JD\nklrkaATUsBL9LMeTHgR7FGn7ITk/0kgzaikueIhoz9ChR/jxIzRcP8hPoTfx7oZd\nGAS6AELNc3KQfdYlfvB/oNjtBiKpc+tPUKFI25XBmkgDAmuPTILCI2JEJFmwZoJe\nICKTOl+5nYDnTqgSwniqr8dBhp+WT0UNninaegjUos0ddW03n9hmaZZ1Qix0kPhu\nWDM2boP4o167xmQ/X3LSaP2YAQ63tjdwZRl5vr4P0oU5MdsKq/ZR0gy+XQr0lLh9\nzMvpYndsX/zpLb9rGRN6dzyf0IqSuIlLZJxqUJQriAAOYLy7TE4buBE4M3c7PIa4\nQTw2PstAGT1z/V7JU01/\n=4p0Q\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 76e26fd9a7a5578b014307303525cc78fc8ada4a\nparent 253e180ce026557a15a3365d7f78b5bdb1da587d\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781230065 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781230065 -0400\n\nfix(code): label `-r` resume as `\"Resuming...\"` in the status bar (#3892)\n\n`deepagents code -r` once again shows a \"Resuming\" status while resuming\na thread instead of a generic \"Connecting\".\n\n---\n\nWhen connection progress moved from the welcome banner into the bottom\nstatus bar, the resume-specific footer was lost. As a result `dcode -r`\nrendered the generic \"Connecting\" spinner instead of the previous\n\"Resuming\" label.\n\nThis reintroduces a dedicated `resuming` connection state on the\n`StatusBar` and arms a new `_resuming` flag from the `-r` resume intent\nduring the initial connect, mirroring how `_reconnecting` is handled.\nThe flag is cleared whenever the connection clears, and reconnect\nlabeling continues to take priority.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-12T02:07:45Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/70cd28643bc2ca7da5a61a7b7203c6de2266ca4e","html_url":