)\n* Confirm modal for `/install --package`\n([#3840](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3840))\n([3d75026](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3d75026e2f241648fae78d9e1de2cbb4985f58ff))\n* Copy focused input selection on `Ctrl+C`\n([#3841](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3841))\n([99f782c](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/99f782cf08336c200d02a24ae4edaa650af67ed2))\n* `[retries]` config\n([#3772](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3772))\n([9334d91](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9334d91ef94997e46d5373daca9c146fa9498763))\n* Show connection state in the status bar\n([#3710](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3710))\n([3e3e8fe](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3e3e8feb0e6e1b77be75a7756fbf32e5c9497c28))\n* Surface LangSmith tracing projects in `LocalContextMiddleware`\n([#3836](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3836))\n([676abec](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/676abecf892ff537fcb1425ba5929cace3c5d503))\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n* Add debug-log guidance for truncated startup errors\n([#3849](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3849))\n([cd1ef30](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/cd1ef303cf5d0e9d746c787eb09a4a89437e965a))\n* Drop lock-key events so Caps Lock in iTerm2 doesn't type\n([#3855](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3855))\n([110f1a7](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/110f1a7a975743efda12e181cb3afc8404202254))\n* Hand pointer over splash tracing project link\n([#3858](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3858))\n([ea7dae5](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ea7dae58a37cfb1d2b96544eb7c941aad331b280))\n* Keep terminal-default theme on Esc in `/theme` selector\n([#3854](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3854))\n([c3bc67b](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c3bc67b0cdeda6f4dbcc6360ddd72b455aec4fe7))\n* Preserve inherited `PYTHONPATH` for server subprocess\n([#3833](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3833))\n([4689569](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4689569f94138987319cd9cbb45ce66a1f496934))\n* Resolve interpreter PTC allowlist against the runtime tool registry\n([#3845](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3845))\n([c59a27e](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c59a27ef2405b8e04c4351ce7ffa53d8d16d519c))\n* Treat multi-line key-event pastes as one input\n([#3856](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3856))\n([6bb15d4](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/6bb15d4bd97bd16f47504f937c8458d1b53d9cc4))\n\n---\n\n_Everything above this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-11T07:42:37Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a2a6a38b0d53efaef56d4c58ef62b284e1c638fd","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a2a6a38b0d53efaef56d4c58ef62b284e1c638fd","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a2a6a38b0d53efaef56d4c58ef62b284e1c638fd/comments","author":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"fecf22b0909e79ff7bdf180baf20abf5fdf1f390","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/fecf22b0909e79ff7bdf180baf20abf5fdf1f390","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/fecf22b0909e79ff7bdf180baf20abf5fdf1f390"}]},{"sha":"fecf22b0909e79ff7bdf180baf20abf5fdf1f390","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGZlY2YyMmIwOTA5ZTc5ZmY3YmRmMTgwYmFmMjBhYmY1ZmRmMWYzOTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"open-swe[bot]","email":"215916821+open-swe[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-11T06:51:57Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T06:51:57Z"},"message":"feat(code): auto-install ripgrep on first run (#3348)\n\nCloses #3120\n\nAuto-installs a pinned `ripgrep` binary on first run when one is not on\n`PATH`. Set `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_OFFLINE=1` to disable.\n\n---\n\nOn first launch without a system `rg`, Deep Agents Code now downloads a\npinned upstream ripgrep release, verifies its SHA-256 against an in-tree\ntable, and installs it into `~/.deepagents/bin/`. In the interactive\nTUI, `_start_server_background` awaits the one-shot install\n(`_ensure_managed_ripgrep`) and prepends `~/.deepagents/bin/` to `PATH`\n**before** spawning the langgraph server subprocess — which snapshots\n`os.environ` — so the SDK's existing `subprocess.run([\"rg\", ...])`\nresolves the managed binary with no SDK change. The headless\n(non-interactive) path installs inline in `cli_main` before launching\nthe agent.\n\nThe managed binary is re-checked on every startup against\n`RIPGREP_VERSION` (one `rg --version` probe, ~10ms) so bumping the pin\nin source automatically triggers a re-download.\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_OFFLINE` opts out of network access entirely and\npreserves the existing missing-tool notification + slow Python regex\nfallback.\n\nA SHA-256 mismatch on the downloaded archive raises a dedicated\n`ChecksumMismatchError` and aborts the install with a loud, user-visible\nnotice rather than being silently treated as \"offline\" — a mismatch is a\nsupply-chain anomaly, not a connectivity problem.\n\nThe Windows ARM entry points at the x86_64-pc-windows-msvc asset —\nupstream doesn't ship an arm64-windows build for ripgrep, and Windows on\nARM runs x64 binaries via emulation. T11 in `THREAT_MODEL.md` documents\nthe new network egress and the in-tree SHA-256 verification.\n\n_Opened collaboratively by Mason Daugherty and open-swe._\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <61371264+mdrxy@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"85ef47a0182092ef176b66c6cfd122a8244714fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/85ef47a0182092ef176b66c6cfd122a8244714fe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/fecf22b0909e79ff7bdf180baf20abf5fdf1f390","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKlsNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQyIQAKciXATEHgxpnWFlvBIO+W7y\n8fGtUoDa7cOdJ9ZamlKVlFcwHP2Z9N+tYxhWXB2iO48thB9sn9k7sDcA9Lh8Rq6e\na5uIK9A7mv78PCQIniMzNH5nr+SUCdWwMVDi9/eoN9r6+9wBXvvx711yaVkBEZXM\nMFbg42OV1p7/xuC4BCCINUI49+f/dDGGfCIkbWilViHBYrjox9U3UuYLfNF5XGph\nqDFu48j7NGWdT/IoCjZ5cvi7uD4bxs/KBiUKmjli3sJ0JhZSnjf4QCDg/cmOXwKZ\nY69BOoCXKXtG4vSQlwlfwuWkLAEwdxw2KuDjxlromOpYJZnkA0bt5hWL9FID6ynu\nLIVpsZirDVi+BI0lb0LcUpg4uKE/E8Oyu6eux6rosvDEHkSzy5boK4wmAeMEHSvH\n+biCXAa8yVVOFCREWzhm3603511FKI0t0uNRoyHlQrp8W6F0a1W5KfnhZ1LKj838\nk2J22F3gLFvUwJ47Fxhw8aDYWj+z/x3mhQA27HBg5yv8+4wCIhfxr6nqOO7HTph7\nu+V4bYB8RcEeOe2APcUj7KWnmv5XmRpITtMYwHyf5sihtcq/dKKrXuw21Z8cj08e\nPb5k97vcTJxY3J7OB9oLz3mHwp7CNZPDCc2dkQAmdA4T1z3IyYi4EMnnmvMePHpK\nrofpJJkOZV8HU33bcvhb\n=mj8e\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 85ef47a0182092ef176b66c6cfd122a8244714fe\nparent cba6caf8f708133381506ecc9e217e7e3ca1c7f2\nauthor open-swe[bot] <215916821+open-swe[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1781160717 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781160717 -0400\n\nfeat(code): auto-install ripgrep on first run (#3348)\n\nCloses #3120\n\nAuto-installs a pinned `ripgrep` binary on first run when one is not on\n`PATH`. Set `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_OFFLINE=1` to disable.\n\n---\n\nOn first launch without a system `rg`, Deep Agents Code now downloads a\npinned upstream ripgrep release, verifies its SHA-256 against an in-tree\ntable, and installs it into `~/.deepagents/bin/`. In the interactive\nTUI, `_start_server_background` awaits the one-shot install\n(`_ensure_managed_ripgrep`) and prepends `~/.deepagents/bin/` to `PATH`\n**before** spawning the langgraph server subprocess — which snapshots\n`os.environ` — so the SDK's existing `subprocess.run([\"rg\", ...])`\nresolves the managed binary with no SDK change. The headless\n(non-interactive) path installs inline in `cli_main` before launching\nthe agent.\n\nThe managed binary is re-checked on every startup against\n`RIPGREP_VERSION` (one `rg --version` probe, ~10ms) so bumping the pin\nin source automatically triggers a re-download.\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_OFFLINE` opts out of network access entirely and\npreserves the existing missing-tool notification + slow Python regex\nfallback.\n\nA SHA-256 mismatch on the downloaded archive raises a dedicated\n`ChecksumMismatchError` and aborts the install with a loud, user-visible\nnotice rather than being silently treated as \"offline\" — a mismatch is a\nsupply-chain anomaly, not a connectivity problem.\n\nThe Windows ARM entry points at the x86_64-pc-windows-msvc asset —\nupstream doesn't ship an arm64-windows build for ripgrep, and Windows on\nARM runs x64 binaries via emulation. T11 in `THREAT_MODEL.md` documents\nthe new network egress and the in-tree SHA-256 verification.\n\n_Opened collaboratively by Mason Daugherty and open-swe._\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <61371264+mdrxy@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-11T06:51:57Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/fecf22b0909e79ff7bdf180baf20abf5fdf1f390","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/fecf22b0909e79ff7bdf180baf20abf5fdf1f390","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/fecf22b0909e79ff7bdf180baf20abf5fdf1f390/comments","author":{"login":"open-swe[bot]","id":215916821,"node_id":"BOT_kgDODN6hFQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1395372?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/open-swe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"cba6caf8f708133381506ecc9e217e7e3ca1c7f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/cba6caf8f708133381506ecc9e217e7e3ca1c7f2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/cba6caf8f708133381506ecc9e217e7e3ca1c7f2"}]},{"sha":"cba6caf8f708133381506ecc9e217e7e3ca1c7f2","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGNiYTZjYWY4ZjcwODEzMzM4MTUwNmVjYzllMjE3ZTdlM2NhMWM3ZjI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Phạm Gia Linh","email":"79445383+phamgialinhlx@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-11T06:27:34Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T06:27:34Z"},"message":"fix(sdk): make sync glob timeout bound wall-clock time (#3866)\n\nFixes #3867\n\n---\n\nThe sync `glob` tool ran the backend glob in a per-call\n`ThreadPoolExecutor` inside a `with` block, so on timeout the `return`\ntriggered `shutdown(wait=True)` and blocked until the runaway glob\nfinished anyway — `GLOB_TIMEOUT` never actually bounded latency. This\nsubmits to a shared executor created at middleware init instead (no\n`with` block, >1 worker so a stuck glob can't stall the next call),\nmaking timeouts return immediately and removing per-call executor\nconstruction.\n\nNo breaking changes.\n\nVerified by: a wall-clock assertion added to the existing timeout test\n(fails on `main` with \"glob tool blocked for 2.01s past its 0.5s\ntimeout\", passes with the fix), a new test that a timed-out glob doesn't\ndelay subsequent calls, and `make format` / `make lint` / `make test`\nall passing from `libs/deepagents` (1758 passed).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"06ce60a274dbbae55fcf081f9242779f99a18202","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/06ce60a274dbbae55fcf081f9242779f99a18202"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/cba6caf8f708133381506ecc9e217e7e3ca1c7f2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKlVWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAS5oQAEL3esUxzXxPHz0vGzVlu1R5\n4ZxUG8mHfaSM8NRCYjVQDT8wNwsc5ERqlLounwiRBMci/JQgwDrV4MJ6mYiePzlO\njnLIWckeH3/RSH0nPRkkn9qf/E5ZFL62ylzk6L7FzuXdE8FB7ojQybj2gp5m+HI5\nlLdUieCFMoUuI2jub41CssFaBnjUuVMHQOeXQtUAo9wDv6tNNmXBbLmOzNQ1VulU\nugjB93aLFBLcu4mXDk4Mv1dbecSJ7ZEDf9/au2GcH2bhU9wKNitCMqWb8f6hzk2C\nXVMtdWKG3jO1+/gT8Z478WTJRzcIgtHm+g01FOCtzFj9CG+fGfOQUMjSwLMzqG7Y\nK5KtQbNlVFfIXladtGAaseDf3m3f6pT/5HkkkHFqjfbZDfL4voy+J5tGHkE32fIM\nMqaAv2YiXsM1ClWugFPsMcRGbkGLHm3r3lwV44zn1hUCQSx8uLMk7OTkx8e1+cwV\nVQC6EDEFAhCDyRTywo3imMpMTgeMF/6LA/ONAwYePd+rsSU1vi16g5iU1GSgyTcP\nkz9qvCwQrENWf35gxlvHuSi0PLriLE4iEVdOW5+VTdMRcz38v9ilB7xod6Vfelbc\nUptqtkFuW1mxNRQQm1zNUsQCv7gOH8MnkbqznyqU3wkYKn/w2N1GZZYOoHKOXMVq\njZwtE+UQGvSG3JT3Lmh6\n=FPdx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 06ce60a274dbbae55fcf081f9242779f99a18202\nparent 194b638a145d77d9ceed1d9f5ebe36b36fd08c21\nauthor Phạm Gia Linh <79445383+phamgialinhlx@users.noreply.github.com> 1781159254 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781159254 -0400\n\nfix(sdk): make sync glob timeout bound wall-clock time (#3866)\n\nFixes #3867\n\n---\n\nThe sync `glob` tool ran the backend glob in a per-call\n`ThreadPoolExecutor` inside a `with` block, so on timeout the `return`\ntriggered `shutdown(wait=True)` and blocked until the runaway glob\nfinished anyway — `GLOB_TIMEOUT` never actually bounded latency. This\nsubmits to a shared executor created at middleware init instead (no\n`with` block, >1 worker so a stuck glob can't stall the next call),\nmaking timeouts return immediately and removing per-call executor\nconstruction.\n\nNo breaking changes.\n\nVerified by: a wall-clock assertion added to the existing timeout test\n(fails on `main` with \"glob tool blocked for 2.01s past its 0.5s\ntimeout\", passes with the fix), a new test that a timed-out glob doesn't\ndelay subsequent calls, and `make format` / `make lint` / `make test`\nall passing from `libs/deepagents` (1758 passed).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-11T06:27:35Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/cba6caf8f708133381506ecc9e217e7e3ca1c7f2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/cba6caf8f708133381506ecc9e217e7e3ca1c7f2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/cba6caf8f708133381506ecc9e217e7e3ca1c7f2/comments","author":{"login":"phamgialinhlx","id":79445383,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5NDQ1Mzgz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/79445383?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/phamgialinhlx","html_url":"https://github.com/phamgialinhlx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/phamgialinhlx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/phamgialinhlx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/phamgialinhlx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/phamgialinhlx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/phamgialinhlx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/phamgialinhlx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/phamgialinhlx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/phamgialinhlx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/phamgialinhlx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"194b638a145d77d9ceed1d9f5ebe36b36fd08c21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/194b638a145d77d9ceed1d9f5ebe36b36fd08c21","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/194b638a145d77d9ceed1d9f5ebe36b36fd08c21"}]},{"sha":"194b638a145d77d9ceed1d9f5ebe36b36fd08c21","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDE5NGI2MzhhMTQ1ZDc3ZDljZWVkMWQ5ZjVlYmUzNmIzNmZkMDhjMjE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-11T05:20:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T05:20:40Z"},"message":"hotfix(code): honor `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_` prefix for `UI_CHARSET_MODE` (#3868)\n\nFixed `dcode config get display.charset` disagreeing with the runtime\nwhen both `UI_CHARSET_MODE` and `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_UI_CHARSET_MODE` are\nset.\n\n---\n\n`_detect_charset_mode` read `UI_CHARSET_MODE` directly from the\nenvironment, bypassing the `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_` prefix-override convention\nthat the rest of the config system follows. Meanwhile, `config get\ndisplay.charset` reports the option's value and source through\n`resolved_env_var_name`, which *does* honor the prefix.\n\nThe result: with both `UI_CHARSET_MODE` and\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_UI_CHARSET_MODE` set, the new config introspection\ncommand reported the prefixed value while the app actually rendered\nusing the canonical one. This change routes the runtime lookup through\n`resolve_env_var`, so the runtime and the introspection command agree on\nwhich variable wins.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"a70938e6619ab0f2126d9235abc6419131d08608","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a70938e6619ab0f2126d9235abc6419131d08608"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/194b638a145d77d9ceed1d9f5ebe36b36fd08c21","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKkWoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhrIQAG/NvVfapJZIAppIt98MPpzf\n2Qp3T4jqSfhbwHGbN17467nLvZj5+ADZ+70atDwIVJFm/l6c1souUWGsqj8HeCSt\nyRxm6BUhfs4WJTzc6se0Dj7W4uGsFEd8Ptn+bS4uLOUhOyVAlLu6K1fRLCM3CZEl\ndZJnYsnIy05SefecGVJRFl6ED/YXIkQPQMBkoT5mBj2izOc5dYS4v2hxIzi5h/O8\n1VbL0oGUc9DPify5hQe2U5f0JX12i7rssJk8Qve3LUZ8pcxj3nWtpQ0E7PP6WWIU\nIdlKMKZNWW6t/rekp+5dUoJRTyBWIcnMOL8KXhJeU0Mg6fxCM0oLmdonl4uyDBVW\nOKfLLA0Goki+wHftphmITCM1ZUQJcjjp1XgZN5tDns36Ry3hKEoOWsdJPdBzFAKN\nlQCNCHlT6VlqQLC+hGCHymCWgOUmdCyf3jzOAFFx0V+Zmdf638Qs1I+vp2bPAwIB\nJsxHPcZo4FF83kCMBIPdSYIYYT9gK3VTMCYg/K/HGPhvJeiWwonCNZgDTreBSZq2\n4Ag88lHkG0N/mNAekj3/x5mVTAOdHXd0VgDH+AnBzom3I4630MBZX1Hl2t8Yt7sF\nu7heE8VFz/wUTNvIbUyFbwuYxxcL55HiDzObJF0QcxL3KlXM5X3lX9zVDnfGmdFT\nz1jBOzw+YdYAz1GP+O8Y\n=mBX0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a70938e6619ab0f2126d9235abc6419131d08608\nparent 3e3e8feb0e6e1b77be75a7756fbf32e5c9497c28\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781155240 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781155240 -0400\n\nhotfix(code): honor `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_` prefix for `UI_CHARSET_MODE` (#3868)\n\nFixed `dcode config get display.charset` disagreeing with the runtime\nwhen both `UI_CHARSET_MODE` and `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_UI_CHARSET_MODE` are\nset.\n\n---\n\n`_detect_charset_mode` read `UI_CHARSET_MODE` directly from the\nenvironment, bypassing the `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_` prefix-override convention\nthat the rest of the config system follows. Meanwhile, `config get\ndisplay.charset` reports the option's value and source through\n`resolved_env_var_name`, which *does* honor the prefix.\n\nThe result: with both `UI_CHARSET_MODE` and\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_UI_CHARSET_MODE` set, the new config introspection\ncommand reported the prefixed value while the app actually rendered\nusing the canonical one. This change routes the runtime lookup through\n`resolve_env_var`, so the runtime and the introspection command agree on\nwhich variable wins.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-11T05:20:41Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/194b638a145d77d9ceed1d9f5ebe36b36fd08c21","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/194b638a145d77d9ceed1d9f5ebe36b36fd08c21","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/194b638a145d77d9ceed1d9f5ebe36b36fd08c21/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3e3e8feb0e6e1b77be75a7756fbf32e5c9497c28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3e3e8feb0e6e1b77be75a7756fbf32e5c9497c28","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3e3e8feb0e6e1b77be75a7756fbf32e5c9497c28"}]},{"sha":"3e3e8feb0e6e1b77be75a7756fbf32e5c9497c28","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDNlM2U4ZmViMGU2ZTFiNzdiZTc1YTc3NTZmYmYzMmU1Yzk0OTdjMjg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-11T05:01:58Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T05:01:58Z"},"message":"feat(code): show connection state in the status bar (#3710)\n\nConnection and queued-message state now stays visible in the bottom\nstatus bar, even after the welcome banner scrolls out of view. Reconnect\npaths distinguish initial startup from mid-session restarts so users can\nsee whether the app is connecting, reconnecting, or holding queued\ninput.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"6c16e32397eb4e545fdabb57ce05b99e21567b9d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/6c16e32397eb4e545fdabb57ce05b99e21567b9d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/3e3e8feb0e6e1b77be75a7756fbf32e5c9497c28","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKkFGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdgQQAJGQ5kHlEBPcMiUmwsJPMd1y\ndGjGNM8iO8yUnSUOffdiHbFeMoVYqGR7lXWh7a129Q4OyLaEEZZSUaA4sQ2IqhV7\nH8uRaUV3cwkHkVvaYNJcKfRK9gxR2o/piRbSD9rQUVAQM3DmCD/Qy2y0l0nN+9I6\nWFo/6cBaQfTXHzd1A+ZbsrMSCXPRo6xZtNOrA8oBITFSqRmycqrIsJCBXrRe8+Yf\nGe+vAKtacytz/Qj+IMKaNg9JTS9wS9P+Y4Z1JOnw8pIb85WthQvFX0K+jf7Q9YIJ\nvdxP83YQ6gxCvtJKpgf9yZj2rLCi0gX2CC4trBYbYCZIf3WFdnvCyOc0UnoLRXD6\n0/d7b1ai/ycm6e4HLXXhWdZKTkeSnlSHB67OkSHHhv2PK52w6ZBI/WNerdTsBQBL\n0hDtbqfSyMXqEyzHt7/vSfWorjJu5kRayTTisIwppsU3EIOC3EJN9oaJCe1TiJIt\nuLJEc/do/v6pWKH8Btez16wI6cej9CdtMlOXPENyH+5g9PAxa4PqSpM5+taMmNmw\nNReWeE3+FZPPigZVUxxYtMpyh6+2dxDHc6JnJMPcGghd7uL5bLn4jJPrcr48pLga\ncerMScVh4HTRh6LneuLBLyuHIdGeqhmIM8SRojhLh0Dzmb8g16kKSIv5kMlRCPkV\nXu/Ru52Dis3U5tkJb76y\n=AmSP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6c16e32397eb4e545fdabb57ce05b99e21567b9d\nparent 79899a306d01de6217a1dfcc013ae92c808a47a0\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781154118 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781154118 -0400\n\nfeat(code): show connection state in the status bar (#3710)\n\nConnection and queued-message state now stays visible in the bottom\nstatus bar, even after the welcome banner scrolls out of view. Reconnect\npaths distinguish initial startup from mid-session restarts so users can\nsee whether the app is connecting, reconnecting, or holding queued\ninput.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-11T05:01:59Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3e3e8feb0e6e1b77be75a7756fbf32e5c9497c28","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3e3e8feb0e6e1b77be75a7756fbf32e5c9497c28","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3e3e8feb0e6e1b77be75a7756fbf32e5c9497c28/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"79899a306d01de6217a1dfcc013ae92c808a47a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/79899a306d01de6217a1dfcc013ae92c808a47a0","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/79899a306d01de6217a1dfcc013ae92c808a47a0"}]},{"sha":"79899a306d01de6217a1dfcc013ae92c808a47a0","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDc5ODk5YTMwNmQwMWRlNjIxN2ExZGZjYzAxM2FlOTJjODA4YTQ3YTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-11T04:39:58Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T04:39:58Z"},"message":"feat(code): add config command and canonical config manifest (#3763)\n\nThe deepagents-code config surface was spread across ~50\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_*` env vars, CLI flags, and `config.toml` sections with\nno single place that enumerated it or let a user see what was actually\nin effect — and the `[interpreter]` defaults were duplicated between the\n`Settings` dataclass and a bespoke TOML reader. This adds a `config`\ncommand for introspection and makes `config_manifest` the canonical\nsource for every scalar option, so defaults and coercion live in exactly\none place.\n\n## Changes\n- Add a `dcode config` command group in `config_commands.py` — `show`\n(effective value + resolution source per option), `list`, `get <key>`,\nand `path`, all with `--json`. Credentials are reported as set/not-set\nonly; their values are never printed.\n- Introduce `config_manifest.py` as the single source of truth:\n`ConfigOption` entries describe each option's `kind`, typed default, env\nvar, and `config.toml` location, with provider credentials generated\nfrom `PROVIDER_API_KEY_ENV` so a new provider can't miss the surface.\n- Add `resolve_scalar`, one resolution engine shared by the runtime and\nthe CLI (precedence: prefixed env > canonical env > `config.toml` >\ntyped default). An empty env value is treated as unset to match\n`resolve_env_var`, and malformed numeric/list/PTC or wrong-typed TOML\nvalues are logged and fall back rather than raising.\n- Derive the `Settings` interpreter field defaults from manifest\nconstants and resolve the `[interpreter]` section through\n`resolve_interpreter_kwargs`, deleting `_resolve_interpreter_kwargs` and\n`_read_config_toml_interpreter` (~120 lines). Credentials, shell\nallow-list, and LangSmith project keep their dedicated loaders;\n`[models.providers.*]`, `[themes.*]`, and other user-defined tables stay\nas typed loaders the manifest references by section.\n- Wire `config` into the argparse dispatch and the `_HELP_SPECS`\nfast-path table (`show_config_help`), keeping `config_manifest`\nimport-light so a bare `config`/help invocation never pulls\n`model_config` onto the startup path.\n\n## Testing\n- Drift tests assert every `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_*` env var and every\nprovider credential has a manifest entry, and that each option's\n`settings_field` names a real `Settings` attribute — the manifest can't\nsilently drop or mistype an option.\n- Cover the resolver's per-kind coercion, log-and-fallback parity with\nthe deleted reader, the empty-prefixed-env suppression (introspection\nmatching `resolve_env_var`), and `config show` JSON redaction across all\nsecret options. Extend the fast-path import test to prove bare `config`\nloads no heavy modules.","tree":{"sha":"a9111eafc16860a3051c94eb379fb7fcee118682","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a9111eafc16860a3051c94eb379fb7fcee118682"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/79899a306d01de6217a1dfcc013ae92c808a47a0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKjweCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7U8QAF4RVqjggAFNqpSrFIeGwOFo\nL6J9zZPhV4YrKKlZ028t7gJTYLBzbGv76eoLX4LQ0SdlwNsmiOJwCVnGW1TrhRFt\niThSfKAe7V71FQafVAKLCx/hQdGrrG60Hka4warX/FrTNarc0qJFIB7xFCbZiu0/\n7kU3s0U2TpPkOzU9DXTroGF0z2Tm2+2+2caLtkuFJJVnQZLCu0nfGrMqKsETqCpD\ndf6btXtz6KtQ7Tog++im2Kztg9wgW8Q5FzvmOPpg+BFoD6i8t6IQuHBhvY9eaEVk\nxRpKd1jU/Xv7ksxhVZn3KIODMCQuj+7hfbx2ajtgHgVzRH1Yf4KrRyruDQFfrmxE\nxNUTMoI/o85Zbed/oLtL0gCZxdUSSRpqw900Kq9oYb04PD7d58uDijqBRWWLUiBd\nk8RJ0a8xUwB6pXswh5MaqBTaM3+b2TVntQQYdmpLM1G+SBuKBfONGAHWJKSGi918\nIXmN4pUqqDrTFaYQ8dppFXCSaljIItLIifG/TgMHKpwWnH/UkJr/d6fR1IwJLBOt\nVpc3XLmo3ly8BcN25QjKBVcuoyKObfjOM1hIbnXz6E14TCZ9mQjG+jSte6bVP/UW\nC6c7lf7lsbr9m4b1UXOMUCl2nwvFBtc8UlDrAqojcKlINbjta6hyxjULIxBtUk/d\nlU7vxhE7drvMqg/nfWLP\n=nVS+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a9111eafc16860a3051c94eb379fb7fcee118682\nparent 8211e85864f93b0f476a7718f7b0ff9362df6346\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781152798 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781152798 -0400\n\nfeat(code): add config command and canonical config manifest (#3763)\n\nThe deepagents-code config surface was spread across ~50\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_*` env vars, CLI flags, and `config.toml` sections with\nno single place that enumerated it or let a user see what was actually\nin effect — and the `[interpreter]` defaults were duplicated between the\n`Settings` dataclass and a bespoke TOML reader. This adds a `config`\ncommand for introspection and makes `config_manifest` the canonical\nsource for every scalar option, so defaults and coercion live in exactly\none place.\n\n## Changes\n- Add a `dcode config` command group in `config_commands.py` — `show`\n(effective value + resolution source per option), `list`, `get <key>`,\nand `path`, all with `--json`. Credentials are reported as set/not-set\nonly; their values are never printed.\n- Introduce `config_manifest.py` as the single source of truth:\n`ConfigOption` entries describe each option's `kind`, typed default, env\nvar, and `config.toml` location, with provider credentials generated\nfrom `PROVIDER_API_KEY_ENV` so a new provider can't miss the surface.\n- Add `resolve_scalar`, one resolution engine shared by the runtime and\nthe CLI (precedence: prefixed env > canonical env > `config.toml` >\ntyped default). An empty env value is treated as unset to match\n`resolve_env_var`, and malformed numeric/list/PTC or wrong-typed TOML\nvalues are logged and fall back rather than raising.\n- Derive the `Settings` interpreter field defaults from manifest\nconstants and resolve the `[interpreter]` section through\n`resolve_interpreter_kwargs`, deleting `_resolve_interpreter_kwargs` and\n`_read_config_toml_interpreter` (~120 lines). Credentials, shell\nallow-list, and LangSmith project keep their dedicated loaders;\n`[models.providers.*]`, `[themes.*]`, and other user-defined tables stay\nas typed loaders the manifest references by section.\n- Wire `config` into the argparse dispatch and the `_HELP_SPECS`\nfast-path table (`show_config_help`), keeping `config_manifest`\nimport-light so a bare `config`/help invocation never pulls\n`model_config` onto the startup path.\n\n## Testing\n- Drift tests assert every `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_*` env var and every\nprovider credential has a manifest entry, and that each option's\n`settings_field` names a real `Settings` attribute — the manifest can't\nsilently drop or mistype an option.\n- Cover the resolver's per-kind coercion, log-and-fallback parity with\nthe deleted reader, the empty-prefixed-env suppression (introspection\nmatching `resolve_env_var`), and `config show` JSON redaction across all\nsecret options. Extend the fast-path import test to prove bare `config`\nloads no heavy modules.","verified_at":"2026-06-11T04:39:59Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/79899a306d01de6217a1dfcc013ae92c808a47a0","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/79899a306d01de6217a1dfcc013ae92c808a47a0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/79899a306d01de6217a1dfcc013ae92c808a47a0/comments","autho