o longer inherited a\nuser-provided launch environment (e.g. `PYTHONPATH=src dcode`), causing\n`ModuleNotFoundError`. Remove `PYTHONPATH` from the denylist; project\n`.env` injection stays blocked by `config._DOTENV_DENIED_ENV_KEYS`.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"f61a2cb376cb38a7a4ee08a4628f4b5372b5e4b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/f61a2cb376cb38a7a4ee08a4628f4b5372b5e4b4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/4689569f94138987319cd9cbb45ce66a1f496934","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKc7jCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9D8QAK77EEdhfr86c1+hkUAqzbUV\ngLiadipR53XoTycRQde3nqp4rgXUBHnDsvF0vQJkktGkMU9GGTGGk08hhFhsBrdz\nPB+SwFOXepidp7t2Me/ap7NRIvzyQSMOv1ehC8F1c7KKyV7+Zk7+q6PJj9Q1U83l\n03YOIpi/WAfF1Lzu1m9vFJItLhkbGX2sUfUNnBru4xDA52xplXmZgf1wZdmjhcz2\nb2bspHcowaRhRD3v20BnNpJWeBgq1pDxlJAe/mTPWwAPKwS3XfKD97fBu9Jl8/pT\n/PmciY2fgz3mwBoa8wIhqIn6l5rYrblufywjPDf7EZgWyeAfaJ3p6zuo2mT0CXyw\nDmU3sLkR3/dUQcUf9Luq86EI/SLIWUXLKLpmsCqtbHRJocAwyJ0XGpGR61HbAB//\njQa5lEHybfDJGyZdyQ6Q9EkDF8Q0AQ/guBLHANWCq8nU9Fz4y1FFKQuQcrETxnxx\ntgwMSISTIpkS+WUcelaOCEszir152ukoxUpNpDU4Se3vxAY2FlzvjbdzOB7lxkOp\nldBkVbTLHTNrD9pbTvlTzgM9HVN6iZfo3xglVbRGGPtur3VvU+erZFW3H/YD35S6\n3F4wVg4Jsejqn/J6oycVJX/H6INRFCnD6U/d8mOC6ZxLqQClmHuyViQkjaONdrm+\n4++2p0g6yTV+6FdjBoUS\n=uBLF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f61a2cb376cb38a7a4ee08a4628f4b5372b5e4b4\nparent c59a27ef2405b8e04c4351ce7ffa53d8d16d519c\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781124835 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781124835 -0400\n\nfix(code): preserve inherited `PYTHONPATH` for server subprocess (#3833)\n\nRestore inheritance of a launch-time `PYTHONPATH` into agent shell\ncommands.\n\n---\n\n`_SERVER_ENV_DENYLIST` stripped `PYTHONPATH` from the `langgraph dev`\nserver process, so agent `execute` shell commands no longer inherited a\nuser-provided launch environment (e.g. `PYTHONPATH=src dcode`), causing\n`ModuleNotFoundError`. Remove `PYTHONPATH` from the denylist; project\n`.env` injection stays blocked by `config._DOTENV_DENIED_ENV_KEYS`.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-10T20:53:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4689569f94138987319cd9cbb45ce66a1f496934","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4689569f94138987319cd9cbb45ce66a1f496934","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4689569f94138987319cd9cbb45ce66a1f496934/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c59a27ef2405b8e04c4351ce7ffa53d8d16d519c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c59a27ef2405b8e04c4351ce7ffa53d8d16d519c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c59a27ef2405b8e04c4351ce7ffa53d8d16d519c"}]},{"sha":"c59a27ef2405b8e04c4351ce7ffa53d8d16d519c","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGM1OWEyN2VmMjQwNWI4ZTA0YzQzNTFjZTdmZmE1M2Q4ZDE2ZDUxOWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-10T19:42:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-10T19:42:16Z"},"message":"fix(code): resolve interpreter PTC allowlist against the runtime tool registry (#3845)\n\nThe interpreter PTC allowlist (`interpreter_ptc`, set via\n`--interpreter-tools` or `[interpreter].ptc`) lets `js_eval` call a\nsubset of the agent's tools by name. Resolution ran while the agent was\nbeing built and validated the configured names against the tool list\nhanded to `create_cli_agent`. That list does **not** contain the Deep\nAgents built-ins (`read_file`, `glob`, `grep`, `write_file`,\n`edit_file`, `execute`, `write_todos`, `task`) — those are injected a\nstep later by SDK middleware. In server and non-interactive mode the\nhanded-in list is only `fetch_url`/`web_search`/MCP tools, so two things\nbroke:\n\n- Naming a built-in (e.g. `--interpreter-tools read_file,grep,task`)\nfailed validation and **aborted server startup** with `Unknown tool\nnames: [...]` (exit code 3).\n- `interpreter_ptc=\"safe\"` intersected its read-only preset against that\nlist, matched none of its members, and silently resolved to an empty\nallowlist — exposing nothing.\n\n`CodeInterpreterMiddleware` already resolves PTC names against the live\nruntime registry and silently drops names that match nothing, so\nbuild-time validation was both unnecessary and wrong. This change stops\nvalidating names at build time: `\"safe\"` resolves to its preset\ndirectly, explicit names pass through to the middleware, and runtime\ndecides what is exposed. The SDK exposes no importable list of built-in\ntool names, so there is deliberately no hardcoded mirror that could\ndrift.\n\nWhile here, the `\"safe\"` preset can now be combined with explicit names\nin a list — `--interpreter-tools safe,task` or `ptc = [\"safe\", \"task\"]`\n— deduplicated with order preserved. `\"all\"` stays a standalone,\nacknowledgement-gated sentinel (it can expose write/shell tools without\nHITL prompts) and is now rejected early, with a clear message, if placed\ninside a list — at the CLI, `config.toml`, and agent-build layers.\n\n## Notes\n\n- `\"safe\"` now genuinely exposes `read_file`/`glob`/`grep` in server and\nnon-interactive mode (previously empty). The preset stays locked to\nread-only, non-HITL-gated tools, enforced by a test against the live\ninterrupt map.\n- Build-time \"unknown tool name\" errors are gone; a mistyped explicit\nname now silently exposes nothing (logged at debug). Recovering that\nfeedback at the layer that can distinguish a typo from an absent tool —\nplus an \"expose-all\" sentinel so `interpreter_ptc=\"all\"` can include the\nSDK built-ins — is tracked in #3847.\n- `interpreter_ptc=\"all\"` enumeration is unchanged from `main`: still\nscoped to the tools passed to `create_cli_agent`, since the runtime\nbuilt-ins are not enumerable at build time (see #3847).\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"ebb205510a1b4998b24dfed4afd3029c0f1c7725","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/ebb205510a1b4998b24dfed4afd3029c0f1c7725"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/c59a27ef2405b8e04c4351ce7ffa53d8d16d519c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKb4YCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqxIQAHC5/03Vj4Qacx2LJG7u0VEv\nOBzDKIDWBtnHBcRQkrGUxd2o9EsFImMXdacAKb90DsxRSmCE1SGINtIHCz62vHRH\nVH1FZ5QzltfaonEMSH5P21rFa+JsNbmykpt7xamc49s/RBgoc3EAUHp2+ko106Pl\nFPp+zEOQiFfEzG2MxBL/nuYOYlWu7pLq3XTBRUN4rDFhlZF1WIn/5/+vupe87ov9\nRXYu6ALql17Ltp3O6sHwb3walmzVo2iJ60fulztWIrmegprODhcnF/iAmJWsEfEL\nweHFiHFzhuoO+w0Gr6/g03Phmqf/ygXxTyAim/FrkmUWIpm9lHy5sXf/6p6b7eqk\n7vX8R5KzbrcurcYuHFWVWVX9e/b0m2l39+dkBhVK3GNGwpbIKTbRYPdvsS3qofDR\nTAsMrD4SJtVgy/VwIoYx6y5TOrkbBPeipkyVgcRzMIHMRaidTzvPL8NQXo3J7Bpv\nDEmBjVvtN2QHqQldBgCW9YqrtaNTa9YFj9sIutsXNYD48pASfM3rm97a8bzpM/uW\ny/MWCs6c+yW+0UxhTxTEDuMHXlMuuSSUptGi4NIXxz++alVIbHr/iwF2EkTzMBr/\nXBAUSmZTxxl8lCNORjohX3c1LrkPJaY9DU0JK8bU3ztSxI2UGfSgZ0LCWrm9SoT6\nhMbBX1WBrKh/06PhSfx8\n=gm75\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ebb205510a1b4998b24dfed4afd3029c0f1c7725\nparent 99f782cf08336c200d02a24ae4edaa650af67ed2\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781120536 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781120536 -0400\n\nfix(code): resolve interpreter PTC allowlist against the runtime tool registry (#3845)\n\nThe interpreter PTC allowlist (`interpreter_ptc`, set via\n`--interpreter-tools` or `[interpreter].ptc`) lets `js_eval` call a\nsubset of the agent's tools by name. Resolution ran while the agent was\nbeing built and validated the configured names against the tool list\nhanded to `create_cli_agent`. That list does **not** contain the Deep\nAgents built-ins (`read_file`, `glob`, `grep`, `write_file`,\n`edit_file`, `execute`, `write_todos`, `task`) — those are injected a\nstep later by SDK middleware. In server and non-interactive mode the\nhanded-in list is only `fetch_url`/`web_search`/MCP tools, so two things\nbroke:\n\n- Naming a built-in (e.g. `--interpreter-tools read_file,grep,task`)\nfailed validation and **aborted server startup** with `Unknown tool\nnames: [...]` (exit code 3).\n- `interpreter_ptc=\"safe\"` intersected its read-only preset against that\nlist, matched none of its members, and silently resolved to an empty\nallowlist — exposing nothing.\n\n`CodeInterpreterMiddleware` already resolves PTC names against the live\nruntime registry and silently drops names that match nothing, so\nbuild-time validation was both unnecessary and wrong. This change stops\nvalidating names at build time: `\"safe\"` resolves to its preset\ndirectly, explicit names pass through to the middleware, and runtime\ndecides what is exposed. The SDK exposes no importable list of built-in\ntool names, so there is deliberately no hardcoded mirror that could\ndrift.\n\nWhile here, the `\"safe\"` preset can now be combined with explicit names\nin a list — `--interpreter-tools safe,task` or `ptc = [\"safe\", \"task\"]`\n— deduplicated with order preserved. `\"all\"` stays a standalone,\nacknowledgement-gated sentinel (it can expose write/shell tools without\nHITL prompts) and is now rejected early, with a clear message, if placed\ninside a list — at the CLI, `config.toml`, and agent-build layers.\n\n## Notes\n\n- `\"safe\"` now genuinely exposes `read_file`/`glob`/`grep` in server and\nnon-interactive mode (previously empty). The preset stays locked to\nread-only, non-HITL-gated tools, enforced by a test against the live\ninterrupt map.\n- Build-time \"unknown tool name\" errors are gone; a mistyped explicit\nname now silently exposes nothing (logged at debug). Recovering that\nfeedback at the layer that can distinguish a typo from an absent tool —\nplus an \"expose-all\" sentinel so `interpreter_ptc=\"all\"` can include the\nSDK built-ins — is tracked in #3847.\n- `interpreter_ptc=\"all\"` enumeration is unchanged from `main`: still\nscoped to the tools passed to `create_cli_agent`, since the runtime\nbuilt-ins are not enumerable at build time (see #3847).\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-10T19:42:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c59a27ef2405b8e04c4351ce7ffa53d8d16d519c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c59a27ef2405b8e04c4351ce7ffa53d8d16d519c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c59a27ef2405b8e04c4351ce7ffa53d8d16d519c/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"99f782cf08336c200d02a24ae4edaa650af67ed2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/99f782cf08336c200d02a24ae4edaa650af67ed2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/99f782cf08336c200d02a24ae4edaa650af67ed2"}]},{"sha":"99f782cf08336c200d02a24ae4edaa650af67ed2","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDk5Zjc4MmNmMDgzMzZjMjAwZDAyYTI0YWU0ZWRhYTY1MGFmNjdlZDI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-10T18:04:35Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-10T18:04:35Z"},"message":"feat(code): copy focused input selection on `Ctrl+C` (#3841)\n\n`Ctrl+C` now copies the selected text in a focused input instead of\nquitting when there is an active selection.\n\n---\n\ndcode's global priority `ctrl+c` binding (`quit_or_interrupt`) shadowed\nTextual's built-in copy binding on focused inputs, so selected text in\nthe chat input could never be copied with `Ctrl+C`. This adds a\nselection check at the top of `action_quit_or_interrupt`: when the\nfocused widget is a `TextArea`/`ChatTextArea` or `Input` with a\nnon-empty selection, the selection is copied via the existing\n`copy_text_to_clipboard` helper and quit/interrupt is skipped. With no\nselection, all existing behavior is preserved, so `Ctrl+C` can still\nquit while an input is focused.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"f6b4638284b4bcaaebe57ff8bd6a39e4592981a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/f6b4638284b4bcaaebe57ff8bd6a39e4592981a7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/99f782cf08336c200d02a24ae4edaa650af67ed2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKaczCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgngQAFPhHWGeaP3u+VImNikeEA7U\nTPbCZHodwwEy8anv+QQ5Bl2bUS81PKg/ORT3pSl3VpA0XNLLOGOjFjm4JbWVt0Z/\nd9bAB1qFFOFhrK8hRTs47sJspKV83KvK9nV/jZs1Gh33yWBHn3Ea2ssnR3irrgeD\nz+lUnEBNdiTO11WQb30GzCjkPJwFiVq6lVSG6jcS4cOnW0+JrenMWzxjQr2RNuej\nyGbhg/jJJVXb+7qgMqQMlHL5gysS6irSRX4k6AmXGIMgHTEV48azSmA3e06ad1RY\nR15+IHvQv9rmRbpnOXXb3lfWGhoQserVrB2Lt2piQUNFQYgRtKkzikDG5ymfjxwW\n5lHUCabUowbz36L/BpSBDXAVVimofPb2/UyTsp2wa5wijQVyFDcNYD6I701o7bwR\nhzXJO4YvVqXHoz0TAty12Ybv+FLf/Z2KZa5piqCEhnTL9KT9r6e/0gHMpvRItLcE\n1ac/aNRrdYm9xwuIGbls+NSUXzc6vkmAKhZkzLlvbl1VuOxjkhaZ/xJge4WKYmxn\nLWbJz6LNrUUgqgY/T26J9mrIffzjRwr+HqIcaWqTp0tLK/W05vW6tnrBO/Xboz/z\n5B+CzE/hEN5ET+w9pJoPyb5cyl5OJ6kzK+57HK2w227YWvzWga0oBb2EiSWqUz2X\n0hvySgALTAM0Z6TRAb54\n=svn1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f6b4638284b4bcaaebe57ff8bd6a39e4592981a7\nparent 3d75026e2f241648fae78d9e1de2cbb4985f58ff\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781114675 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781114675 -0400\n\nfeat(code): copy focused input selection on `Ctrl+C` (#3841)\n\n`Ctrl+C` now copies the selected text in a focused input instead of\nquitting when there is an active selection.\n\n---\n\ndcode's global priority `ctrl+c` binding (`quit_or_interrupt`) shadowed\nTextual's built-in copy binding on focused inputs, so selected text in\nthe chat input could never be copied with `Ctrl+C`. This adds a\nselection check at the top of `action_quit_or_interrupt`: when the\nfocused widget is a `TextArea`/`ChatTextArea` or `Input` with a\nnon-empty selection, the selection is copied via the existing\n`copy_text_to_clipboard` helper and quit/interrupt is skipped. With no\nselection, all existing behavior is preserved, so `Ctrl+C` can still\nquit while an input is focused.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-10T18:04:36Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/99f782cf08336c200d02a24ae4edaa650af67ed2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/99f782cf08336c200d02a24ae4edaa650af67ed2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/99f782cf08336c200d02a24ae4edaa650af67ed2/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3d75026e2f241648fae78d9e1de2cbb4985f58ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3d75026e2f241648fae78d9e1de2cbb4985f58ff","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3d75026e2f241648fae78d9e1de2cbb4985f58ff"}]},{"sha":"3d75026e2f241648fae78d9e1de2cbb4985f58ff","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDNkNzUwMjZlMmYyNDE2NDhmYWU3OGQ5ZTFkZTJjYmI0OTg1ZjU4ZmY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-10T17:10:01Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-10T17:10:01Z"},"message":"feat(code): confirm modal for `/install --package` (#3840)\n\nIn the TUI, `/install <pkg> --package` previously refused to install\nunless the user re-ran with `--force`. That was inconsistent with the\nCLI, which prompts interactively. This makes the TUI prompt too: it\nopens a non-blocking Textual confirmation modal\n(`InstallPackageConfirmScreen`) explaining that installing an arbitrary\npackage runs third-party code.\n\nConfirming runs the same install path `--force` used; cancelling shows a\n\"Cancelled install\" message and never calls `perform_install_package`.\n`--force` (and a new undocumented `--yes` alias) still bypass the\nprompt. Invalid package names and editable installs are still rejected\nbefore any confirmation. The CLI `--install <pkg> --package` flow and\nits `--yes` behavior are unchanged.\n\nThe new modal reuses the existing confirm-screen pattern (mirrors\n`MCPReconnectForceConfirmScreen`/`RestartPromptScreen`), and the wait is\nbounded by a watchdog so a stuck modal can't wedge command handling.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"0b996a060a1d0b146d3e5dac6faebb6fda6f43a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/0b996a060a1d0b146d3e5dac6faebb6fda6f43a0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/3d75026e2f241648fae78d9e1de2cbb4985f58ff","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKZppCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAorwQAAPAptIqRNsQuj6jUgUNnG3Z\nfysgQiRcFyKoHrXj+mQQwQEHVjjeeCf9T8KnY2jqbL2+S8LV/h3kNjfJbG+5iy0D\nUbfk/a0pa7zdxYDGHXorRT4h+JnViaBxlTS8PlVn3XTYbpz9kcFzlPxytaAM4uP6\nXufrM4/XI3fL2Qxm47a1YvIuNaZ8pf00NzokKkm8OD3GGRYh67u1xMZc0NKZfUiu\nKM1NLFzCJZyfM65dHlelYOsV1DIIgylquUjDQ5jbGBWoR/03QG1iOZJV1mxfngtY\npn+TWgX1g2EUk0HdF/3YQbET4OjQlWUdRfpNSbybaCjjfWu5PHo9+/hJV6sLgnv3\nNYMInPHd2b7cA0K9ZcQUMWrXoHbDmp6tLQ9RDxAjZkMn+axIzrLrslMKqaZ80JfH\nXHFplE/8aH7f/4iBW/HB7yGJSenmjMeWral9FF4Gxc+CMXAApHIwTZGVkq02ium8\nqZOFn8C+P8nAmcaUlrCxrB2GgVlN09KVjbnjoQQ+gg2DUybH5mbWweSPJK/uDVkU\nKQrAbLKfqM0WO7H1xPNjGjLCZYS4tarmUXopwkDMUQiPesdIirLKWvwuA8pimvLi\nzB701WDiuI42y0iImLZ2Xo8K/neQI9xnEeWSmu9hKJaLYYXFyOkW0b7SxwI8Y0HQ\nU0SZUbTqQP794ivp81ff\n=ou9D\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0b996a060a1d0b146d3e5dac6faebb6fda6f43a0\nparent 676abecf892ff537fcb1425ba5929cace3c5d503\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781111401 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781111401 -0400\n\nfeat(code): confirm modal for `/install --package` (#3840)\n\nIn the TUI, `/install <pkg> --package` previously refused to install\nunless the user re-ran with `--force`. That was inconsistent with the\nCLI, which prompts interactively. This makes the TUI prompt too: it\nopens a non-blocking Textual confirmation modal\n(`InstallPackageConfirmScreen`) explaining that installing an arbitrary\npackage runs third-party code.\n\nConfirming runs the same install path `--force` used; cancelling shows a\n\"Cancelled install\" message and never calls `perform_install_package`.\n`--force` (and a new undocumented `--yes` alias) still bypass the\nprompt. Invalid package names and editable installs are still rejected\nbefore any confirmation. The CLI `--install <pkg> --package` flow and\nits `--yes` behavior are unchanged.\n\nThe new modal reuses the existing confirm-screen pattern (mirrors\n`MCPReconnectForceConfirmScreen`/`RestartPromptScreen`), and the wait is\nbounded by a watchdog so a stuck modal can't wedge command handling.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-10T17:10:02Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3d75026e2f241648fae78d9e1de2cbb4985f58ff","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3d75026e2f241648fae78d9e1de2cbb4985f58ff","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3d75026e2f241648fae78d9e1de2cbb4985f58ff/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"676abecf892ff537fcb1425ba5929cace3c5d503","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/676abecf892ff537fcb1425ba5929cace3c5d503","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/676abecf892ff537fcb1425ba5929cace3c5d503"}]},{"sha":"676abecf892ff537fcb1425ba5929cace3c5d503","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDY3NmFiZWNmODkyZmY1MzdmY2IxNDI1YmE1OTI5Y2FjZTNjNWQ1MDM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-10T04:46:50Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-10T04:46:50Z"},"message":"feat(code): surface LangSmith tracing projects in `LocalContextMiddleware` (#3836)\n\nThe coding agent now sees the active LangSmith tracing project name(s)\nin its context when tracing is enabled.\n\n---\n\n`LocalContextMiddleware` already injects environment context (git,\nruntimes, MCP servers) into the system prompt, but it said nothing about\nLangSmith tracing. `deepagents-code` deliberately routes its *own*\ntraces to a dedicated project (`get_langsmith_project_name()`) while\npreserving the user's original `LANGSMITH_PROJECT` for shell commands it\nruns — so the agent had no way to know where to look for its traces.\n\nThis adds a `**LangSmith Tracing**` section listing both project *names*\n(no network/URL lookup) so the agent can fetch the relevant runs via the\nLangSmith MCP server or CLI. The section is omitted entirely when\ntracing is disabled, and the second line collapses when the two projects\nare identical.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"13004f63f1becb61ee44a12daf744f078f4835b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/13004f63f1becb61ee44a12daf744f078f4835b3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/676abecf892ff537fcb1425ba5929cace3c5d503","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKOw6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANIQQABrZobEvkRuVk89nC1EoA3z6\nKBqz02cu3ucLQ0wnr+4zeRq7SXvLPkg2+nayWzDEC3ESWIY5ccpmgHSdKIYH5CT8\nN9fD1XU+Led6iA3QW1iv9C6V/ET6tbLYfPrUOdtfaQ4QI0/zYYLxo94GfGkgIz3L\nLloMO0EidceDIMooA7ht/AxklTEsGwJsWQmkxaaps/vH0OpMpoa3czcvz9A+7OUb\nW8jUOIJ36xgmJ+ynA5VptzVdZeqL7wgnrS5n62kHxm72FYEYAFO98h5bUhUVEnjB\n4M7d66pYPqhsl9e6frLlJ7aprGSixlbY89rwBDko570b5Tz1ZXZVmPHM33RSwmix\nf6eZuLHSk85Se5i/GWkgjEcge2hk2QU5uVxUupAfTiJMRIHHk5z2Az1rc/PqoDEy\nbC49A/yLeAaofXxHpLhJlVvZpu29NnjpspgdQ6F1XWhjWYdo7ZG6RFxDdgm2Z43i\nyMW8HXW/xgiCef517k7keDXCj9h7Mv19KWlcD7UxBG7v6IDZCOr/GqR01Y560IZ9\n6jG0/hAl+l+TOMIsjY2mzwwyc+EB5tG310uahvWH/Ckq5SE9gfRimKyPGyV2kSf5\nlxdTtozKGNsHDbY1fq5rDaEBtTJ9gFJsmJuV/ItChV66pcNMj1jyk0+4YFZKSVFv\nvT5HHyga8IKROFdy0iO8\n=lzYU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 13004f63f1becb61ee44a12daf744f078f4835b3\nparent 6a3779286101b5523dddca84ad392ee1e6515175\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781066810 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781066810 -0400\n\nfeat(code): surface LangSmith tracing projects in `LocalContextMiddleware` (#3836)\n\nThe coding agent now sees the active LangSmith tracing project name(s)\nin its context when tracing is enabled.\n\n---\n\n`LocalContextMiddleware` already injects environment context (git,\nruntimes, MCP servers) into the system prompt, but it said nothing about\nLangSmith tracing. `deepagents-code` deliberately routes its *own*\ntraces to a dedicated project (`get_langsmith_project_name()`) while\npreserving the user's original `LANGSMITH_PROJECT` for shell commands it\nruns — so the agent had no way to know where to look for its traces.\n\nThis adds a `**LangSmith Tracing**` section listing both project *names*\n(no network/URL lookup) so the agent can fetch the relevant runs via the\nLangSmith MCP server or CLI. The section is omitted entirely when\ntracing is disabled, and the second line collapses when the two projects\nare identical.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-10T04:46:50Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/676abecf892ff537fcb1425ba5929cace3c5d503","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/676abecf892ff537fcb1425ba5929cace3c5d503","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/676abecf892ff537fcb1425ba5929cace3c5d503/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6a3779286101b5523dddca84ad392ee1e6515175","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6a3779286101b5523dddca84ad392ee1e6515175","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/6a3779286101b5523dddca84ad392ee1e6515175"}]},{"sha":"6a3779286101b5523dddca84ad392ee1e6515175","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDZhMzc3OTI4NjEwMWI1NTIzZGRkY2E4NGFkMzkyZWUxZTY1MTUxNzU","commit":{"author":{"name":"github-actions[bot]","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-10T03:53:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-10T03:53:16Z"},"message":"release(deepagents-code): 0.1.12 (#3805)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Everything below this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.12](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.11...deepagents-code==0.1.12)\n(2026-06-10)\n\n### Features\n\n* Add `get_current_thread_id` tool\n([#3820](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3820))\n([18ce094](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/18ce094b7036796c7e23ce1338f4da56dc2ef126))\n* Guard managed onboarding-name memory block from edits\n([#3822](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3822))\n([dc0a51f](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/dc0a51fc81d01b62dc8043148a9fd87099fc9123))\n* Offer restart after restart-capable install\n([#3821](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3821))\n([e356efe](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e356efeff1c8bfb894119cebbb7d3c0853d327a2))\n* Persist `/threads` directory-scope preference\n([#3824](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3824))\n([51a29f4](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/51a29f4a0c28c122acae296a0df03bee20474455))\n* Surface gateway key mismatch on `PermissionDeniedError`\n([#3813](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3813))\n([5bd1ef8](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5bd1ef8cb29db781ccbb37755db44ce0ab1d7bd2))\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n* Surface cached MCP errors as failed tool messages\n([#3829](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3829))\n([d83b428](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d83b428f7f97bc40b9219c02846c2d8b4ccac434))\n* Handle MCP tool errors locally\n([#3830](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3830))\n([97a7052](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/97a7052b3eef7ec80bc90a4c3b606deeaf13cb9b))\n* Make non-incognito `!` shell output visible to the model\n([#3825](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3825))\n([2407bca](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2407bca66bac5d199a923a0e58872c813eb006bc))\n* Expose `/restart` slash command\n([#3809](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3809))\n([64505b8](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/64505b848868b80213b6da87113cd63890c3d520))\n* Agent retries `gh search` with invalid `mergedAt` field\n([#3802](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3802))\n([0b683a9](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0b683a9435b95bce79d10451868eae54c6a3e88c))\n* Clarify `/restart` message during server startup\n([#3823](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3823))\n([49ded9e](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/49ded9ef448dcd263bee07ac15f4904dd342bfa2))\n* Cursor at end when popping queued message to input\n([#3832](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3832))\n([aa522c9](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/aa522c94fffb93dc578addb39b4879f779ac5899))\n* Coalesce streamed markdown writes to keep input responsive\n([#3819](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3819))\n([b45eeeb](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b45eeebaf7e6ae6e07b8f9ca521525c66fe14f63))\n* Don't show `\"No threads found\"` while threads load\n([#3815](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3815))\n([68e6426](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/68e64263f590b3244b689664715f354fb3a389cd))\n* Ignore stale cwd warmers in file autocomplete cache\n([#3835](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3835))\n([9c8c2b2](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9c8c2b24853b7b3a7610cbcfc368a6464c0711e0))\n* Offer cwd switch on resume\n([#3810](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3810))\n([d417f53](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d417f530aafa8c77523487393dc3039cc822dc09))\n* Recover from tool errors instead of aborting run\n([#3804](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3804))\n([45691c5](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/45691c556105e171c7210c7c10388dc73202a025))\n* Show `/restart` feedback\n([#3808](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3808))\n([c40bef9](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c40bef9b2aaace3909593503b28e8b548bc20014))\n* Standardize search previews and restart status\n([#3806](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3806))\n([71a6d50](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/71a6d508b21b275c0c7c6bd2e0752adfba496ea9))\n* Suppress stale update notices\n([#3801](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3801))\n([db25241](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/db252411d8ca945aca86429acb644540ec970bdb))\n* Unblock `/remember` in server mode\n([#3812](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3812))\n([12e00e1](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/12e00e1a78e2d6be106147a0aa95a518be66849f))\n* Unblock TUI input during `/restart`\n([#3826](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3826))\n([366cd81](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/366cd81269e2d3891a477848b774cf51af0cefc0))\n\n---\n\n_Everything above this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"7877972428a6349362d946d2e4bd7838491bc7d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/7877972428a6349362d946d2e4bd7838491bc7d0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/6a3779286101b5523dddca84ad392ee1e6515175","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKN+sCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyWAQADij0MuYtB4SleIcDnBrj7y9\nK5NGonoggwJfBP4g1EgcXgXLspPQK5bTOc9bjjT7c7LZpOHIusjTPKkGONcSsBYx\n9zYZAPg/LN7apmAwhbPnKXG2iHF8ck/LYnxlfnU4YiiVapINS1VECzFzkhG5x9+I\n1SgdYkeF7b9M6wWDdIOtf6WJrrNxn1yOqeVixVEhcKt+qIoYnJWhvvePghWIzYH2\nKhLVQY16yfNJRL4hRx8amfhMjTbVcRAjsrgIi2A9QaWxRlo5foDlYKdEZZDBPPpu\nPvMaqz/LwUiCNvvFMuT42LWJq7lHuNaVA5ca22RFOHBzJblXIWlFMDS3Z/Uuk9GV\nuTIkCi3xlI9tuEnDfllvOiST0vOlPZJC/nJ8aW6nyyht48BsM4FiufP3R/1J3MbE\n+4aq6U4XRW14jNe2WXubYhtUGfAns1uAfutCz3FG78aLBo4abURhKycRfvtaL9tK\nl7uRg1SnGIijwE1KtjZZJQGorNBVtPDT/37k5oYHtTa19A1hhB7Rx2Bi0FhCNt28\nfyHmfM624JLgc+QAAj4Mmoxmzf7FkvERknj/VZLRiAuskJdFklzBzYU/3ZQATApQ\nvbihMTvkcaz4XOMt6njCRACiXE0Gli7694n8rWcIjhwN4QZ7rxHjqFxFJ0OCYEUt\nkK50p5Kva3s8nEvnr1mo\n=pTrY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7877972428a6349362d946d2e4bd7838491bc7d0\nparent 9c8c2b24853b7b3a7610cbcfc368a6464c0711e0\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1781063596 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781063596 -0400\n\nrelease(deepagents-code): 0.1.12 (#3805)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Everything below this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.12](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.11...deepagents-code==0.1.12)\n(2026-06-10)\n\n### Features\n\n* Add `get_current_thread_id` tool\n([#3820](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3820))\n([18ce094](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/18ce094b7036796c7e23ce1338f4da56dc2ef126))\n* Guard managed onboarding-name memory block from edits\n([#3822](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3822))\n([dc0a51f](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/dc0a51fc81d01b62dc8043148a9fd87099fc9123))\n* Offer restart after restart-capable install\n([#3821](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3821))\n([e356efe](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e356efeff1c8bfb894119cebbb7d3c0853d327a2))\n* Persist `/threads` directory-scope preference\n([#3824](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3824))\n([51a29f4](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/51a29f4a0c28c122acae296a0df03bee20474455))\n* Surface gateway key mismatch on `PermissionDeniedError`\n([#3813](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3813))\n([5bd1ef8](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5bd1ef8cb29db781ccbb37755db44ce0ab1d7bd2))\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n* Surface cached MCP errors as failed tool messages\n([#3829](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3829))\n([d83b428](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d83b428f7f97bc40b9219c02846c2d8b4ccac434))\n* Handle MCP tool errors locally\n([#3830](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3830))\n([97a7052](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/97a7052b3eef7ec80bc90a4c3b606deeaf13cb9b))\n* Make non-incognito `!` shell output visible to the model\n([#3825](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3825))\n([2407bca](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2407bca66bac5d199a923a0e58872c813eb006bc))\n* Expose `/restart` slash command\n([#3809](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3809))\n([64505b8](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/64505b848868b80213b6da87113cd63890c3d520))\n* Agent retries `gh search` with invalid `mergedAt` field\n([#3802](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3802))\n([0b683a9](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0b683a9435b95bce79d10451868eae54c6a3e88c))\n* Clarify `/restart` message during server startup\n([#3823](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3823))\n([49ded9e](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/49ded9ef448dcd263bee07ac15f4904dd342bfa2))\n* Cursor at end when popping queued message to input\n([#3832](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3832))\n([aa522c9](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/aa522c94fffb93dc578addb39b4879f779ac5899))\n* Coalesce streamed markdown writes to keep input responsive\n([#3819](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3819))\n([b45eeeb](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b45eeebaf7e6ae6e07b8f9ca521525c66fe14f63))\n* Don't show `\"No threads found\"` while threads load\n([#3815](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3815))\n([68e6426](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/68e64263f590b3244b689664715f354fb3a389cd))\n* Ignore stale cwd warmers in file autocomplete cache\n([#3835](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3835))\n([9c8c2b2](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9c8c2b24853b7b3a7610cbcfc368a6464c0711e0))\n* Offer cwd switch on resume\n([#3810](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3810))\n([d417f53](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d417f530aafa8c77523487393dc3039cc822dc09))\n* Recover from tool errors instead of aborting run\n([#3804](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3804))\n([45691c5](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/45691c556105e171c7210c7c10388dc73202a025))\n* Show `/restart` feedback\n([#3808](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3808))\n([c40bef9](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c40bef9b2aaace3909593503b28e8b548bc20014))\n* Standardize search previews and restart status\n([#3806](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3806))\n([71a6d50](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/71a6d508b21b275c0c7c6bd2e0752adfba496ea9))\n* Suppress stale update notices\n([#3801](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3801))\n([db25241](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/db252411d8ca945aca86429acb644540ec970bdb))\n* Unblock `/remember` in server mode\n([#3812](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3812))\n([12e00e1](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/12e00e1a78e2d6be106147a0aa95a518be66849f))\n* Unblock TUI input during `/restart`\n([#3826](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3826))\n([366cd81](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/366cd81269e2d3891a477848b774cf51af0cefc0))\n\n---\n\n_Everything above this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-10T03:53:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6a3779286101b5523dddca84ad392ee1e6515175","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/6a3779286101b5523dddca84ad392ee1e6515175","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6a3779286101b5523dddca84ad392ee1e6515175/comments","author":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9c8c2b24853b7b3a7610cbcfc368a6464c0711e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9c8c2b24853b7b3a7610cbcfc368a6464c0711e0","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9c8c2b24853b7b3a7610cbcfc368a6464c0711e0"}]},{"sha":"9c8c2b24853b7b3a7610cbcfc368a6464c0711e0","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDljOGMyYjI0ODUzYjdiM2E3NjEwY2JjZmMzNjhhNjQ2NGMwNzExZTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-10T03:47:27Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-10T03:47:27Z"},"message":"fix(code): ignore stale cwd warmers in file autocomplete cache (#3835)\n\n`FuzzyFileController.warm_cache` is scheduled non-exclusively, so two\nquick cwd switches can run concurrently. Because the warmer awaited\n`find_project_root` and `_get_project_files` against the mutable `_cwd`,\nan older warmer finishing after a newer cwd switch could overwrite\n`_project_root`, `_project_root_pending`, or `_file_cache` with stale\ndata — leaving `@file` autocomplete rooted at the previous project until\nthe next cwd change or cache refresh.\n\nThe fix snapshots `cwd` before each await and re-checks `cwd ==\nself._cwd` before mutating controller state. A superseded warmer now\ndrops its results instead of clobbering the newer cwd's root/cache. The\nprovisional-root behavior in `set_cwd` is unchanged, and the single-cwd\npath is unaffected.\n\nNew unit tests force the race by making the older warmer's project-root\nlookup and file-cache warm complete last; both fail before the fix and\npass after.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"cbcb8573c3e4069e01080a45519f1d60f28f1e8b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/cbcb8573c3e4069e01080a45519f1d60f28f1e8b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/9c8c2b24853b7b3a7610cbcfc368a6464c0711e0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKN5PCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlTMQADD0QkG+ksexVyM6e3AzfwvT\nd/LgGszLGJ6bubuJbBsGqayB30d2JBZHWdoJdhabjxkxdZYBVooR3zXt0kqgU938\ni8eUsOXoOdu2bbfEZwa7eIaOGxjg/0kNB774gFhKaeDD320dNTJyAXs/gQvQFkuj\nK0MN3zl5hM6g17HXQc2bQMByB+ddtwG1VU7ArfVXPRgX/xamz1nvBzKWasoH2467\nwG9kE06CIa67ad8nTAxS4IlIygO7z/08U4U4iAcFnuG0ms1/fAAR7zcwmUoCO/j9\nqRKZvjDcS5PQWK+5PhjE8kUE2cxRp81uYZ+V3c5R+jqQva5GBecnPQn4X0+hk2sm\na4lBidjgVDbgiX65ywhTz7GCnxwdhd2oqL1RpOhLtFMNns+lU90eV6amcXbor1Of\naESx2lhgdUHV45t9BzInu1r0EPqwXQMgrsjlb/M0w5zUrwN2VSAQ3GsilVoJXURQ\nSYqnngSX1nGXJpyLm6lwIlU97cjot1qRVFiR3ouxEKULYhsXudRb9nNu0ArPbT+c\np5FOiL1dPURCftPu/FD/zIjUUjWBOHyJP/PVyldwuxJMLaRa3dBKh+J04smtjpEJ\nYiHw3hBoFeq/ETFsE6XtNkHBaXWRuBf2OFE1zm2zDPP+Rup8gor+Kypuairh8Vbh\nP219mpetCOa6+U/oKFv5\n=SMnw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree cbcb8573c3e4069e01080a45519f1d60f28f1e8b\nparent aa522c94fffb93dc578addb39b4879f779ac5899\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781063247 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781063247 -0400\n\nfix(code): ignore stale cwd warmers in file autocomplete cache (#3835)\n\n`FuzzyFileController.warm_cache` is scheduled non-exclusively, so two\nquick cwd switches can run concurrently. Because the warmer awaited\n`find_project_root` and `_get_project_files` against the mutable `_cwd`,\nan older warmer finishing after a newer cwd switch could overwrite\n`_project_root`, `_project_root_pending`, or `_file_cache` with stale\ndata — leaving `@file` autocomplete rooted at the previous project until\nthe next cwd change or cache refresh.\n\nThe fix snapshots `cwd` before each await and re-checks `cwd ==\nself._cwd` before mutating controller state. A superseded warmer now\ndrops its results instead of clobbering the newer cwd's root/cache. The\nprovisional-root behavior in `set_cwd` is unchanged, and the single-cwd\npath is unaffected.\n\nNew unit tests force the race by making the older warmer's project-root\nlookup and file-cache warm complete last; both fail before the fix and\npass after.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-10T03:47:27Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9c8c2b24853b7b3a7610cbcfc368a6464c0711e0","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9c8c2b24853b7b3a7610cbcfc368a6464c0711e0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9c8c2b24853b7b3a7610cbcfc368a6464c0711e0/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"aa522c94fffb93dc578addb39b4879f779ac5899","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/aa522c94fffb93dc578addb39b4879f779ac5899","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/aa522c94fffb93dc578addb39b4879f779ac5899"}]},{"sha":"aa522c94fffb93dc578addb39b4879f779ac5899","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGFhNTIyYzk0ZmZmYjkzZGM1NzhhZGRiMzliNDg3OWY3NzlhYzU4OTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-10T03:34:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-10T03:34:16Z"},"message":"fix(code): cursor at end when popping queued message to input (#3832)\n\n## Description\nPopping a queued message back to the chat input (ESC) restored the text\nvia the plain `value` setter, which reset the cursor to index 0. This\nadds a `set_value_at_end` helper and uses it in\n`_pop_last_queued_message`, so the cursor lands at the end — consistent\nwith readline and the widget's own history-recall path.\n\n## Release Note\nFix chat input cursor jumping to the start when a queued message is\npopped back to the input; it now lands at the end of the text.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [ ] Queue a `!!` command while the agent is busy, press ESC, and\nconfirm the cursor sits at the end of the restored text.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"21891834ca2be5b8dc5f54c960d82666750cabfe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/21891834ca2be5b8dc5f54c960d82666750cabfe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/aa522c94fffb93dc578addb39b4879f779ac5899","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKNs4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0kAQAIQJZkAsJyeDWLX6kZKj+LbA\nPUfYP4GzCcXWnN6dsrYUygTunOwijDccI87AN3h8UxbLoOBZCkTcfSR9p5nInGSE\nfXJuABLBXabn6Z6d3z0UdZDCS8QP8ob4EszBlprh5X8+sK8u1uDtMv7rkVKdrr2j\nxMKh5TiO/KreT93ohWTn8WnpaKa8R7UC9MINcFcI8Zq2R05BtzR/xJmYxVf6cDOY\nkqNST3iLR1YIwRxD0C2zjZ4F26WkQRVRKGACsJ5uS8UlyAjDWkvQ26GJ/PhmODb8\nFNQNhm9CcI0wFbh+stCy12iYclNFVqmUki0E/Cs0vcviiWEXs+I6T5bjr6h9iWx4\nrrKoV1r8e0e/ADVNNRcC00V1qLLiYmj9/tVI5Bt4TnOrk8eIsPSSzbIm4fBOFqLA\nuJQcbWDhwqC8hEm3o5Vg5QB+P8LKSNiLV3RVRu8WzoYdqgROj8Lbsr4GOPqFbg0u\nuTKjw4Hw+g2Pgeu0jzujG4s47PWb2w3mGOYeq8ZP/DUzHWA0duFpN/CjkYdQuxyT\nhd/2KkCRkJ3c+w/ny6OhZPRUGJBpjFV71rIIvBBsDFl1gEC4+L6AYu4Z/YZZn9/E\njQiNxYXtY5KZIug09+83tVbMZtHhHpmLY/pK0M9PNsb9dUCW43ZM/nDa0oVMDDGO\nbM+dsfNCt2imizxgz6rK\n=Ehi1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 21891834ca2be5b8dc5f54c960d82666750cabfe\nparent 619e55f49f1837e8e1760eb0ff7a84bb2c833551\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781062456 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781062456 -0400\n\nfix(code): cursor at end when popping queued message to input (#3832)\n\n## Description\nPopping a queued message back to the chat input (ESC) restored the text\nvia the plain `value` setter, which reset the cursor to index 0. This\nadds a `set_value_at_end` helper and uses it in\n`_pop_last_queued_message`, so the cursor lands at the end — consistent\nwith readline and the widget's own history-recall path.\n\n## Release Note\nFix chat input cursor jumping to the start when a queued message is\npopped back to the input; it now lands at the end of the text.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [ ] Queue a `!!` command while the agent is busy, press ESC, and\nconfirm the cursor sits at the end of the restored text.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-10T03:34:16Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/aa522c94fffb93dc578addb39b4879f779ac5899","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/aa522c94fffb93dc578addb39b4879f779ac5899","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/aa522c94fffb93dc578addb39b4879f779ac5899/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"619e55f49f1837e8e1760eb0ff7a84bb2c833551","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/619e55f49f1837e8e1760eb0ff7a84bb2c833551","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/619e55f49f1837e8e1760eb0ff7a84bb2c833551"}]},{"sha":"619e55f49f1837e8e1760eb0ff7a84bb2c833551","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDYxOWU1NWY0OWYxODM3ZThlMTc2MGViMGZmN2E4NGJiMmM4MzM1NTE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-10T03:27:59Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-10T03:27:59Z"},"message":"chore(ci): validate Talon when `libs/talon/uv.lock` is directly changed (#3834)\n\n`_touches_talon()` excluded `libs/talon/uv.lock`, so a PR changing only\nthat lockfile skipped Talon's `uv lock --check`, allowing a\nstale/malformed lockfile to pass pre-commit. Now any `libs/talon` path\n(including `uv.lock`) counts as touching Talon, while unrelated changes\nstill skip Talon to preserve the optimization.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"a5872897a5fb23ea9b31c25dc8f7343981d17753","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a5872897a5fb23ea9b31c25dc8f7343981d17753"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/619e55f49f1837e8e1760eb0ff7a84bb2c833551","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKNm/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANCsQAF5XsK2Dwx8G6F/srrkMPEkX\nmMwibGdChZvDjdG+lrINSago0KU3cBr9S6FXGNSDmiiI0zW0ViS9wuijDV+/ZzW9\nKML1z2PE1qzmIn1+ub82c/+kJgyoGEXc4YUqWjTL83qaL8LPEfzYqlqAeQqoZPt+\nYRqzgETvGk5K3SPa+6wDzMtpzVIk9fiPbrTdYkoP2PsVRs6GaCVyMRhOizSmvi6X\nOBVQKXGpSLII3GjZP7XG+V7GFkdZqH0LxcuiYl3lCgzn2RK7QUzTx3nMYxWfip+9\nNMYV24ySkJoB41OCRhsOMh1d+BL2En06NsiFTpVBmGdacHRx5BDJ1ptnpHpraU4O\nacqhsiML5XI2c4iXGaUvmkZb+yuIPbdnH2RT8ngxOIIxCXteTq5h4z//bH3aaiX9\nTQeotec/BVKhFhtV0q6cI6avoIh7a9HB3GMCvF7yAUgENm5aOQbly1tLlG65RIUe\ndZKPhfNTy2ZdrFvpbHFoVB3bgPvqwDTFeIhxuJHE7mNwN8TUl0LO/rYM+L5uZ87t\neG4m1k5h8wvLiIhHPLQbZ7D0ldh0tcDeycUgbnC3Io7o3BWAM1dMVAdBGqvkRm3W\naCVWxlo9OG+/8ICdcsqa4f+69s+1KLDBONOK5kasqcSYMguVJuMgiL8SVZKdN9P4\nboF1Ghicmtn+WH0a51Lq\n=KRI9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a5872897a5fb23ea9b31c25dc8f7343981d17753\nparent 2407bca66bac5d199a923a0e58872c813eb006bc\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781062079 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781062079 -0400\n\nchore(ci): validate Talon when `libs/talon/uv.lock` is directly changed (#3834)\n\n`_touches_talon()` excluded `libs/talon/uv.lock`, so a PR changing only\nthat lockfile skipped Talon's `uv lock --check`, allowing a\nstale/malformed lockfile to pass pre-commit. Now any `libs/talon` path\n(including `uv.lock`) counts as touching Talon, while unrelated changes\nstill skip Talon to preserve the optimization.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-10T03:27:59Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/619e55f49f1837e8e1760eb0ff7a84bb2c833551","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/619e55f49f1837e8e1760eb0ff7a84bb2c833551","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/619e55f49f1837e8e1760eb0ff7a84bb2c833551/comments","author":{"login":"md